3344.' }, { title = 'Reckoning line (starts at trial 1503)', note = '• Begins with a plain Reckoning; produces Reckoning +1/+2/+3 and Basanizo.\n• 1503: Reckoning → Reckoning (DMG +5, Nightmare Scythe damage +10%): use Nightmare Scythe 50 times; next 1504.\n• 1504: → Reckoning (DMG +10, Spinning Scythe damage +10%): use Spinning Scythe 100 times; next 1505.\n• 1505: → Reckoning (DMG +14, Vorpal Scythe damage +10%): use Vorpal Scythe 150 times on Vermin-type; next 1506 or 1507.\n• 1506: → Reckoning (DMG +21, Spiral Hell damage +10%): use Spiral Hell 250 times on Beast-type; next 2061.\n• 2061: → Reckoning +1 (Weapon skill damage +10%): kill 150 Plantoid-type; next 2464 or 2465.\n• 2464: → Reckoning +2 (DMG +7, Weapon skill damage +10%): kill 150 Bird-type; next 2897.\n• 2897: → Reckoning +3 (DMG +7, Weapon skill damage +10%): kill 150 Amorph-type; next 3360.\n• 3360: → Basanizo (DMG +8, Weapon skill damage +10%, Weapon skill damage +11%, Double Attack +6%): kill 150 Arcana-type; end.\n• TP Bonus branch: any of Slice, Dark Harvest, Shadow of Death, Nightmare Scythe, Spinning Scythe, Vorpal Scythe, Guillotine, Cross Reaper, Spiral Hell, Catastrophe, Insurgency, Infernal Scythe, Quietus, Entropy, Origin counts; each must deal 400+ damage.\n• 2465: Reckoning +1 (Weapon skill damage +10%) → Reckoning +2 (TP Bonus): 250 such weapon skills on Demon-type; next 2898.\n• 2898: → Reckoning +3 (TP Bonus): 250 on Lizard-type; next 3361.' } } },
    { name = 'Guide: Magian trials: Staff', group = 'Server', desc = 'Staff Magian trial chains on this server, with each trial\'s number, required weapon, objective, reward and follow-up trials. Source: https://vanadreams.org/wiki/#guide-c_magian_trials_staff', steps = { { title = 'Overview', note = '• Trials are started and rewarded by the Magian Moogle (orange, weapons) in Ru\'Lude Gardens; delivery items go in the Delivery Crate beside it.\n• Bring the exact weapon shown (with exactly those augments), accept the trial, complete the objective with it equipped, then return it to the Moogle for the upgrade.\n• Counts listed are this server\'s: half of standard.\n• Format below: trial: weapon in → weapon out: objective; next trials.\n• See the Magian trials guide for kill/delivery rules and bonus augments on finished weapons.' }, { title = 'Crook line (starts at trial 776)', note = '• Begins with a plain Crook; also produces Yantok, Yantok +1/+2/+3 and Urduja (later rows cut off in source).\n• Lines that reach an Empyrean weapon continue in Empyrean weapons: Magian trials.\n• 776: Crook → Shillelagh: kill Teporingo (Dangruf Wadi) x2; next 777.\n• 777: → Shillelagh (Attack +3): kill Valkurm Emperor (Valkurm Dunes) x2; next 778.\n• 778: → Shillelagh (Attack +5): kill Hyakume (Ranguemont Pass) x2; next 779 or 784.\n• 779: → Slaine: kill Gloomanita (North Gustaberg [S]) x2; next 780.\n• 780: → Slaine (Attack +3): kill Mischievous Micholas (Yuhtunga Jungle) x2; next 781.\n• 781: → Slaine (Attack +5): kill Cactuar Cantautor (Western Altepa Desert) x2; next 782.\n• 782: → Slaine (Attack +7): kill Erebus x3 (Beaucedine Glacier, Xarcabard, or either\'s [S]); next 783.\n• 783: → Slaine (DMG +13): kill Skuld x3 (Batallia Downs, Rolanberry Fields, Sauromugue Champaign, or any of their [S]); next 1646.\n• 1646: → Slaine (DMG +15): kill Chesma x4 (Konschtat Highlands, La Theine Plateau or Tahrongi Canyon); next 1647 or 1648.\n• 1647: → Hvergelmir: deliver 25 Kukulkan\'s Fang; continues at 2163 (Empyrean).\n• 1648: → Taiaha: deliver 8 Coin of Ruin; next 2164.\n• 2164: → Taiaha +1: deliver 8 Beastmen\'s Seal; next 2572.\n• 2572: → Taiaha +2: deliver 10 Kindred\'s Seal; next 3005.\n• 3005: → Taiaha +3: deliver 18 Devious Die; next 3468.\n• 3468: → Paikea (Magic Attack Bonus +31, Magic Accuracy +31, Magic burst damage +11%, Fast Cast +11%): deliver 18 Liminal Residue; end.\n• 784: Shillelagh (Attack +5) → Danda: kill 200 Beast-type; next 785.\n• 785: → Danda (Delay -9): kill 150 Chigoe family; next 786 or 787.\n• 786: → Danda (DMG +41, Delay +13, Occasionally attacks twice): deliver 5 Orcus Mandible; next 1649.' }, { title = 'Crook line (starts at trial 790)', note = '• Begins with a plain Crook; produces Teiwaz, Shareeravadi, Shareeravadi +1/+2/+3, Tuahjebat, and the elemental staves: Agni\'s Staff/+1/+2/+3 then Atar I-III; Vayu\'s Staff/+1/+2/+3 then Vayuvata I-III; Indra\'s Staff/+1/+2/+3 then Apamajas I-III; Surya\'s Staff/+1/+2/+3 then Arka I-IV; Varuna\'s Staff/+1/+2/+3 then Vourukasha I-III; Kubera\'s Staff/+1/+2/+3 then Vishrava I-III; Soma\'s Staff/+1/+2/+3 then Haoma I-III; Yama\'s Staff/+1/+2/+3 then Xsaeta I-III.\n• 790: Crook → Teiwaz: kill 25 Treant family (1 point each, 6 in any elemental weather); next 791 or 841.\n• 791: → Teiwaz (Fire, Wind, Thunder and Light resistance +5): kill 25 Spider family; only counts on Firesday/Windsday/Lightningday/Lightsday (1) or in Fire/Wind/Thunder/Light weather (5, or 6 if the day matches); next 792, 804, 816 or 828.\n• From 792 on, kills count only on Firesday (1) or in Fire weather (5, or 6 on Firesday).\n• 792: → Teiwaz (Fire resistance +10, Additional effect: Fire damage): kill 25 of any monster; next 793.\n• 793: → Teiwaz (STR +1, Additional effect: Fire damage): kill 38 Bird-type; next 794, 796, 798 or 802.\n• 794: → Teiwaz (DMG +14, Delay -10, STR +2, Attack +8): kill 50 Lizard-type; next 795.\n• 795: → Teiwaz (DMG +20, Delay -10, STR +4, Attack +15): kill 100 Wamoura family; next 1654.' }, { title = 'Sedikutchi line (starts at trial 1753)', note = '• Begins with a plain Sedikutchi; produces Sedikutchi +1/+2/+3 and Muruga.\n• 1753: Sedikutchi → Sedikutchi (DMG +7, Rock Crusher damage +10%): use Rock Crusher 50 times; next 1754.\n• 1754: → Sedikutchi (DMG +12, Shell Crusher damage +10%): use Shell Crusher 100 times; next 1755.\n• 1755: → Sedikutchi (DMG +16, Full Swing damage +10%): use Full Swing 150 times on Plantoid-type; next 1756 or 1757.\n• 1756: → Sedikutchi (DMG +21, Retribution damage +10%): use Retribution 250 times on Bird-type; next 2217.\n• 2217: → Sedikutchi +1 (Weapon skill damage +10%): kill 150 Vermin-type; next 2625 or 2626.\n• 2625: → Sedikutchi +2 (DMG +7, Weapon skill damage +10%): kill 150 Lizard-type; next 3058.\n• 3058: → Sedikutchi +3 (DMG +7, Weapon skill damage +10%): kill 150 Aquan-type; next 3521.\n• 3521: → Muruga (DMG +6, Weapon skill damage +10%, Magic Attack Bonus +31, Magic Accuracy +31): kill 150 Arcana-type; end.\n• TP Bonus branch: any of Heavy Swing, Rock Crusher, Earth Crusher, Starburst, Sunburst, Shell Crusher, Full Swing, Spirit Taker, Retribution, Gate of Tartarus, Vidohunir, Garland of Bliss, Omniscience, Cataclysm, Myrkr, Shattersoul, Oshala, Tartarus Torpor counts; each must deal 400+ damage.\n• 2626: Sedikutchi +1 (Weapon skill damage +10%) → Sedikutchi +2 (TP Bonus): 250 such weapon skills on Undead-type; next 3059.\n• 3059: → Sedikutchi +3 (TP Bonus): 250 on Plantoid-type; next 3522.' } } },
    { name = 'Guide: Magian trials: Sword', group = 'Server', desc = 'Sword Magian trial chains on this server, with each trial\'s number, required weapon, objective, reward and follow-up trials. Source: https://vanadreams.org/wiki/#guide-c_magian_trials_sword', steps = { { title = 'Overview', note = '• Trials are started and rewarded by the Magian Moogle (orange, weapons) in Ru\'Lude Gardens; delivery items go in the Delivery Crate beside it.\n• Bring the exact weapon shown (with exactly those augments), accept the trial, complete the objective with it equipped, then return it to the Moogle for the upgrade.\n• Counts listed are this server\'s: half of standard.\n• Format below: trial: weapon in → weapon out: objective; next trials.\n• See the Magian trials guide for kill/delivery rules and bonus augments on finished weapons.' }, { title = 'Side-sword line (starts at trial 150)', note = '• Begins with a plain Side-sword; also produces Khanda, Khanda +1/+2/+3 and Khadga (later rows cut off in source).\n• Lines that reach an Empyrean weapon continue in Empyrean weapons: Magian trials.\n• 150: Side-sword → Schiavona: kill Serpopard Ishtar (Tahrongi Canyon) x2; next 151.\n• 151: → Schiavona (Attack +3): kill Tottering Toby (Batallia Downs) x2; next 152.\n• 152: → Schiavona (Attack +5): kill Drooling Daisy (Rolanberry Fields) x2; next 153 or 158.\n• 153: → Nobilis: kill Gargantua (Beaucedine Glacier) x2; next 154.\n• 154: → Nobilis (Attack +3): kill Megalobugard (Lufaise Meadows) x2; next 155.\n• 155: → Nobilis (Attack +5): kill Ratatoskr (Fort Karugo - Narugo [S]) x2; next 156.\n• 156: → Nobilis (Attack +7): kill Jyeshtha x3 (Meriphataud Mountains, West Sarutabaruta, or either\'s [S]); next 157.\n• 157: → Nobilis (DMG +7): kill Capricornus x3 (East Ronfaure, Jugner Forest, or either\'s [S]); next 1200.\n• 1200: → Nobilis (DMG +8): kill Tammuz x4 (Konschtat Highlands, La Theine Plateau or Tahrongi Canyon); next 1201 or 1202.\n• 1201: → Almace: deliver 25 Helm of Briareus; continues at 1940 (Empyrean).\n• 1202: → Badelaire: deliver 8 Coin of Glory; next 1941.\n• 1941: → Badelaire +1: deliver 8 Beastmen\'s Seal; next 2340.\n• 2340: → Badelaire +2: deliver 10 Kindred\'s Seal; next 2773.\n• 2773: → Badelaire +3: deliver 18 Devious Die; next 3236.\n• 3236: → Brunello (Weapon skill damage +11%, Double Attack +6%, Store TP +9, Critical hit rate +6%): deliver 18 Liminal Residue; end.\n• 158: Schiavona (Attack +5) → Antea: kill 200 Bird-type; next 159.\n• 159: → Antea (Delay -6): kill 150 Cluster monsters; next 160 or 161.\n• 160: → Antea (DMG +17, Delay +36, Occasionally attacks twice): deliver 5 Ruthven\'s Nail; next 1203.' }, { title = 'Side-sword line (starts at trial 164)', note = '• Begins with a plain Side-sword; produces Soulsaber, Shamshir, Shamshir +1/+2/+3 and Shikargar.\n• 164: Side-sword → Soulsaber: kill 25 Leech family (1 point each, 6 in any elemental weather); next 165 or 190.\n• 165: → Soulsaber (Fire, Wind, Thunder and Light resistance +5): kill 25 Sea Monk family; only counts on Firesday/Windsday/Lightningday/Lightsday (1) or in Fire/Wind/Thunder/Light weather (5, or 6 if the day matches); next 166, 172, 178 or 184.\n• From 166 to 1945, progress counts only on Firesday (1) or in Fire weather (5, or 6 on Firesday).\n• 166: → Soulsaber (Fire resistance +10, Additional effect: Fire damage): kill 25 of any monster; next 167.\n• 167: → Soulsaber (STR +1, Additional effect: Fire damage): trigger the weapon\'s additional effect 38 times on Aquan-type; next 168 or 170.\n• 168: → Soulsaber (DMG +7, Delay -10, STR +2, Attack +5): kill 50 Beast-type; next 169.\n• 169: → Soulsaber (DMG +12, Delay -10, STR +4, Attack +12): kill 100 Flan family; next 1208.\n• 1208: → Soulsaber (DMG +14, Delay -10, STR +4, Attack +12): kill 100 Vermin-type; next 1209.\n• 1209: → Shamshir (STR +6, Attack +16): kill 125 Manticore family; next 1945.\n• 1945: → Shamshir +1 (STR +8, Attack +18): kill 150 Bird-type; next 2344.\n• 2344: → Shamshir +2 (STR +9, Attack +20): deliver 8 Flame Geode; next 2777.\n• 2777: → Shamshir +3 (STR +10, Attack +20): deliver 20 Flame Geode; next 3240.' }, { title = 'Machaera line (starts at trial 1241)', note = '• Begins with a plain Machaera; produces Machaera +1/+2/+3 and Thibron.\n• 1241: Machaera → Machaera (DMG +4, Burning Blade damage +10%): use Burning Blade 50 times; next 1242.\n• 1242: → Machaera (DMG +7, Shining Blade damage +10%): use Shining Blade 100 times; next 1243.\n• 1243: → Machaera (DMG +9, Circle Blade damage +10%): use Circle Blade 150 times on Bird-type; next 1244.\n• 1244: → Machaera (DMG +13, Savage Blade damage +10%): use Savage Blade 250 times on Beast-type; next 1961.\n• 1961: → Machaera +1 (Weapon skill damage +10%): kill 150 Plantoid-type; next 2360 or 2361.\n• 2360: → Machaera +2 (DMG +2, Weapon skill damage +10%): kill 150 Lizard-type; next 2793.\n• 2793: → Machaera +3 (DMG +2, Weapon skill damage +10%): kill 150 Undead-type; next 3256.\n• 3256: → Thibron (DMG +3, Weapon skill damage +10%, Weapon skill damage +11%, Double Attack +6%): kill 150 Demon-type; end.\n• Sword weapon skills that count (here and in the 1245 line): Fast Blade, Burning Blade, Red Lotus Blade, Flat Blade, Shining Blade, Seraph Blade, Circle Blade, Spirits Within, Vorpal Blade, Swift Blade, Savage Blade, Sanguine Blade, Knights of Round, Death Blossom, Atonement, Expiacion, Chant du Cygne, Requiescat, Knights of Rotund, Final Paradise, Fast Blade II, Imperator, Uriel Blade, Glory Slash.\n• 2361: Machaera +1 (Weapon skill damage +10%) → Machaera +2 (TP Bonus): 250 such weapon skills dealing 400+ damage on Demon-type; next 2794.\n• 2794: → Machaera +3 (TP Bonus): same on Bird-type; next 3257.' }, { title = 'Machaera line (starts at trial 1245)', note = '• Begins with a plain Machaera; produces Machaera +1/+2/+3 and Thibron. Each trial needs 400 uses of any sword weapon skill listed in the 1241 line.\n• 1245: Machaera → Machaera (DMG +11, Store TP +9): on Arcana-type; next 1962.\n• 1962: → Machaera +1 (Store TP +14): on Mandragora family; next 2362.\n• 2362: → Machaera +2 (DMG +2, Store TP +17): on Magic Pot family; next 2795.\n• 2795: → Machaera +3 (DMG +2, Store TP +17): on Skeleton family; next 3258.' } } },
    { name = 'Guide: Magicked Skull in Valkurm Dunes', group = 'Server', desc = 'Ghouls in Valkurm Dunes drop the Magicked Skull, needed for Elder Memories, The Road to Aht Urhgan and Dormant Powers Dislodged, and for Records of Eminence. Source: https://vanadreams.org/wiki/#guide-c_valkurm_ghouls_magicked_skull', steps = { { title = 'Where to find a Ghoul', note = '• Four black-mage Ghouls are always up, day or night.\n• West beach near Selbina, among the Beach Pugils.\n• Middle of the south shore, among Snippers and Beach Pugils.\n• South-east shore by the Hippomaritimus.\n• Just north-east of the conquest outpost (Quanteilleron, R.K.).\n• 20:00-04:00: Goblins killed at Goblin camps may be replaced by a Ghoul; these vanish at 04:00.' }, { title = 'Tips', note = '• Ghouls: level 18-22, aggressive, sound aggro.\n• Skull is a common drop; Rare/Ex, so only one can be held.' } } },
    { name = 'Guide: Merit abilities on your support job', group = 'Server', desc = 'Support jobs level with the main job on Vanadreams, so from level 75 merit job abilities bought for the support job are usable (e.g. No Foot Rise as /DNC, Warrior\'s Charge as /WAR). Source: https://vanadreams.org/wiki/#guide-c_subjob_merit_abilities', steps = { { title = 'How it works', note = '• Ability strength matches the merits spent on it.\n• No Foot Rise as /DNC: one Finishing Move per merit level, max 5 Finishing Moves.\n• Merit the ability on that job (Merit Points menu, job group 2), then set the job as support.' } } },
    { name = 'Guide: MiniFerrin\'s small talk', group = 'Server', desc = 'MiniFerrin is an AI in the VanaNews linkshell who replies when named (MiniFerrin, MiniF, mf) or sent a /tell, and greets players unprompted in a few cases. Source: https://vanadreams.org/wiki/#guide-c_miniferrin_small_talk', steps = { { title = 'Unprompted replies', note = '• Morning greetings ("good morning", "gm") get a reply.\n• Goodnights ("gn all", "off to bed") get a reply.\n• Announcing a big fight (Shadow Lord, Promathia, Kamlanaut, Ark Angels, Maat, Kirin, Dynamis, Limbus, etc.) gets encouragement naming the foe.\n• Limits: each kind once in a while per player, and one such line per 20 seconds for the whole shell; questions don\'t trigger these.' }, { title = 'Asking him things', note = '• He checks the wiki (including player notes), NPC locations/roles and server game data before answering; page links point to this wiki.\n• Ask where to level for your level and he names camps.\n• Understands FFXI slang (e.g. Sheol Gaol V0-V25).\n• Write in Japanese for a Japanese reply; also answers to ミニフェリン.\n• Cannot act in game (no items, gil, moves or fixes); use !report for bugs and !posfix if stuck.' } } },
    { name = 'Guide: Moblin Maze Mongers', group = 'Server', desc = 'Order a party maze from the Lower Jeuno Moblins, configure it with a tabula, voucher and runes, clear it, and earn Moblin Marbles, EXP and loot. Source: https://vanadreams.org/wiki/#guide-c_moblin_maze_mongers', steps = { { title = 'Getting started', note = '• Talk to Goldagrik, Muckvix\'s Junkshop, Lower Jeuno (H-9) to get the Tattered Maze Monger Pouch (key item), Maze Tabula M01, Maze Voucher 01 and two starter runes.\n• Use each voucher/rune from inventory once to stow it in the pouch; it is then reusable on any tabula.\n• Every maze entrant needs their own pouch.' }, { title = 'The Moblins', note = '• Goldagrik (H-9): sign-up.\n• Maze Mongers Shopfront (G-11, by the chocobo stables): arrange tabula, order maze, join leader\'s maze.\n• Chatnachoq (H-9): marble exchange.\n• Duplidoc (H-9): tabula copies.' }, { title = 'Setting up a tabula', note = '• At the Shopfront choose Arrange a tabula; the board prints to chat.\n• Symbols: # black square, . open square, f i w e t a l d elemental squares, A-L runes; capital = rune on its own element, enhanced (~1.5x).\n• Set exactly one voucher (chooses the maze).\n• Set up to 12 runes; each auto-places at the first fit, preferring matching element squares. Remove runes and reorder if one won\'t fit.\n• M01 is the beginner board; M02 and M03 use other layouts.' }, { title = 'Ordering a maze', note = '• Gather 1-6 players with pouches near the Shopfront.\n• Choose Place a maze order (or trade the tabula) and pay the voucher\'s gil fee; an M tabula is consumed, so copy it at Duplidoc first if needed.\n• Members within ~50 yalms enter; others use Join my party leader\'s maze while it runs.\n• One order per 20 hours.\n• Monster level follows the lowest member (Vouchers 01-03, 08), highest member (04, 06, 07, 09) or leader (05).' }, { title = 'The vouchers', note = '• Format: voucher | goal | fee (gil) | base marbles.\n• 01 | clear all monsters in Everbloom Hollow | 100 | 8\n• 02 | beat four waves, Ruhotz Silvermines | 100 | 9\n• 03 | clear five floors of Ghoyu\'s Reverie | 100 | 8\n• 04 | collect materials from kills, synthesize at the Fabricant Idol | 150 | 25\n• 05 | keep goblin Chaperix alive through three waves | 250 | 25\n• 06 | open four lockboxes; none open while in combat; guards call extra foes | 100 | 40\n• 07 | defeat a strong foe and two retainers | 200 | 10\n• 08 | cull aquans in Everbloom Hollow | 100 | 10\n• 09 | wake each Moblin Idol, then beat its two guardians | 300 | 10\n• Time limit 30 minutes (warnings 15/10/5/3/2/1 min); fails on timeout or full party down for three minutes.\n• Flaraflic at the start: How are we doing? for progress, Take the whole party out to exit.' }, { title = 'Runes', note = '• Most runes alter the marble payout.\n• 001-012 lures pick monster families (aquan, amorph, bird, beast, lizard, vermin, plantoid, undead, arcana, demon, dragon, elemental); none set = mixed.\n• 013-020: Great/Tiny Warrior (more/less HP), Motion (foes chase) / Stillness (foes wait), Supreme Might, Might, Weakness, Peon (level up/down); stronger = more marbles, Weakness/Peon = fewer.\n• 021-028 elements; add Altered Aggression (039) for en-spells or Altered Defense (040) for spikes.\n• 029-081 stat/skill/job/combat runes (STR-CHR, Hardiness, Mysticism, Conspicuous Behavior, magic schools, jobs, Onslaught, Protection, Accuracy, Evasion, Critical, Rapid Strike, Fleetfoot); +1 marble each.\n• 082-093 gathering/craft runes add ore, logs, crops, fish or craft materials to the Hoardbox.\n• Trials 094-104: Lost and Found = more and rarer loot, fewer marbles.\n• Swift/Superior Synthesis: Voucher 04 only.\n• Insurance Contract: no EXP.\n• Trial by Velocity: extra marbles for a quick clear.\n• Trial by Budget: 25-minute limit instead of 30.\n• Trial by Numbers: more monsters.\n• Amnesiac\'s Trial / Trial by Silence: party is amnesic / silenced all maze long; both pay a large marble bonus.\n• Contracts 106-116: Guidance = Flaraflic indicates the closest foe.\n• Reinforcement: six idols in Voucher 09.\n• Conditioning: more EXP.\n• Sustenance: Packapic sells temporary items for marbles at the start.\n• Camaraderie: a Moblin mercenary joins the fight.\n• Goldagrik\'s Generosity: extra foes in Voucher 04.\n• Obscured Entrance: start point is random.\n• Shortcut: Voucher 03 has four floors.\n• Walloper/Barrager/Spellslinger: give Chaperix a job in Voucher 05.\n• 118-119 Skillchain and Magic Burst: boost party skillchain and magic burst damage.' }, { title = 'Rewards', note = '• A Hoardbox appears on completion; each player opens it once.\n• Marbles = voucher base adjusted by runes; EXP unless Insurance Contract; rune materials; occasional Moblin gear or unbuyable runes (more with Lost and Found).\n• After three minutes, remaining players are auto-paid and returned to the Shopfront.' }, { title = 'Chatnachoq\'s exchange', note = '• Tabulae: M01 1 marble, M02/M03 100.\n• Vouchers: 01 1, others 100.\n• Runes: 100-500 tiers; unlisted runes only from Hoardboxes.\n• Gear: Eyepatch 10, Noble Poulaines 100, Caver\'s Shovel 200, Spelunker\'s Hat 300, Club Hammer 400.\n• Titles Maze Wanderer/Navigator/Scholar/Artisan/Overlord need 10/50/100/500/1000 clears and cost 10/100/500/1000/5000 marbles; re-wearing an earned title costs 1.' }, { title = 'Duplidoc\'s copies', note = '• Trade an M tabula with a voucher set plus 500 gil and 5 marbles for an uneditable R tabula copy valid for 5 orders; the M tabula is returned.\n• One copy per Vana\'diel day.' }, { title = 'Tips', note = '• Begin with Voucher 01 on M01 plus one or two lure runes.\n• Place element runes on matching squares for enhanced payouts.\n• Trials and stacked monster-strengthening runes pay the most.' } } },
    { name = 'Guide: Modern look', group = 'Server', desc = 'Vanadreams includes HD textures and a ReShade-style colour pass with presets toggled in game. Source: https://vanadreams.org/wiki/#guide-c_modern_look', steps = { { title = 'HD content', note = '• HD faces for all races, HD player bodies and armour.\n• HD towns: San d\'Oria, Bastok, Windurst, Jeuno, Selbina, Mhaura, Aht Urhgan Whitegate, Western and Eastern Adoulin.\n• HD Adoulin fields: Rala Waterways, Yahse Hunting Grounds, Ceizak Battlegrounds, Foret de Hennetiel, Yorcia Weald, Morimar Basalt Fields.\n• HD starter fields: Ronfaure, Gustaberg, Sarutabaruta, La Theine, Valkurm.' }, { title = 'Colour pass', note = '• Home opens the preset menu; Scroll Lock toggles effects.\n• Vanadreams-Standard (default): soft bloom, colour grade, sharpening.\n• Vanadreams-Ultra: stronger bloom, light vignette.\n• Vanadreams-Look: colour grade only.\n• Game runs at 60 fps with world drawn at 2048.' }, { title = 'Other mods and older PCs', note = '• HD texture packs (e.g. Ashenbubs\') can coexist; updates overwrite shipped files.\n• Another ReShade or d3d8/d3d9 wrapper (dgVoodoo, dx8to9) in the same folder conflicts and may black-screen; remove it or disable the built-in pass.\n• To disable the colour pass: in the bootloader folder beside xiloader.exe, rename d3d8.dll and d3d9.dll with .off; HD textures remain.' } } },
    { name = 'Guide: Mog Bonanza (weekly)', group = 'Server', desc = 'A weekly lottery: buy a numbered Bonanza Pearl, wait for Saturday\'s draw, then trade a winning pearl for a prize from that week\'s list. Source: https://vanadreams.org/wiki/#guide-c_mog_bonanza', steps = { { title = 'Where', note = '• Port San d\'Oria, Port Bastok, Port Windurst, Chocobo Circuit: two Bonanza Moogles plus a Pearl Moogle.\n• Rolanberry Fields bazaar hangout (!hangout): Bonanza Pearls (sells), Bonanza Prizes (pays out) and the Prize Chest.' }, { title = 'Buying', note = '• Pearl Moogle / Bonanza Pearls, Monday 00:00 to Saturday 18:00 server time.\n• Pick three digits or random; 200,000 gil; one per character per week.\n• View prizes via "This week\'s prizes" or the Prize Chest, then First/Second/Third; lists rotate weekly.' }, { title = 'Prize tiers', note = '• First: all three digits; level 76-99 NM gear.\n• Second: last two digits; level 1-75 NM gear and abjurations.\n• Third: last digit; progress items (seals, testimonies, coffer keys, pop items).' }, { title = 'Draw and claiming', note = '• Draw every Saturday 18:00 server time; winners receive a Mog Bonanza Marble by delivery box.\n• Trade the pearl to a port Bonanza Moogle, or trade/talk to Bonanza Prizes at the hangout, before the next Saturday draw.\n• Claim last week\'s winner before buying a new pearl.\n• Losing pearls give a Bonanza Biscuit.' } } },
    { name = 'Guide: Mog Locker for everyone', group = 'Server', desc = 'All characters get a free 80-slot Mog Locker with no lease, time limit, Treasures of Aht Urhgan progress or Imperial Bronze Pieces required. Source: https://vanadreams.org/wiki/#guide-c_mog_locker', steps = { { title = 'Access', note = '• Open it in your Mog House or any town with a Nomad Moogle.\n• Created automatically at login; transferred characters keep existing locker contents.' } } },
    { name = 'Guide: Monisette: reforging artifact, relic and empyrean armor', group = 'Server', desc = 'Monisette in Port Jeuno (I-8) reforges artifact, relic and empyrean armor to item level 109, after which Oseem in Norg handles further grades. Source: https://vanadreams.org/wiki/#guide-c_monisette_reforge', steps = { { title = 'How', note = '• Trade her one armor piece with materials in main inventory (not satchel or wardrobes); she quotes the cost and asks for confirmation.\n• Rem\'s Tale chapter by slot: head Ch.1, body Ch.2, hands Ch.3, legs Ch.4, feet Ch.5.' }, { title = 'Materials', note = '• Artifact: Rem\'s Tale x10 + job ingredient + slot ingredient.\n• Artifact +1: Rem\'s Tale x5.\n• Relic: Rem\'s Tale x10 + Lungo-Nango Jadeshell x2.\n• Relic +1: Rem\'s Tale x10 + Lungo-Nango Jadeshell x1.\n• Relic +2: Rem\'s Tale x10 + job ingredient + slot ingredient.\n• Empyrean +1: Rem\'s Tale x10.\n• Empyrean +2: Rem\'s Tale x5 + job ingredient + slot ingredient.\n• Slot ingredients: Phoenix Feather (head), Malboro Fiber (body), Beetle Blood (hands), Damascene Cloth (legs), Oxblood (feet).' }, { title = 'Restrictions', note = '• Plain empyrean not accepted; upgrade to +1 first.\n• Geomancer and Rune Fencer relic and empyrean armor are not reforged here.' } } },
