78, River Murex 77-78, Blademaw Pugil / Slough Bats / Spitting Spider 79-81; Aestutaur, Clammy Imp, Coccinelle, Devegetator 81-95; Jasconius, Russet Rarab, Slaughterous Smilodon, Speltercap, Wily Opo-opo 79-83; Gruesome Gargouille, Helter-skelter, Peapuk, Pneumaflayer, Shewriwhile 80-84' }, { title = 'Adoulin', note = '• Ceizak Battlegrounds: Careening Twitherym, Fernfelling Chapuli, Twigtrip Lapinion, Blanched Mandragora, Longclaw Raptor, Fluffy Sheep 100-101; Colossal Spider 99-107, Belaboring Wasp 100-101, Downy Emerald 99-107, Resplendent Luckybug 99-107, Undergrowth Hornet 100-101, Bight Uragnite 100-101, Deathmaw Orobon / Knobby Treant 100-102\n• Yahse Hunting Grounds: Calfcleaving Chapuli, Twitherym Infestation, Nettled Wasp, Luckybug Hoarder, Pinetorum, Broad Scarlet, Fiery Wasp, Monstrosiraptor, Ulbukan Sheep 100-101; Bight Uragnite, Edacious Orobon, Velkk Marauder, Verdant Treant 100-103; also Frondescent Leafkin, Shy Heartwing, Wooded Ungeweder\n• Foret de Hennetiel: Scummy Slug 102-104, Riverwashed Toad 102-110, Skinsipper Chigoe 102-104, Vampire Leech 102-103, Perfidious Crab 102-110, Vorst Gnat / Zoldeff Jagil 102-110, Careening Twitherym 101-103; Primordial Orobon, Shrouded Obdella, Bellicose Tarichuk, Glutinous Clot, Hoary Craklaw, Velkk Sage 101-110\n• Morimar Basalt Fields: Tephra Lizard, Frosty Twitherym, Animosiraptor, Mountain Peiste, Felsic Eruca, Maca Maca, Sinewy Matamata, Acerbic Jagil, Tundra Eft 102-105; Anthousai, Befuddled Twitherym, Lavawalker Raptor, Petrous Lizard 105-110; Mafic Spider, Qohanyk, Snowcap Umbril, Volcanic Wivre, Emberflash Matamata 107-109; Hoarfrost Gefyrst\n• Yorcia Weald (all 107-109 except Swollen Chigoe 115-117): Snapweed, Saptrap, Shade-speckled Spider, Twitherym, Cheeky Opo-opo, Droughted Treant, Grove Wasp, Leaflick Lapinion, Nascent Sapling, Bronzecap, Corpse Flower, Loyal Snapweed, Luckybug, Tight-lipped Flytrap, Shadowscourge Umbril, Irksome Leafkin, Abashed Heartwing\n• Marjami Ravine (all 106-109): Stryx, Lapiniontrap, Whispering Twitherym, Cliffclinger Toad, Tulfaire, Velkk Defiler, Velkk Jaguar, Canyon Apkallu, Lapinion, Longface Colibri, Velkk Inquisitor, Velkk Shadowmancer, Vinelash Vulture\n• Kamihr Drifts (all 111-113): Cicatricose Raaz, Snowpelt Rabbit, Bedraggled Lucerewe, Shaggy Ovim, Ashen Tiger, Cyanotic Raptor, Hailstone, Wailing Umbril, Slobbering Ruszor, Gnarring Yztarg, Sprightly Leafkin\n• Cirdas Caverns: Pallid Funguar, Tenebrous Obdella, Flatus Acuex, Crepuscular Worm, Foreboding Funguar, Fuliginous Mandragora, Subterrane Spider, Asperous Marolith, Tunnel Lizard, Grossular Bat, Balas Bats, Igneous Clot, Invidious Lizard 102-106; Moist Funguar, Putrid Acuex 104-109; Drearyeyed Bat, Snippy Rafflesia 125-126; Imposing Dullahan 127' }, { title = 'Escha / Reisenjima / other', note = '• Escha - Zi\'Tah: Eschan Opo-opo / Tarichuk / Puk / Bugard 107-110; Eschan Wasp / Snapweed 80-89; Eschan Warrior / Vulture / Sorcerer 70-79; Eschan Weapon / Coeurl 60-69; Eschan Crawler / Obdella / Worm 50-59\n• Escha - Ru\'Aun: Eschan Ilaern 115-119, Eschan Phuabo 112-115; Eschan Amoeban, Clionid, Limule, Murex, Eschan Ghrah 115-119\n• Reisenjima (121-126 unless noted): Lentic Toad, Indomitable Faaz, Devouring Mosquito, Obstreperous Panopt, Territorial Mantis, Porxie, Officious Unseelie, Agitated Chapuli, Lucani, Glowering Ladybug, Quarrelsome Hippogryph, Jeering Pixie, Perfervid Naraka, Snaggletoothed Tiger, Wanton Danaid, Macabre Skeleton, Rampaging Beetle, Thunder Elemental, Arboreal Chigoe, Asphyxiating Cyhiraeth, Wretched Poroggo, Water Elemental\n• Apollyon (all 150): Apollyon Demon, Antlion, Doomed, Skeleton, Adamantoise, Bugard, Crawler, Diremite, Eft, Hecteyes, Ladybug, Leech, Raptor, Wasp, Wight' } } },
    { name = 'Guide: New Adventurer Starter Gifts (Adventurer Coupon and Echad Ring)', group = 'Server', desc = 'New characters receive an Adventurer Coupon and can earn the Echad Ring, matching retail. Source: https://vanadreams.org/wiki/#guide-c_new_adventurer_tutorial', steps = { { title = 'Adventurer Coupon (50 gil)', note = '• Granted automatically in your nation\'s opening cutscene; keep an inventory slot free or it is lost.\n• Trade it to an Adventurer\'s Assistant for 50 gil.\n• San d\'Oria: Ailevia (Southern San d\'Oria), Matildie (Northern San d\'Oria), Teilsa (Port San d\'Oria).\n• Bastok: Reet (Bastok Markets), Arva (Bastok Mines), Dulsie (Port Bastok).\n• Windurst: Jack of Hearts (Windurst Waters), Jack of Diamonds (Windurst Walls), Jack of Clubs (Port Windurst), Jack of Spades (Windurst Woods).' }, { title = 'Echad Ring (the EXP ring)', note = '• Earned by finishing the beginner tutorial; report to the guide after each task.\n• Guides: Alaune (Southern San d\'Oria), Gulldago (Bastok Markets), Selele (Windurst Woods).\n• Obtain Signet from a gate guard: Meat Jerky x6.\n• Eat any food.\n• Raise a weapon skill slightly.\n• Activate Records of Eminence (Memorandoll): 100 gil, then a crystal and crafting materials.\n• Check the Auction House: Conquest promotion voucher.\n• Reach level 5: Raising Earring.\n• Obtain your nation\'s Trust permit: Warp Ring.\n• Check the Survival Guide in town and at an outpost: Saltena x12.\n• Reach level 18: Copper A.M.A.N. Voucher.\n• Set a support job: Echad Ring plus 12 Free Chocopasses.\n• Echad Ring (Rare/Ex): equip and use for +150% EXP, ending after 30,000 EXP or 12 hours.\n• For slower leveling, see the Classic EXP band (Castor\'s Ring) page.' } } },
    { name = 'Guide: New player guide', group = 'Server', desc = 'Setup and first-steps summary for Vanadreams, a non-profit custom FFXI fan server, plus its main differences from retail. Source: https://vanadreams.org/wiki/#guide-c_new_player_guide', steps = { { title = '1. Get the launcher', note = '• Download the Vanadreams Launcher from the site\'s front page; keep the file if the browser asks.\n• The launcher is signed; if Windows warns on first run, pick More info, then Run anyway.\n• No install needed and it self-updates.\n• Requires Windows 10 or 11; no PlayOnline or Square Enix account needed.' }, { title = '2. Install the game', note = '• Press Setup and choose a folder for the loader and runtime.\n• Press Install game to download the server-matched client; interrupted downloads resume and Windows asks once at the end to register it.\n• An existing FFXI install can be used instead.\n• Press Play.\n• Only three Vanadreams addons start enabled: music player, merit-window fix, Auction House search button; enable others on the Addons page and press Save.' }, { title = '3. Make your character', note = '• On first Play the loader asks you to create an account (name and password), then create a character as usual.\n• After the opening scene, answer yes to "Customize your look further?" to open the Stylist Moogle menu (free, unlimited; also available later).\n• Keep a free slot for the Adventurer Coupon from the nation cutscene.\n• Every character starts with a VanaNews linkshell pearl.' }, { title = '4. First steps', note = '• Do your nation\'s beginner tutorial to earn the Echad Ring.\n• Get your nation\'s Trust permit and summon your first Alter Egos.\n• Type !hangout to go to the Rolanberry bazaar hangout.' }, { title = '5. Echad Ring tutorial', note = '• Talk twice to your guide to start, then return after each step: Alaune, Southern San d\'Oria (G-10); Gulldago, Bastok Markets (D-11); Selele, Windurst Woods (K-10).\n• Get Signet from a gate guard (Meat Jerky x6).\n• Eat some food.\n• Learn a weapon skill by raising a weapon skill a bit (100 gil).\n• Activate Records of Eminence for the memorandoll (nation-specific starter items and a crystal).\n• Use an Auction House counter (Conquest promotion voucher).\n• Reach level 5 (Raising Earring).\n• Get your nation\'s Trust permit (Warp Ring).\n• Check two Survival Guides (Saltena x12): Bastok Mines then North Gustaberg; Northern San d\'Oria then West Ronfaure; Port Windurst then West Sarutabaruta.\n• Reach level 18 (Copper A.M.A.N. Voucher).\n• Set a support job (Echad Ring and 12 Chocopasses).\n• Echad Ring gives +150% EXP until 30,000 EXP earned or 12 hours pass.\n• Keep a free slot for each reward.' }, { title = '6. Server differences', note = '• EXP, Records of Eminence, TP and drop rates are standard; capacity points are 10x.\n• Roughly half of monsters drop a Treasure Casket.\n• Regular monsters: +15% HP, +20% stats; notorious monsters: +10% to each.\n• Classic mode (level held at 75 until that era\'s content is done): talk to MiniFerrin outside your Mog House before any job exceeds level 30.\n• Your main job may equip gear your support job can wear (e.g. BLM/WAR can use a great axe), via vanagear sets.\n• vanagear: enable it on the launcher Addons page, then use /vg in game; /vg help lists job-relevant commands.\n• All 122 Trusts are available; begin with your capital\'s Trust quest.\n• Bank of Vana\'diel: the Bank Clerk at the hangout lends gil, repaid automatically from Auction House sales.\n• All Auction Houses share one market, stocked by a trading bot that also buys sold items; the DreamyAH addon adds a search window.\n• Daily login earns points spent at a Greeter Moogle or the Login Moogle; the Login Moogle also takes Beastmen\'s and Kindred\'s Seals at 10 points each.\n• The Stylist Moogle at the hangout changes face and hair colour for free.' }, { title = 'The hangout: !hangout', note = '• Reach it with !hangout or by leaving Lower Jeuno into Rolanberry Fields; you start at the north end of the bazaar street.\n• Heading south: Auction Moogle (Auction House, Mog House menu), Login Moogle, Survival Guide and Home Point crystal, Mog Bonanza plaza, Stylist Moogle and MiniFerrin (Classic mode), Bank Clerk, Montblanc and the Clan Provisioner (Clan Centurio), Training Moogle (spawns a practice crab), bazaar shopkeepers.' }, { title = '7. MiniFerrin and VanaNews', note = '• VanaNews linkshell chat is mirrored to the VanaNews thread on the Vanadreams Discord within seconds; Discord messages do not go into the game.\n• MiniFerrin is an AI in VanaNews; address him as MiniFerrin, MiniF or mf, or /tell him; he answers game and server questions, including in Japanese.\n• In the world he is an automaton and runs the Classic mode desk.' }, { title = '8. Troubleshooting', note = '• On a disconnect or frozen screen, close the game and log back in.\n• Ask for help in VanaNews or on the Vanadreams Discord; report bugs on Discord with what you were doing and where.\n• Windower users: the launcher\'s Addons page lists Ashita equivalents of Windower addons.' } } },
    { name = 'Guide: Notorious monsters that now appear', group = 'Server', desc = 'Four NMs that previously could not spawn on the server are now fixed. Source: https://vanadreams.org/wiki/#guide-c_nm_fixes_2026_10', steps = { { title = 'Fixed NMs', note = '• Coordinates are in-game x, y, z.\n• Eyegouger (Batallia Downs, Lv 46): kill the nearby roaming Ba, which may instead pop Tottering Toby; around 177, -2, -55.\n• Bugbear Strongman x2 (Oldton Movalpolos, Lv 50): kill the guarding Bugbear Bondmen; around -1, 11.5, -98 and 62, 15.5, -122.\n• Shieldtrap (Riverne - Site #A01, Lv 39-44): trade a Shield Bug to the ??? at 162, 1, 466.\n• Hemodrosophila (Meriphataud Mountains [S], Lv 80-83): kill the two Gnats flying next to its spawn; around -247, -8.4, 136.' } } },
    { name = 'Guide: Nyzul Isle NMs', group = 'Server', desc = 'Lists the notorious monsters found on Nyzul Isle floors, their notable abilities and their drops or appraisal results. Source: https://vanadreams.org/wiki/#guide-c_nyzul_survey_nms', steps = { { title = 'Nyzul Isle Investigation: boss floors', note = '• Bosses are the enemy leader on floors 20, 40, 60, 80 and 100; the Archaic Rampart on those floors is optional.\n• Floors 20/40: Adamantoise, Behemoth or Fafnir. Floors 60/80/100: Khimaira, Hydra or Cerberus.\n• Adamantoise plays like the Valley of Sorrows HNM: huge defence, low HP, draws in attackers who are out of range.\n• Adamantoise: strong Earth/Water resistance; immune to Slow, Stun, Poison and Sleep; Bind and Gravity land. Use elemental magic.\n• Floor 20/40 bosses always drop one random Nyzul weapon, plus a chance at boss armour: feet on 20 (Askar Gambieras, Denali Gamashes, Goliard Clogs), legs on 40 (Askar Dirs, Denali Kecks, Goliard Trews).\n• No title is awarded for this Adamantoise kill.' }, { title = 'Nyzul Isle Uncharted Area Survey: floor NMs', note = '• The Survey uses its own NM lists per floor range, separate from the Investigation; they roam, and an "Eliminate the enemy leader" floor\'s leader is one of them. Survey monsters are high level.\n• Each kill yields one Alexandrite (never a Nyzul weapon) and an Armoury Crate holding that NM\'s unappraised ??? item.\n• Appraising gives a small chance of the Appraisal item listed (e.g. Gwyllgi\'s ??? Sash → Gosha Sarashi), otherwise a basic item (e.g. Leather Belt). Vanadreams uses a 5% rate.' }, { title = 'Floors 1-19', note = '• Format: NM (family) → appraisal.\n• Amanita (funguar) → Tenax Strap; Tococo (bird) → Armiger\'s Lace; Duke Decapod (crab) → Pelte; Rambukk (ram) → Bukktooth.\n• Numbing Norman (bee) → Pike; Yara Ma Yha Who (sapling) → Fasting Ring; Barbastelle (bat) → Felling Axe; Doppelganger Gog (shadow) → Cruel Spear.\n• Nocuous Weapon (evil weapon) → Disciple Grip; Ghillie Dhu (sapling) → Estramacon; Slumbering Samwell (sheep) → Samwell\'s Shank; Habrok (bird) → Besieger Mantle.\n• Teporingo (rabbit) → Succubus Grip; Desmodont (bat) → Fidelity Mantle; Maltha (slime) → Trailer\'s Tunica; Wake Warder Wanda (crab) → Melampus Staff.\n• Chocoboleech (leech) → Gassan; Doppelganger Dio (shadow) → Cruel Scythe.' }, { title = 'Floors 21-39', note = '• Gwyllgi (hound) → Gosha Sarashi: frequent Poison Breath and Methane Breath.\n• Yal-un Eke (cluster) → Beacon Cuffs: only move is Sling Bomb; Regain makes it chain them at low HP.\n• Hercules Beetle (beetle) → Black Hose; Skewer Sam (cockatrice) → Wind Spear; Edacious Opo-opo (opo-opo) → Nanban Kariginu; Hippomaritimus (pugil) → Channeling Robe.\n• Kirata (tiger) → Boreas Cesti; Mucoid Mass (slime) → Spellcaster\'s Ecu; Sekhmet (coeurl) → Layqa Seraweels; Patripatan (coeurl) → Nous Arbalest.\n• Mycophile (funguar) → Mycophile Cuffs; Koropokkur (mandragora) → Aega\'s Doublet; Serra (pugil) → Volans Greaves; Noble Mold (funguar) → Rain Hat.\n• Megalobugard (bugard) → Hercules\' Ring; Waraxe Beak (cockatrice) → Monsoon Tekko; Herbage Hunter (crawler) → Precision Bandana; Dosetsu Tree (treant) → Raikiri.' }, { title = 'Floors 41-59', note = '• Hazmat (bomb) → Promptitude Solea: no TP moves; casts only Flare, ~3x normal speed, ~1000 damage; shadows help; immune to Silence, Sleep, Bind, Gravity.\n• Okyupete (roc) → Shepherd\'s Chain: does not aggro; alternates Giga Scream and Dread Dive; fast TP gain, so moves come often late.\n• Death from Above (bee) → Hornetneedle; Hovering Hotpot (magic pot) → Sleight Kukri; Diamond Daig (beetle) → Protecting Bangles; Nussknacker (lizard) → Sand Gloves.\n• Skulls (skeleton): Gluttony → Gluttony Sword, Sloth → Sloth Wand, Pride → Pride Staff, Greed → Greed Scimitar, Lust → Lust Dagger, Envy → Envy Spear, Wrath → Wrath Tabar.\n• Cwn Cyrff (hound) → Swan Bilbo; Boroka (hippogryph) → Boroka Earring*; Habetrot (crawler) → Twincoon; Demonic Tiphia (bee) → Tiphia Sting; Woodland Sage (treant) → Sunlight Pole.' }, { title = 'Floors 61-79', note = '• Picolaton (roc) → Thrakon Breastplate: only Stormwind; melee adds 20-50 wind damage; heavy Regain at low HP; immune to Sleep, Bind, Gravity.\n• Rogue Receptacle (magic pot) → Lyricist\'s Gonnelle: frequent Double Ray from the start (pierces Utsusemi); melee adds light damage.\n• Splacknuck (eft) → Knack Pendant: frequent Nimble Snap; permanent Enwater; Triple Attack.\n• Gloom Eye (ahriman) → Wit Pendant: alternates Eyes On Me and Blindeye (one hits 500+); Gravity/Bind fail; Paralyze, Slow, Blind work.\n• Barbaric Weapon (evil weapon) → Rover\'s Gloves: only Whirl of Rage, frequent late, each grants ~30 s Dread Spikes; Double Attack; Sleep/Bind/Gravity fail; Paralyze, Slow, Stun work.\n• Calchas (scorpion) → Fuchingiri: frequent Venom Storm (AoE poison 20 HP/3 s); Triple Attack; Sleep/Bind/Gravity fail.\n• Amemet (lizard) → Amemet Skin; Arachne (spider) → Arachne Web; Oni Carcass (doomed) → Onikiri; Shii (hound) → Sukesada; Yowie (raptor) → Yowie Skin.\n• Drexerion the Condemned (shadow) → Flagellant\'s Crossbow; Lizardtrap (flytrap) → Fenrir\'s Crown; Phanduron the Condemned (shadow) → Ascalon.\n• Ose (coeurl) → Assault Jerkin; Lumber Jack (beetle) → Bloodsword*; Elel (corse) → Frenzy Sallet*; Lindwurm (raptor) → Valiant Knife.' }, { title = 'Floors 81-99', note = '• Copper Borer (wamouracampa) → Wayang Kulit Mantle: never curls; permanent Blaze Spikes and Enfire; only Thermal Pulse (AoE fire, Blind, removes Utsusemi); Sleep/Bind/Gravity fail; Slow, Paralyze, Blind, Poison work.\n• Gharial (wivre) → Tartaglia: always double-hits hard; Demoralizing Roar is immediately followed by Boiling Blood; Regain; Heavy/Bind/Sleep fail; Poison, Paralyze, Blind, Slow work.\n• Aynu-kaysey (qutrub) → Cinquedea: Mangle is 3 hits (Shell helps); a single-hit stun attack; HP-draining melee; frequent Triple Attack; no magic.\n• Killer Jonny (cockatrice) → Fendoir: only Sound Vacuum; melee adds 100 HP/3 s poison; frequent Double Attack; low accuracy suits evasion tanks.\n• Ignamoth (wamoura) → Octant: Erratic Flutter and Fire Break (less damage at range); removes Utsusemi; hard hits that can Paralyze; Paralyze/Sleep/Bind/Heavy fail.\n• Narasimha (manticore) → Narasimha Hide; Lord of Onzozo (sea monk) → Octave Club (unconfirmed on BG-Wiki); Nis Puk (puk) → Tempest Belt; Ancient Goobbue (goobbue) → Daihannya.\n• Voluptuous Vivian (morbol) → Vivian Ring; Kreutzet (bird) → Sirocco Kukri; Ogama (doomed) → Amanojaku; Tarasque (lizard) → Ascention*; Ash Dragon (dragon) → Murasame.\n• Charybdis (sea monk) → Joyeuse; Bune (wyvern) → Enhancing Sword; Mahishasura (marid) → Veuglaire; King Arthro (crab) → Velocious Belt*.\n• * Not named by the wikis; Vanadreams uses the NM\'s home-zone drop.' }, { title = 'Survey boss floors', note = '• Floors 20/40/60: Stealthlord Haraal Ja, Dabargar the Stoic or Stheno. Floor 80: Lord Vryko. Floor 100: Dvali Jonah.\n• Choose the target floor at the lobby rune.' }, { title = 'Nyzul Isle NMs: three ??? items with a third result', note = '• These ??? items can now also appraise into the NM\'s own drop.\n• Bonnacon, ??? Footwear: Ash Clogs 81.8%, Tredecim Scythe 9.1%, Cure Clogs 9.1%.\n• Fraelissa, ??? Cape: Cotton Cape +1 81.8%, Bellicose Mantle 9.1%, Almogavar Bow 9.1%.\n• Argus, ??? Necklace: Regen Collar 81.8%, Peacock Charm 9.1%, Peacock Amulet 9.1%.' } } },
    { name = 'Guide: Nyzul Isle run guide', group = 'Server', desc = 'How to enter and run Nyzul Isle in both modes: orders, starting floors, floor objectives, tokens, bosses and rewards. Source: https://vanadreams.org/wiki/#guide-c_endgame_nyzul_run', steps = { { title = 'Overview', note = '• Orders: Sorrowful Sage, Aht Urhgan Whitegate Public Office (L-9). Entrance: Runic Seal in Alzadaal Undersea Ruins.\n• Up to 6 players clear each floor\'s objective to light the Rune of Transfer and climb; every 20th floor holds a boss.\n• Nyzul Isle Investigation: start from a floor your Runic Disc permits; rewards tokens, Vigil weapons and the Runic Key.\n• Uncharted Area Survey: level 99, floor 1 up to a chosen boss floor; rewards Rheic, Euxine, Tethyan armor and Phorcys, Thaumas, Nares sets.\n• Floor NMs and boss moves: see Nyzul Isle NMs.' }, { title = 'Getting in', note = '• Obtain an Imperial Army ID tag (requires a Mercenary rank; see Assault).\n• Holding the tag and no other orders, talk to the Sorrowful Sage and pick Investigation or Uncharted Area Survey; he exchanges the tag for Nyzul Isle Assault Orders.\n• Enter at the Runic Seal in Alzadaal Undersea Ruins.\n• Both modes: 1-6 players from the leader\'s party, each with their own orders, 30-minute limit, Trusts not allowed.\n• Investigation: any level, start floor bought with tokens. Survey: main job 99 (no Level Sync), always starts on floor 1.\n• Party members in the zone, within 50 yalms and holding orders enter together.\n• A cage of fireflies is provided for an early warp out.\n• The run fails if the entire party is down for 3 minutes.\n• Exit through the Rune of Transfer before time expires; tokens and Runic Disc updates are granted only then. Timing out gives nothing.' }, { title = 'Starting floor (Investigation)', note = '• Touching the lobby rune the first time grants the Runic Disc; afterwards the player who touches it chooses and pays the party\'s start floor in tokens.\n• Allowed starts: floor 1, or the first floor of any 5-floor block up to the block after your best record. The Runic Key unlocks every block.\n• Disc holders who exit via the rune get their best floor saved, but only if the run began at most one floor above their record.\n• Costs: floor 1 free; 6 = 500, rising 50 per block to 46 = 900; 51 = 1,000, rising 100 per block to 96 = 1,900.\n• Lobby Vending Box: temporary items (drinks, Strange Milk, Strange Juice, Dusty potions, a Reraise scroll) for 100, 200 or 300 tokens.' }, { title = 'The floors', note = '• Each floor has a random layout and objective; clearing it lights the rune, and the first player to touch it chooses to go up or leave. An objective never repeats twice in a row.\n• Eliminate the enemy leader: kill the single leader NM.\n• Eliminate specified enemies: kill all 2-5 marked foes (check as NMs) of one type: Heraldic Imps, Psycheflayers, Poroggo Gents, Ebony Puddings, Qiqirn Treasure Hunters, Qiqirn Archaeologists or Racing Chariots.\n• Eliminate the specified enemy: find the one regular monster that checks as an NM and kill it.\n• Eliminate all enemies: ramparts and NMs included; a Dahak may appear.\n• Activate all lamps: one of three lamp puzzles.\n• Free floor: at most once per run; clears itself after a few seconds.\n• Register lamp: a single lamp every player must touch once.\n• All-at-once lamps: 3-5 (more for bigger parties); each stays lit 30 s, then is locked 30 s. Put one player on each lamp and touch together.\n• In-order lamps: 3-5 with a hidden sequence; a wrong order goes dark after 10 s. Note each lamp\'s position to solve in 2-3 tries.\n• Archaic Gears (~1 floor in 6): the floor message forbids either being attacked by them or destroying them; a violation applies that floor\'s fixed penalty type.\n• Penalties: Time (-1 minute), Tokens (payout reduced), Restriction (random job ability, weapon skill, magic or stat restriction until the next floor).\n• Under "don\'t be attacked", route around gears; a gear already struck by someone is exempt, but one that aggroes or links on its own counts. Under "don\'t destroy", keep AoE away.\n• Most floors have an Archaic Rampart (sometimes two); kill only when the objective requires it.\n• 0-2 roaming NMs on most floors; each leaves an Armoury Crate with a ??? item and has a 20% Vigil weapon chance.\n• Regular monsters sometimes drop a small casket of temporary items.\n• The rune sometimes offers two paths; one has a 50% chance of a next-floor buff such as Regain, Regen, Refresh or Flurry.' }, { title = 'Tokens', note = '• Each cleared floor adds 200 tokens plus 10 per five floors climbed.\n• Parties of 4+: 10% less per extra member. Each gear token penalty: -117.\n• The final payout at the rune is doubled by the server\'s content currency rate.\n• A good Investigation party clears a floor in 1-2 minutes, about 10-15 floors per 30-minute run.' }, { title = 'Boss floors', note = '• Floors 20, 40, 60, 80, 100: the boss is the only objective; the nearby Archaic Rampart is optional.\n• Investigation: floors 20/40 Adamantoise, Behemoth or Fafnir; floors 60/80/100 Khimaira, Hydra or Cerberus.\n• Survey: floors 20/40/60 Stealthlord Haraal Ja, Dabargar the Stoic or Stheno; floor 80 Lord Vryko; floor 100 Dvali Jonah.' }, { title = 'Boss strategy', note = '• Adamantoise: very high defense, hard hits; use magic damage.\n• Behemoth: heavy attack; plain tank-and-spank with a strong healer.\n• Fafnir: high attack/defense, double attacks, very fast TP (frequent breaths). Stand at its flanks, keep tank shadows up, prepare for consecutive breaths.\n• Khimaira: stun-resistant, slight magic resistance; critical hits can break its wings.\n• Hydra: -90% magic damage, so use melee; resists poison, blind, silence, slow, stun, sleep. Heads break from crits, Shield Bash, Weapon Bash, jumps and steps; fewer heads slow its HP/TP regen and remove moves; heads regrow. Pyric Blast, Polar Blast, Barofield hit the front; Serpentine Tail hits behind.\n• Cerberus: double attacks, regen; resists poison, paralyze, blind, silence, slow. Below 25% gains TP rapidly and adds Gates of Hades; unload saved burst from 25%. Lava Spit and Sulfurous Breath hit the front, Scorching Lash behind.\n• Stealthlord Haraal Ja (Survey): high evasion, double attack; Perfect Dodge at 50%, switch to magic.\n• Dabargar the Stoic (Survey): high defense, -15% physical damage, regen; Invincible at 50%, stop weapon skills and nuke.\n• Stheno (Survey): fast-casting BLM; Manafont at 50%, spread out with Stoneskin and Shell up.\n• Lord Vryko (Survey, floor 80): extra and double attack, strong Regen/Regain; Blood Weapon at 60% heals it on hit, so kite or pull the tank back.\n• Dvali Jonah (Survey, floor 100): strong fast magic, high magic defense, Regain; Manafont at 40%, save Shell and burst for it.\n• Survey boss levels: 90 (floor 20), 95 (40), 100 (60), 105 (80), 110 (100). Survey floor monsters are high 80s-90s.' }, { title = 'Running the Survey', note = '• Choose the destination (20, 40, 60, 80 or 100) at the lobby rune.\n• At each lit rune choose: Advance one floor, Advance 2 to 11 floors (random, never past the destination), or Leave.\n• Take the random jump until within one floor of the destination; every floor still needs its objective, so fewer floors leaves more time for the boss.\n• Survey floor NMs each drop one Alexandrite and an Armoury Crate with a ??? item; enemy-leader floors use them as leaders.\n• Nothing is saved to the Runic Disc.' }, { title = 'Rewards', note = '• Investigation Vigil weapons: floor 20/40/60/80 bosses always drop one random; floor 100 drops two (one random, one for the disc holder\'s job if anyone in the party lacks it).\n• Boss armor: 10% chance per boss floor of one Askar, Denali or Goliard piece: feet 20, legs 40, hands 60, body 80, head 100.\n• Runic Key: defeat the floor 100 boss on a run started no more than one floor above your record; unlocks every starting block.\n• Mythic weapons: An Imperial Heist, the first Mythic quest, takes the Runic Key and a Vigil weapon to Abquhbah in Whitegate; the Vigil weapon sets which Mythic you pursue.\n• Tokens: spent on the Vending Box and starting floors.\n• Survey: Rheic, Euxine, Tethyan armor (NQ to +3), Phorcys, Thaumas, Nares sets, and astraria for choosing pieces (see Nyzul Isle Uncharted Area Survey).\n• Every boss and floor NM killed also rolls the server\'s upgrade material table (see Endgame materials).' } } },
    { name = 'Guide: Nyzul Isle Uncharted Area Survey', group = 'Server', desc = 'The level 99 Nyzul Isle mode: race from floor 1 to a chosen boss floor for Rheic, Euxine, Tethyan and Phorcys, Thaumas, Nares armor. Source: https://vanadreams.org/wiki/#guide-c_nyzul_survey_gear', steps = { { title = 'Overview', note = '• Level 99 Nyzul Isle variant with no Runic Disc progress: pick boss floor 20, 40, 60, 80 or 100 and race there.\n• Bosses drop Rheic, Euxine and Tethyan armor; floor 100 drops Phorcys, Thaumas and Nares.' }, { title = 'Requirements', note = '• Main job level 99 (Level Sync not accepted).\n• An Imperial Army ID tag.\n• 1-6 players, each holding their own orders.' }, { title = 'Getting the orders', note = '• Visit the Sorrowful Sage in the Nyzul Isle corner of the Public Office, Aht Urhgan Whitegate (L-9).\n• Speak to him holding an Imperial Army ID tag and no assault orders.\n• Choose Uncharted Area Survey; he swaps the tag for Survey orders (Nyzul Isle Investigation is still offered in the same menu).\n• Enter through the Runic Portal in Alzadaal Undersea Ruins.' }, { title = 'Inside', note = '• 30-minute limit; buffs are stripped on entry.\n• Always starts on floor 1; select the destination (20/40/60/80/100) at the lobby Rune of Transfer.\n• Each floor has an Investigation-style objective; once done, the rune lights and the first player to touch it picks: Advance one floor, Advance 2 to 11 floors (random, never past the destination), or Leave Nyzul Isle (ends the run, pays Nyzul Isle assault tokens).\n• Monsters are stronger than in the Investigation and scale up with depth.\n• Nothing is recorded on the Runic Disc.' }, { title = 'Boss floors', note = '• 20/40/60: random one of Stealthlord Haraal Ja (Mamool Ja ninja), Dabargar the Stoic (Troll paladin), Stheno (Lamia black mage).\n• 80: Lord Vryko (Vampyr dark knight), uses Blood Weapon when weakened.\n• 100: Dvali Jonah (Dvergr black mage), uses Manafont when weakened; defeating him gives the title Delver of the Depths.\n• Every boss uses its job\'s two-hour ability at low HP.' }, { title = 'Rewards', note = '• The destination boss puts 1-3 pieces in the treasure pool: floor 20 Rheic/Euxine/Tethyan NQ, 40 +1, 60 +2, 80 +3, 100 Phorcys/Thaumas/Nares.\n• Bosses occasionally also drop a Cotton Coin Purse.\n• Phorcys (lower grade Rheic): WAR PLD DRK BST SAM DRG; Salade, Korazin, Mitts, Dirs, Schuhs.\n• Thaumas (Euxine): MNK THF RNG NIN BLU COR PUP DNC RUN; Hat, Coat, Gloves, Kecks, Nails.\n• Nares (Tethyan): WHM BLM RDM BRD SMN SCH GEO; Cap, Saio, Cuffs, Trews, Clogs.\n• All pieces are Rare/Ex.' }, { title = 'Astraria: picking the piece you want', note = '• Repeat boss kills award astrarium key items, each exchangeable for one chosen piece from Berangere beside the Sorrowful Sage (L-9).\n• Bronze Astrarium: floor 20 boss x5 → a +1 piece.\n• Silver Astrarium: floor 40 boss x5 → a +2 piece.\n• Mythril Astrarium: floor 60 boss x5 → a +3 piece.\n• Gold Astrarium: floor 80 boss x5 → a Phorcys/Thaumas/Nares piece.\n• Platinum Astrarium: floor 100 boss x1 → a Phorcys/Thaumas/Nares piece.\n• Your kill count is shown after each kill. Only one of each astrarium can be held, so redeem before earning another.\n• To redeem: talk to Berangere, select astrarium, set, piece, then confirm; keep an inventory slot free.\n• Investigation floor 80 and 100 bosses also count toward Gold and Platinum astraria and also drop Phorcys/Thaumas/Nares pieces.' } } },
    { name = 'Guide: Oboro\'s Job Weapons', group = 'Server', desc = 'Oboro in Port Jeuno (E-6) forges one weapon per job from three crafted pieces plus 75 stones. Source: https://vanadreams.org/wiki/#guide-c_oboro_job_weapons', steps = { { title = 'Overview', note = '• Oboro, swordsmith at Port Jeuno (E-6), forges one weapon per job: Minos, Nyepel, Sindri, Kaladanda, Egeking, Sandung, Priwen, Cronus, Arktoi, Terpander, Lionsquall, Kurikaranotachi, Shigi, Areadbhar, Gridarvor, Mimesis, Deathlocke, Ohtas, Polyhymnia, Coeus, Dunna, Aettir.\n• His Aeonic weapon augments are unchanged.' }, { title = 'Who can ask', note = '• Qualify with either: a defeated Delve boss (Muyingwa, Dakuwaqa, Tojil in Cirdas Caverns [U]; Cailimh, Wopket, Utkux in Yorcia Weald [U]),\n• or a phantom gem battle (★ mission or avatar fight) cleared on Normal or higher.' }, { title = 'How it works', note = '• Talk to Oboro; if eligible he lists his weapons.\n• Trade in one go the weapon\'s three pieces plus 75 of a single stone type: Pluton, Beitetsu or Riftborn Boulder (no mixing).\n• The weapon is ready once Vana\'diel midnight has passed; speak to him then to receive it. Only one weapon can be in progress.\n• Trade a lone Cehuetzi Claw or Cehuetzi Pelt to hear the pieces for your current job. HQ pieces are refused.\n• WAR Minos: Cehuetzi Claw, Darksteel Voulge, Toporok. MNK Nyepel: Cehuetzi Pelt, Bone Patas, Koenigs Knuckles.\n• WHM Sindri: Cehuetzi Pelt, Darksteel Mace, Darksteel Maul. BLM Kaladanda: Cehuetzi Pelt, Mythic Pole, Dark Staff.\n• RDM Egeking: Cehuetzi Claw, Schlaeger, Anelace. THF Sandung: Cehuetzi Claw, Darksteel Knife, Misericorde.\n• PLD Priwen: Cehuetzi Pelt, Darksteel Shield, Januwiyah. DRK Cronus: Cehuetzi Claw, Ivory Sickle, Orichalcum Scythe.\n• BST Arktoi: Cehuetzi Claw, Darksteel Pick, Tabarzin. BRD Terpander: Cehuetzi Pelt, Ebony Harp, Shofar.\n• RNG Lionsquall: Cehuetzi Pelt, Hellfire, Matchlock Gun. SAM Kurikaranotachi: Cehuetzi Claw, Jindachi, Butachi.\n• NIN Shigi: Cehuetzi Claw, Muketsu, Hirenjaku. DRG Areadbhar: Cehuetzi Claw, Dark Mezraq, Orichalcum Lance.\n• SMN Gridarvor: Cehuetzi Pelt, Mahogany Staff, Light Staff. BLU Mimesis: Cehuetzi Claw, Shotel, Adaman Kilij.\n• COR Deathlocke: Cehuetzi Pelt, Hexagun, Matchlock Gun. PUP Ohtas: Cehuetzi Pelt, Darksteel Claws, Adaman Sainti.\n• DNC Polyhymnia: Cehuetzi Claw, Darksteel Kukri, Jambiya. SCH Coeus: Cehuetzi Pelt, Mahogany Pole, Ice Staff.\n• GEO Dunna: Cehuetzi Pelt, Imperial Wootz Ingot, Star Sapphire. RUN Aettir: Cehuetzi Claw, Zweihander, Nagan.' }, { title = 'Where the pieces come from', note = '• Cehuetzi Claw/Pelt: from Utkux (Delve boss, Yorcia Weald [U]); after defeating it, also from Forri-Porri\'s Mweya Plasm exchange in Western Adoulin.\n• Weapons and staves: crafted via Smithing, Woodworking, Goldsmithing or Bonecraft, or bought from players.\n• Imperial Wootz Ingot: Smithing. Star Sapphire: past-zone Campaign battle spoils and Abyssea Sturdy Pyxides.\n• Pluton, Beitetsu, Riftborn Boulder: ★ orb and phantom gem battlefields (Horlais Peak, Waughroon Shrine, Qu\'Bia Arena, Throne Room, etc.).' } } },
    { name = 'Guide: Odyssey material boxes', group = 'Server', desc = 'Sheol A, B and C boxes open from inventory into upgrade materials. Source: https://vanadreams.org/wiki/#guide-c_odyssey_material_boxes', steps = { { title = 'Overview', note = '• Open boxes from Sheol A/B/C in your inventory; a free slot is required.\n• Lustreless Scale / Hide / Wing Box: 10-20 of that material.\n• Large Lustreless Scale / Hide / Wing Box (Sheol exit reward): 40-50 of that material.\n• Trade the materials to the usual gear upgrade NPCs.' } } },
    { name = 'Guide: Odyssey, Sortie and Limbus: how to get in and move around', group = 'Server', desc = 'Entry requirements and movement rules for Limbus, Sortie and Odyssey Sheol on Vanadreams. Source: https://vanadreams.org/wiki/#guide-c_odyssey_sortie_limbus_fixes', steps = { { title = 'Limbus (Temenos and Apollyon)', note = '• Requires Scintillating Rhapsody, Chains of Promathia through "Garden of Antiquity", and the White Card (Temenos) or Black Card (Apollyon).\n• Monster level: talk to the Operator, select "Set monster level", choose a level.\n• Floor selection: Matter Diffusion Module in Temenos, gates in Apollyon; choose a tower, then a floor or "Coffer".\n• Mannequin damage now earns Unique Data like phase 2/3 NMs: party/alliance within 30 yalms gets 1 point per 1,000 damage (minimum 1 per hit).\n• 300 points open a coffer; cap is 3,000 (ten coffers).' }, { title = 'Sortie (Outer Ra\'Kaznar)', note = '• Complete Seekers of Adoulin, then talk to Ruspix in Leafallia for the Shiny plate; it recharges at midnight JST.\n• Enter via the Diaphanous Transposer in Kamihr Drifts; party members within 50 yalms join.\n• Trusts and pets are allowed.\n• Holding a Prime weapon at stage 2+: each sector boss (A-H) has a 15% extra chance at a Chunk of Octahedrite.\n• Holding one at stage 3+: bosses E-H also have a 1% chance at a Chunk of Hexahedrite.' }, { title = 'Odyssey Sheol', note = '• Next floor: the Veridical Conflux sits a few steps from the arrival point; unusable while monsters are chasing you.\n• Early exit: the Otherworldly Vortex next to the arrival point, with no exit reward.\n• Credited exit: on A-7, B-5 and C-4 that vortex grants gil per kill, bonus segments and, first time, access to the next Sheol.\n• Some treasure chests are Mimics; real ones give temporary items to the whole party.' } } },
    { name = 'Guide: Omen (Reisenjima Henge)', group = 'Server', desc = 'How to enter Omen and how its floors, bosses and additional objectives work. Source: https://vanadreams.org/wiki/#guide-c_omen', steps = { { title = 'Getting in', note = '• Get a Mystical Canteen from Incantrix in Reisenjima, next to the Earthly Concrescence (behind Ethereal Ingress #10): one per 20 hours, max 3 held.\n• Main job 99 required. The leader touches the Earthly Concrescence; alliance members within 30 yalms with a canteen enter and spend it.\n• If a run fails on floors 1-3 (timeout or wipe), Incantrix replaces the canteen.\n• 1-18 players; objectives scale up to 6 players.' }, { title = 'Leaving', note = '• Everyone gets a temporary Reisenjima Cage on entry; using it returns you alone to Reisenjima by the Earthly Concrescence.' }, { title = 'The run', note = '• Timer starts at 10 minutes; each Ethereal Ingress adds time (10 min, 20 entering floor 4, 30 entering the checkmate floor), capped at 50 minutes.\n• Monsters: tigers and flies on floor 1, beetles and leeches on floor 2.\n• Each floor rolls one objective: kill a set number of Sweetwater monsters, kill all Transcended monsters, kill everything, kill one hidden monster, or rarely a free floor. Completing it opens the Ethereal Ingress.\n• At floor 2\'s ingress, choose the light (to floor 3) or the light of checkmate (wave floor).\n• The floor 3 boss is a single Glassy monster (Gorger, Thinker or Craver); the distorted fragment drops on the first defeat.\n• Floor 3\'s ingress offers Kin, Gin, Kei, Kyou or Fu; the choice sets floor 4\'s monsters and floor 5\'s boss, which drops that piece\'s bead.\n• Checkmate floor: monsters from eight families arrive in waves of two. Clear it with the leader alive holding all five beads to fight Ou (everyone\'s beads are consumed).' }, { title = 'Boss special moves', note = '• View Sync, Pain Sync, Unfaltering Bravado, Dancing Fullers, Zero Hour and Gardez are announced in chat as "<boss> readies <move>!" 3 seconds early; at most one per boss every 15 seconds.\n• Glassy Craver\'s View Sync: pulls everyone within 25\', deals 1/5 of max HP, binds 10 s.\n• Kyou\'s Unfaltering Bravado is a cone; move behind or to the side during the readying.' }, { title = 'Additional objectives', note = '• They begin when something first notices you on a trash floor (weapon skills, critical hits, spells, abilities, kills, a single 2,000-damage hit).\n• Every 5 completed grants 2 Paragon cards for the main job.\n• Cards that don\'t fit are held for the job that earned them, even after a job change, and delivered at your next award or by Coelestrox.' } } },
    { name = 'Guide: Omen: the Reisenjima Cage', group = 'Server', desc = 'Entering Omen gives you a Reisenjima Cage for leaving at any time. Source: https://vanadreams.org/wiki/#guide-c_omen_reisenjima_cage', steps = { { title = 'Overview', note = '• You arrive on floor 1\'s arena with a Reisenjima Cage in inventory.\n• Use it anywhere in Omen to exit to Reisenjima beside the Earthly Concrescence.\n• Temporary item: removed when you leave.' } } },
    { name = 'Guide: Outpost Warps (Getting Around)', group = 'Server', desc = 'All characters on Vanadreams, new and existing, have all sixteen conquest outpost warps unlocked without supply runs. Source: https://vanadreams.org/wiki/#guide-c_outpost_warps', steps = { { title = 'How to use it', note = '• Speak to a conquest guard in your nation\'s city ("T.K.", "I.M." or "W.W." by gates and Mog House areas).\n• Pick the outpost teleport option and a region.\n• Pay in gil or conquest points (CP cost is 1/10 of the gil cost).\n• Homing Rings and Return Rings also use these warps: in a region your nation controls, they send you to its outpost.' }, { title = 'Unlocked regions', note = '• Format: region (outpost zone): level, fee.\n• Ronfaure (West Ronfaure): 10, 100 gil. Zulkheim (Valkurm Dunes): 10, 100 gil. Norvallen (Jugner Forest): 15, 150 gil. Gustaberg (North Gustaberg): 10, 100 gil.\n• Derfland (Pashhow Marshlands): 15, 150 gil. Sarutabaruta (West Sarutabaruta): 10, 100 gil. Kolshushu (Buburimu Peninsula): 10, 100 gil. Aragoneu (Meriphataud Mountains): 15, 150 gil.\n• Fauregandi (Beaucedine Glacier): 35, 350 gil. Valdeaunia (Xarcabard): 40, 400 gil. Qufim Island (Qufim Island): 15, 150 gil. Li\'Telor (The Sanctuary of Zi\'Tah): 25, 250 gil.\n• Kuzotz (Eastern Altepa Desert): 30, 300 gil. Vollbow (Cape Teriggan): 50, 500 gil. Elshimo Lowlands (Yuhtunga Jungle): 25, 250 gil. Elshimo Uplands (Yhoator Jungle): 35, 350 gil.' }, { title = 'Good to know', note = '• Main job must meet the listed level.\n• Listed fees apply when your nation holds the region; otherwise the warp costs 3x.\n• Tavnazian Archipelago is excluded: take its supply run from a guard and deliver it to the Lufaise Meadows outpost.\n• Movalpolos has no outpost warp.' } } },
    { name = 'Guide: Placeholder NMs that share a spawn point', group = 'Server', desc = 'Certain NMs occupy the same spot as their placeholders, so only one is up at a time; on Vanadreams the NM pops roughly 3 seconds after the killed placeholder fades, and the placeholders return once the NM dies. Source: https://vanadreams.org/wiki/#guide-c_placeholder_nm_pop_fix', steps = { { title = 'Overview', note = '• Kill the placeholder; the NM appears about 3 seconds after its body fades.\n• After the NM is defeated, placeholders respawn and the next placeholder kill pops it again.\n• Thousandarm Deshglesh: Ghelsba Outpost (north-east orc camp); Orcish Grunt, Orcish Stonechucker or Orcish Neckchopper on that spot.\n• Teporingo: Dangruf Wadi; Hoarder Hare.\n• Be\'Hya Hundredwall: Palborough Mines; Old Quadav or Copper Quadav.\n• Desmodont: Outer Horutoto Ruins; Stink Bats.\n• Antican Proconsul: Quicksand Caves; Antican Signifer.\n• Konjac: Toraimarai Canal; Mousse.\n• Enkelados: Upper Delkfutts\' Tower; Gigas Bonecutter.\n• Nightmare Vase and Rogue Receptacle: Ro\'Maeve; Magic Flagon.\n• Friar Rush: Den of Rancor; Bifrons.\n• Tawny-fingered Mugberry: Den of Rancor; Tonberry Slasher.\n• Bistre-hearted Malberry: Den of Rancor; Tonberry Beleaguerer.\n• Rampaging Ram: Konschtat Highlands; Tremor Ram.\n• Steelfleece Baldarich: Konschtat Highlands; kill Tremor Ram, then Rampaging Ram.' }, { title = 'Grand Marid', note = '• Not an NM; found in Bhaflau Thickets and Wajaom Woodlands.\n• Each shares its spawn point with a Marid, so a respawning point can produce either one.' }, { title = 'Chariotbuster Byakzak (Fort Ghelsba)', note = '• Killing the Orcish Panzer pops Byakzak in its place every time.\n• Without the fast-NM setting, the Panzer would be replaced by an Orcish Fighter and Byakzak would wait 21 to 24 hours.' }, { title = 'Jailer of Temperance (Grand Palace of Hu\'Xzoi)', note = '• Killing any of the five Eozdei Still in the Temperance area pops the Jailer where it died, with no cooldown.\n• Retail rule (not used here): one random Eozdei Still, rotating every 15 minutes, and a 15-minute wait after each pop.' }, { title = 'Bigmouth Billy (East Ronfaure)', note = '• Two of the Carrion Worms on the road east of the Gate of Rhoslind are placeholders: one roams near (453, -127), the other near (404, -16).\n• Billy pops where the killed placeholder fell.' }, { title = 'Roaming NMs appear at the placeholder', note = '• Most wandering field NMs now spawn on the spot their placeholder was killed, not somewhere on their patrol route.' } } },
    { name = 'Guide: Player damage rates', group = 'Server', desc = 'Vanadreams multipliers for player weapon skills, healing, items and recasts, plus the older rates they replaced. Source: https://vanadreams.org/wiki/#guide-c_player_damage', steps = { { title = 'Overview', note = '• Weapon skills deal 1.25x damage; skillchains from them get the same boost.\n• Elemental, Divine, Ninjutsu, Blue magic and Dark magic drains: normal damage.\n• Cures and healing Blue magic: 1.2x healing.\n• Potions, ethers and other healing items: 2.5x restore.\n• Job ability recasts: 15% shorter.\n• Haste and other delay reduction can lower weapon delay by up to 80%.\n• Monster spells: normal damage.\n• History: cure potency was 2.5x until 22 October 2026; weapon skills and spells were 2.5x until mid-October 2026.' } } },
    { name = 'Guide: Playing two characters at once (launcher)', group = 'Server', desc = 'Launcher versions newer than 0.2.39 start the game without a Windows UAC prompt, so you can run a second character alongside the first without disabling UAC. Source: https://vanadreams.org/wiki/#guide-c_launcher_two_clients', steps = { { title = 'Overview', note = '• Press Play on every profile you want running; each client launches with no prompt.\n• Exceptions that still prompt: official-game profiles, and game or Ashita folders inside Program Files.\n• To force admin rights for a profile: Profiles, tick Run as administrator, save; Windows will then prompt each time it starts.' } } },
    { name = 'Guide: Pulse weapons (Voidwatch)', group = 'Server', desc = 'All 15 Mog Kupon W-Pulse weapons are obtainable in game: Sagasinger from the Arch Dynamis Lord (Dynamis - Xarcabard), the other 14 as rare Riftworn Pyxis rewards after Voidwalker kills. Source: https://vanadreams.org/wiki/#guide-c_pulse_weapons', steps = { { title = 'How to get one', note = '• Sign up for a Voidwatch path with a Voidwatch Officer (Rolanberry Fields, Batallia Downs, Sauromugue Champaign, Qufim Island or a city officer); level 75+ required; you receive stratum abyssite and voidstones.\n• Defeat Voidwalkers on the path and upgrade abyssite at an Atmacite Refiner to the tier listed below.\n• In the target zone, locate a Planar Rift (visible on widescan; three per zone, any one calls the Voidwalker).\n• Optionally trade Phase Displacers (weaken the NM) and cells: Rubicund (red) raise reward quality and Pulse odds; Cobalt (blue) add reward rolls, up to 4.\n• Examine the rift twice to begin; each fight uses one voidstone and has a 30-minute limit.\n• After the kill a Riftworn Pyxis spawns; every participant may open it once within 3 minutes and rolls individually.\n• Pulse weapons are Rare/Ex; one you already own is never rolled for you.' }, { title = 'Where each weapon drops', note = '• Format: weapon (type) – Voidwalker – zone – abyssite – rift positions (x, z).\n• Coruscanti (dagger) – Qilin – The Shrine of Ru\'Avitau – Ashen III – (-68, 68), (68, 68), (-68, -68).\n• Asteria (dagger) and Ikarigiri* (katana) – Botulus Rex – Buburimu Peninsula – White VI – (80, -195), (360, -240), (-360, -200).\n• Ephemeron (sword) – Aello – Ru\'Aun Gardens – Ashen III – (377, 246), (-117, 436), (94, -459).\n• Borealis (great sword), Girru* (hand-to-hand), Adflictio* (scythe) – Ig-Alima – Valkurm Dunes – White VI – (720, 195), (650, 0), (-75, -45).\n• Aytanri (axe) – Morta – Aydeewa Subterrane – Amber II – (280, 396), (-153, 44), (437, 393).\n• Delphinius (polearm) – Bismarck – Bibiki Bay – Hyacinth II – (-643, -655), (-275, -920), (-120, -629).\n• Murasamemaru (great katana) – Uptala – Ve\'Lugannon Palace – Ashen III – (-119, -384), (379, 39), (-342, 280).\n• Gusterion* (dagger) – Ildebrann – Ifrit\'s Cauldron – Ashen I – (-269, -169), (-125, 170), (9, 290).\n• Himthige* (great axe) – Nympha Eunomia – Crawlers\' Nest [S] – White II – (55, 260), (-193, 197), (-137, 377).\n• Tenkomaru* (great katana) – Rw Nw Prt M Hrw – East Sarutabaruta – White IV – (-120, -415), (40, 280), (240, 560).\n• Dukkha* (club) – Voidwrought – Outer Horutoto Ruins – Jade IV – (-260, 740), (-380, 740), (-480, 760).\n• * Meeble Burrows does not exist on Vanadreams, so these were moved to the nearest family match: Gallu → Ig-Alima, Botulus → Botulus Rex, wyvern → Ildebrann, wamoura → Nympha Eunomia, grimoire → Rw Nw Prt M Hrw, construct → Voidwrought.\n• Girru and Ikarigiri also drop from Legion\'s Paramount Gallu and Paramount Botulus (Hall of Mul).' }, { title = 'Drop chance', note = '• Base ~5% per reward roll for a Pulse weapon; +3% per red light earned.\n• If an NM has several Pulse weapons, a hit selects one at random.\n• Additionally, each Pulse weapon on the NM gets a separate 2% roll per opened share.' }, { title = 'Named rewards', note = '• Each Voidwalker has a named-reward list, rolled per item for your share alongside the normal rare slot: 50% for "often" items, 10% for other named items, 2% for Pulse weapons.\n• Owned Rare items are skipped; a Rare item cannot appear twice in one share.\n• Sarimanok (East Ronfaure): Chimera Hairpin.\n• Krabimanjaro (Ordelle\'s Caves): Percept Bow, Carapacho Cuffs.\n• Belphoebe (Jugner Forest): Carabineer Dagger, Tefnut Wand.\n• Kholomodumo (Jugner Forest [S]): Genesis Shield, Genesis Locket, Kholomodumo\'s Hide.\n• Hahava (King Ranperre\'s Tomb): Ganesha\'s Mala, Ganesha\'s Mask (often).\n• Sallow Seymour (North Gustaberg): Apathy Gorget.\n• Ushumgal (North Gustaberg [S]): Accursed Belt.\n• Lorbulcrud (Gusgen Mines): Fulcrum Pole, Veisa Collar.\n• Murk-veined Baneberry (Pashhow Marshlands): Jingang Greatsword, Rancor Collar.\n• Melancholic Moira (Pashhow Marshlands [S]): Moira\'s Molar, Anger Bomblet, Appetence Crown.\n• Celaeno (Dangruf Wadi): Phineus\' Gun (often), Langeleik, Silver Mirror, Riftsand.\n• Virvatuli (West Sarutabaruta): Irrwisch Ring.\n• Ogbunabali (Maze of Shakhrami): Mantodea Harpe, Pipilaka Belt.\n• Lord Asag (Meriphataud Mountains): Tonatiuh Axe, Cadushi Grip.\n• Akupara (Meriphataud Mountains [S]): Deluxe Animator, Scuta Cape, Akupara Shell.\n• Voidwrought (Outer Horutoto Ruins): Dukkha (Pulse), Strendu Ring (often), Strendu Mantle.\n• Cherufe (Batallia Downs): Egoist\'s Tathlum, Tyrant\'s Ring, Silver Mirror.\n• Taweret (Batallia Downs [S]): Castellan\'s Shield, Justiciar\'s Torque, Silver Mirror.\n• Yatagarasu (Rolanberry Fields): Lenore\'s Hairpin, Corvax Sash.\n• Agathos (Rolanberry Fields [S]): Kaikias\' Cape, Eurus\' Ledelsens.\n• Goji (Sauromugue Champaign): Grotesque Cesti, Romanus Cape.\n• Gugalanna (Sauromugue Champaign [S]): Phrenic Torque, Bruiser\'s Earring.\n• Mellonia (Crawlers\' Nest): Oynos Knife, Whetted Molar, Silver Mirror.\n• Nympha Eunomia (Crawlers\' Nest [S]): Himthige (Pulse), Ban, Magma Gauntlets, Silver Mirror.\n• Roly-Poly (Garlaige Citadel): Wiglen Gorget, Putrid Cuspid, Silver Mirror.\n• Laidly Laurence (Garlaige Citadel [S]): Jurfu Cloak, Pavor Gauntlets, Silver Mirror.\n• Giltine (The Eldieme Necropolis [S]): Ultio Grip, Galvanic Slops, Silver Mirror.\n• Pil (Behemoth\'s Dominion): Dilaram\'s Sollerets, Dark Ixion Tail, Aliyat Chakram (often).\n• (List continues on the source page.)' }, { title = 'Provenance: Pil\'s arena', note = '• This arena combines the Beguiling, Seductive and Maddening Radiance fights; each winner gets whichever of the Beguiling, Seductive and Maddening Petrifacts they lack.\n• Named rewards at 10% each per share: Strategema Knife, Canute\'s Helm, Pensee Earring, Lenitive Abjuration: Hands, Bryoja\'s Staff, Myrmex Mittens, Wanion Belt, Nikko-ichimonji, Wohpe\'s Sabots, Folhardi Ring.' } } },
    { name = 'Guide: Quest and mission scene fixes (October 2026)', group = 'Server', desc = 'Many quests now use their real cutscenes and menus in place of stand-in dialog; the steps listed here are the ones whose play actually changed. Source: https://vanadreams.org/wiki/#guide-c_quest_scene_fixes_2026_10_16', steps = { { title = 'Adoulin', note = '• Do Not Go Into the Light: examine the hospital door in Western Adoulin to hand in the Inventors\' Coalition pickaxe; Othellius keeps it for Logan after Alianne and Othellius report his decline.\n• Hypocritical Oath: begins at Svenja\'s Manor door (I-8) one Vana\'diel day after the previous quest; you are sent to Maester Margret (Wegellion, rear of the Scouts\' Coalition, Eastern Adoulin). Trade him a Frost Turnip and a Vial of Slime Oil, then go back to the manor door (re-checking it beforehand repeats the request).\n• Epiphany (Rune Fencer empyrean): Octavernost\'s menu gives iridal cores for King Ranperre\'s Tomb, Fei\'Yin or Ranguemont Pass; afterward it can warp you to the Hazy Rune of your held core. Swapping a held core is unlimited; getting a core with none held is once per conquest tally.\n• Raptor Rapture and Scaredy Cats: choose "Might as well." to accept.\n• Survey: Yahse Hunting Grounds: examining an Ergon Locus plays the survey scene.\n• Yahse Hunting Grounds, Foret de Hennetiel, Yorcia Weald, Morimar Basalt Fields, Marjami Ravine, Kamihr Drifts, Maquette Abdhaljs: monsters and NPCs have correct names and their own talk scenes.' }, { title = 'Wings of the Goddess', note = '• Champion of the Dawn / The Dawn Also Rises: Cait Sith\'s menu offers the Nesanica belt, ring or torque, 10,000 gil, or the Cait Sith pact; rewards you own are hidden.\n• Beast from the East: starts only with the answer "Immensely, yes."\n• Son and Father: if Landeric refuses the Bronze Sword, trade it again.' }, { title = 'Treasures of Aht Urhgan and Abyssea', note = '• Promotion: Captain: speak to Abquhbah in Salaheem\'s Sentinels; Naja then needs 30 correct rubs, and a mistake resets the count.\n• An Imperial Heist (Mythic weapons): Naja offers it when you enter Salaheem\'s Sentinels or speak to her. Get the weapon list from Abquhbah, give him your job\'s Vigil weapon, hear Naja\'s briefing, return with the required titles. Trading a different weapon while one is held destroys the first.\n• The Voracious Resurgence 4-3 to 5-5 (Whitegate): Naja, Abquhbah, Raubahn, Ghatsad, Abda-Lurabda and Tateeya have full scenes and reminders; if your bag was full at reward time, talk to that NPC again.\n• Five Seconds of Fame: film is kept only if a shot was recorded.\n• Abyssea side quests (Bad Communication, Missing in Action, Smoke over the Coast, Soil and Green, His Box His Beloved, Sisters in Crime, Dropping the Bomb, others): real scenes; you must pick the accepting answer.\n• Missing in Action: Fariel, Mathurin and Quasim each play a scene when taking the linkpearl.\n• Unidentified Research Object: a plain Apple Pie is accepted.' }, { title = 'Rhapsodies and Voracious Resurgence missions', note = '• The Voracious Resurgence 3-5 (Of Knights and Orcs): at the Point of Interest choose "Yes." to "Climb the cliff?"; one scene plays before the fight and another after.\n• Rhapsodies 3-13 (Become Something More): the Sanctorium scene with your dark double plays when you zone in.' }, { title = 'Other', note = '• Ponono (Windurst Woods): a new cutting is 100,000 gil, ready after the next midnight; "I\'ve had enough" cancels.\n• Odin\'s gate (Odin\'s Chamber) and the Allied checkpoint guards (Jugner Forest [S]) use their correct scenes.' } } },
    { name = 'Guide: Quest Fixes: Furniture, Gargoyles, Charms and Rings', group = 'Server', desc = 'Fixed walkthrough steps for Unexpected Treasure, A Reputation in Ruins, the Black Mage Earthen Charm and Bard AF3 The Circle of Time. Source: https://vanadreams.org/wiki/#guide-c_original_quest_fixes_2026_10_16', steps = { { title = 'Unexpected Treasure (San d\'Oria)', note = '• Buy a Cupboard at Justi\'s Furniture (Northern San d\'Oria) and place it in your Mog House.\n• Leave and re-enter the Mog House, then speak to your Moogle for the Small Teacup.\n• Only one furniture quest can be completed per conquest tally; if you already did one, wait for the next tally.\n• Bring the teacup to Morunaude in Justi\'s shop, then to Calovour in the Cathedral.\n• Trade Calovour a Sprig of Mistletoe to receive 12,000 gil.' }, { title = 'A Reputation in Ruins (Jeuno)', note = '• In Pso\'Xja the gargoyle pairs (Gargoyle-Iota/-Kappa, then Gargoyle-Lambda/-Mu) alternate between physical immunity and magic immunity, both switching together about every 30 seconds.\n• Bring melee and magic, or change targets and tactics at each switch.\n• Gather the whole party inside before clicking the ???, since it shuts the door.' }, { title = 'Earthen Charm (Black Mage)', note = '• After completing The Root of the Problem (BLM AF3), speak to Kupipi in Heavens Tower for the key item Earthen Charm.\n• Use it to open the Gate of Earth in Inner Horutoto Ruins (Rose Tower side, entrance at East Sarutabaruta J-7).' }, { title = 'The Circle of Time (Bard AF3)', note = '• Digging the buried ring from the Perennial Snow in Xarcabard now gives the cleansed Star Ring key item, replacing the dirty one from The Requiem.\n• Surrender both the Star Ring and Moon Ring at the Monastic Cavern altar.' } } },
    { name = 'Guide: Quest, mission and NM changes (October 2026)', group = 'Server', desc = 'Player-visible changes to missions, quests, notorious monsters and town/travel NPCs from the October 2026 update. Source: https://vanadreams.org/wiki/#guide-c_zone_quest_and_nm_changes_2026_10_16', steps = { { title = 'Missions', note = '• Imperial Coronation (ToAU): Nadeey in Walahra Temple (Aht Urhgan Whitegate) replaces a lost ring, once per conquest tally.\n• Back to the Beginning → Light in the Darkness (WotG): wait one Vana\'diel day; Gentle Tiger repeats the wait message until Burden of Suspicion opens.\n• The Fighting Fourth (WotG): only one nation\'s quest may be pledged at a time; pledging plays the Turbulent Storm scene.\n• The Rites of Life (CoP 1-1) and A Shantotto Ascension mission 1: disconnecting mid-opening resumes the scene where it stopped.\n• The Davoi Report / Infiltrate Davoi (San d\'Oria): the Davoi wall marks are East, South and North Block Code, and the document is Lost Document.\n• A Shrouded Canopy (SoA): from this mission onward the Blockaded Path in Kamihr Drifts leads to Leafallia; earlier you only get "A snow-dusted crag blocks your path."\n• A Day in the Life of a Pioneer (SoA): choosing "Like Yesterday" in Levil\'s scene no longer freezes it.' }, { title = 'Quests', note = '• Campaign allegiance: you may switch nations\' allied forces; returning to a former nation costs two medal ranks; Bronze Ribbon is kept.\n• Lost Memories (Abyssea): repeatable after completion by trading 2 Lambent Scales for 480 cruor; a lost potion key item is reissued.\n• Wish Upon a Star (Bastok): use logging points in Yuhtunga or Yhoator Jungle; any swing where the hatchet survives may yield the Fallen Star.\n• Full Speed Ahead!: steep slopes drain raptor motivation faster (it sweats); use flat routes.\n• Monstrosity: the Feretory opening shows your own race and face.' }, { title = 'Notorious monsters', note = '• Coppercap (North Gustaberg [S]): stealing a Woozyshroom changes its cap; stealable Woozyshroom and Sleepshroom.\n• High-level Fomors (Lufaise Meadows): BRD, RDM, PLD, DRG, DRK and BLM Fomors drop Spectral Crimson.\n• Lamia No.19 (Arrapago Reef): random wander within her area instead of a set loop.\n• Mamool Ja / Two Horn the Savage (Mamook): stays facing you while moving between healing spots.\n• Moblin Fantocciniman, Automaton Assault (Mine Shaft #2716): a Thief can Steal his dice; afterward he only uses player-targeting rolls.\n• Fantoccini (Mine Shaft #2716): WHM, BLM and PLD puppets use more spells.\n• Chary Apkallu (Mount Zhayolm): high resistance to Bind, Sleep, Gravity.\n• Khimaira (Nyzul Isle): high Stun resistance.\n• Gem Heister Roorooroon, Stealth Bomber Gagaroon (Nyzul Isle): no bomb drops while slept or stunned.\n• Moblin Gurneyman (Oldton Movalpolos): versus a Trust only Poison II, Dia, Bio; other spells once a player has hate.\n• Hyakume (Ranguemont Pass): can spawn from any Hecteyes around its pond.\n• Shikigami Weapon (Ro\'Maeve): spawns anywhere on its ring path and returns to the closest point of it after combat.\n• Delicieuse Delphine, Erle (Rolanberry Fields [S]) and Mountain Worm NM (Uleguerand Range): stop chasing when they lose you.\n• Elel (Sacrarium): one of four spawn spots.\n• Charybdis (Sea Serpent Grotto): 2–8 hits per round.\n• Ix\'aern DRK (The Garden of Ru\'Hmet): on revival targets a previous attacker before the rest of the alliance.\n• Absolute Virtue (Al\'Taieu): waits for its last special\'s effect to end before the next; Wynav pets join in.\n• Jailer of Love (Al\'Taieu): pets attack the boss\'s target on spawning.' }, { title = 'Towns and travel', note = '• Gajaad (Al Zahbi) accepts Imperial Bronze Piece donations only while Al Zahbi holds the Astral Candescence.\n• Shihu-Danhu (Al Zahbi) asks you to recover the Astral Candescence when it is lost.\n• Runic Seal (Alzadaal Undersea Ruins): party leader gets "Commencing transport to Nyzul Isle!" on entry.\n• King Ranperre\'s Tomb: the stairway ??? plays a teleport animation first.\n• Priming Gate (Windurst Walls): standing on the door\'s inner edge no longer returns you to Toraimarai Canal.\n• Tonberry priest (Temple of Uggalepih): casts on you at the end of the scene after the hate reset.\n• Watchful Pixie (Beaucedine Glacier [S]): always opens with her line about her sister Callisto in Grauberg [S].' }, { title = 'Lebros Cavern (Excavation Duty)', note = '• A Qiqirn Mine detonates exactly at zero, and only if the player who placed it is still in combat.\n• Qiqirn Ceramists and Volcanists drop a Qiqirn Mine roughly one time in three.' } } },
    { name = 'Guide: Rare NM drops: better odds on the rare piece', group = 'Server', desc = 'Vanadreams reweights NM drops that pick one item from a pair or longer list so rarer pieces drop more often; tables list the per-monster odds. Source: https://vanadreams.org/wiki/#guide-c_nm_rare_drop_odds', steps = { { title = 'Monsters that drop one of two items', note = '• Paired drops (e.g. Behemoth: Thundercloud or Comet Tail): common 60%, rare 30%, nothing 10%.\n• Some monsters never give nothing; their odds are shown separately.\n• Treasure Hunter and server drop rate do not affect which of the pair you get.\n• Format: monster (zone): common / rare.\n• Tiamat (Attohwa Chasm): Wyrm Horn 60% / Dragon Heart 30%.\n• Bigho Headtaker B (Beadeaux): Power Crossbow 60% / Plantbane 30%.\n• Dadha Hundredmask (Beadeaux): Parrying Knife 60% / Mithran Scimitar 30%.\n• Gabhu Unvanquished (Beadeaux): Duel Rapier 60% / Valkyries Mask 30%.\n• Zokhu Blackcloud (Beadeaux): Marine Hat 60% / Faerie Shield 30%.\n• Behemoth (Behemoths Dominion): Thundercloud 60% / Comet Tail 30%.\n• King Behemoth (Behemoths Dominion): Pixie Earring 60% / Defending Ring 30%.\n• Mee Deggi The Punisher (Castle Oztroja): Impact Knuckles 65% / Ochimusha Kote 35%.\n• Moo Ouzi The Swiftblade (Castle Oztroja): Barbarians Sword 60% / Demonic Sword 30%.\n• Quu Domi The Gallant (Castle Oztroja): Strider Sword 65% / Sarutobi Kyahan 35%.\n• Yaa Haqa The Profane (Castle Oztroja): Frost Robe 60% / Earth Doublet 30%.\n• Yagudo Avatar (Castle Oztroja): Oak Staff 60% / Walrus Staff 30%.\n• Hawkeyed Dnatbat (Davoi): Archers Knife 60% / Assassins Bow 30%.\n• Poisonhand Gnadgad (Davoi): Jujitsu Sitabaki 60% / Jujitsu Gi 30%.\n• Steelbiter Gudrud (Davoi): Lizard Piercer 60% / Sentinels Mantle 30%.\n• Tigerbane Bakdak (Davoi): Warriors Axe 60% / Tigerhunter 30%.\n• Arch Dynamis Lord (Dynamis Xarcabard): Talekeeper 60% / Sagasinger 30%.\n• Hundredscar Hajwaj (Fort Ghelsba): Coarse Leggings 60% / Wild Cudgel 30%.\n• Thousandarm Deshglesh (Ghelsba Outpost): Obelisk 60% / Plate Belt 30%.\n• Juu Duzu The Whirlwind (Giddeus): Light Soleas 60% / Hunters Longbow 30%.\n• Vuu Puqu The Beguiler (Giddeus): Bird Whistle 60% / Bonzes Circlet 30%.\n• Vrtra (King Ranperres Tomb): Wyrm Horn 60% / Dragon Heart 30%.\n• Overlord Bakgodek (Monastic Cavern): Nightmare Sword 60% / Highlanders Targe 30%.\n• Bughi Howlblade (Palborough Mines): Marine Shield 65% / Scale Gorget 35%.\n• Nomho Crimsonarmor (Palborough Mines): Bonzes Circlet 65% / Pixie Mace 35%.\n• (Table continues on the source page.)' }, { title = 'Monsters that drop one of three or more items', note = '• Longer drop lists (ores, logs, scrolls, abjurations, Abyssea materials) are flattened: the rarest entries gain most, though common ones remain the most frequent.\n• Tzee Xicu The Manifest (Castle Oztroja): Damascus Ingot 10.89%; Spool Of Malboro Fiber 10.89%.\n• Morion Worm (Korroloka Tunnel): Chunk Of Darksteel Ore 20.17%; Chunk Of Tin Ore 31.67%.\n• Phantom Worm (Kuftal Tunnel): Chunk Of Adaman Ore 15%; Chunk Of Darksteel Ore 17.5%.\n• Ouryu (Riverne Site A01): Behemoth Hide 9.31%; Piece Of Oxblood 9.31%.' }, { title = 'Gration\'s Tatami Shield', note = '• Gration (Misareaux Coast): Tatami Shield rate raised from 15% to 24%; guaranteed if popped with a Picaroon\'s Shield.' }, { title = 'Endgame materials from every NM', note = '• Any NM near your level can drop endgame upgrade materials; major bosses drop them more often (see the guide Endgame upgrade materials outside their home content).' } } },
    { name = 'Guide: Records of Eminence, Sparks and Deeds', group = 'Server', desc = 'All 1,584 client Records of Eminence objectives exist on Vanadreams with their original sparks, EXP, accolades and rewards. Source: https://vanadreams.org/wiki/#guide-c_records_of_eminence', steps = { { title = 'Highlights', note = '• Reives: Lair, Colonization and Subjugation objectives in all Adoulin zones; Lair records pay that area\'s Yggrete rock.\n• Wildskeeper Reives: each Sovereign Subjugation objective awards its Naakual paragon.\n• Seven Treasures: holding all six paragons, choose Exchange the Seven Treasures at a Records of Eminence guide (Rolandienne, Isakoth, Fhelm Jobeizat or Eternal Flame) for one IL115 Sovereign item.\n• Harvesting objectives for Adoulin, the Gates, Outer Ra\'Kaznar and Abyssea, including each zone\'s "II" rare-material record.\n• Subjugations: Outer Ra\'Kaznar [U] bosses, Reisenjima Henge bosses, all Sortie bosses.\n• Level Cap Increase 75 for BLU, COR, PUP, DNC, SCH, GEO, RUN.\n• Max fame in all 14 areas.\n• Entering Dynamis in all six cities; Sheol A/B/C exits in Odyssey.\n• Weekly objectives, Vana\'bout objectives (pay plaudits), and Artifact/Relic/Empyrean/Ambuscade gear progression records.' }, { title = 'Monthly objectives and deeds', note = '• Each monthly objective is completable once per calendar month (Japan time) and pays a special item (e.g. Silver A.M.A.N. Voucher, Trust Primer, Mars Orb, Abdhaljs Seal); some also pay deeds of heroism.\n• Monthly topics: talking to Greyson (Lower Jeuno), home points in your nation, Unity chat, Conquest kills under Signet/Sanction/Sigil/Ionis, Reive bayld, Ambuscade (party and Intense), Omen, Dynamis - Divergence, Mog Garden, Unity Wanted, Peculiar Foes.\n• Spend deeds at the A.M.A.N. Validator in Bastok Markets, Southern San d\'Oria or Windurst Woods; the first visit completes its own record.' } } },
    { name = 'Guide: Records of Eminence: Peculiar Foes', group = 'Server', desc = 'Peculiar Foes I–XV (records 3789–3803) each task you with defeating an "Awoken" level 119 version of a well-known NM. Source: https://vanadreams.org/wiki/#guide-c_peculiar_foes', steps = { { title = 'How to fight one', note = '• Accept that zone\'s Peculiar Foes objective in Records of Eminence.\n• Go to the Peculiar Footprints (coordinates below) and examine them.\n• The Awoken NM spawns already claimed by you; the footprints vanish for 5 minutes, so one group at a time.\n• Defeat it to complete the record. All Awoken NMs are level 119.' }, { title = 'Footprint locations', note = '• Format: record – objective – NM – zone – footprints (x, y, z).\n• 3789 – I – Awoken Hildesvini – Wajaom Woodlands – -80.7, -8, -638.2\n• 3790 – II – Awoken Mokkuralfi – Mount Zhayolm – 333.9, -14.5, -361.5\n• 3791 – III – Awoken Vampyr Jarl – Caedarva Mire – 784.9, -12.3, 647.2\n• 3792 – IV – Awoken Gorgimera – Beaucedine Glacier – 401.3, 0, 279.2\n• 3793 – V – Awoken Ariri Samariri – Palborough Mines – 24, -31.5, -106\n• 3794 – VI – Awoken Hrungnir – Aydeewa Subterrane – -211, 8.5, 96\n• 3795 – VII – Awoken Morbol Emperor – Arrapago Reef – -391, -3.7, 330\n• 3796 – VIII – Awoken Stoorworm – Reisenjima – -584.5, -417.4, -1051.6\n• 3797 – IX – Awoken Dendainsonne – Western Altepa Desert – -19, 0.6, 170\n• 3798 – X – Awoken Freke – Batallia Downs – 233, 7.9, 76\n• 3799 – XI – Awoken Tanngrisnir – Qufim Island – -190.7, -19.7, 45.2\n• 3800 – XII – Awoken Nihhus – Kamihr Drifts – -268.6, 20.1, 67.5\n• 3801 – XIII – Awoken Hakenmann – Rala Waterways – 307, -5.8, 107\n• 3802 – XIV – Awoken Andhrimnir – Newton Movalpolos – 350.4, 26, -48.4\n• 3803 – XV – Awoken Hrani, Awoken Hjorvarth, Awoken Angantyr – Xarcabard – -424.2, -44.1, -14.6' }, { title = 'Peculiar Foes XV: the Xarcabard trio', note = '• All three spawn together from the Xarcabard footprints.\n• Awoken Angantyr is immune to damage while guards Hrani and Hjorvarth live.\n• Each guard killed removes one third of Angantyr\'s max HP; with both dead it takes normal damage.\n• Kill the two guards first.' } } },
    { name = 'Guide: Relic, Mythic and Empyrean weapons: 99 to 119 III', group = 'Server', desc = 'Oboro in Port Jeuno (E-6) upgrades level 99 Relic, Mythic, Ergon and Empyrean weapons to 119 and then 119 III using weapon-specific stones. Source: https://vanadreams.org/wiki/#guide-c_relic_mythic_empyrean_119', steps = { { title = 'Before you start', note = '• Requirement: a defeated Delve boss in Cirdas Caverns [U] or Yorcia Weald [U], or a high-tier mission or avatar battlefield cleared on Normal or above.\n• Stones: Relic = Pluton; Mythic and Ergon = Beitetsu; Empyrean = Riftborn Boulder.\n• Delve field NMs: a stone per alliance member, sometimes a case.\n• Delve fractures: each NM gives everyone a stone (sometimes a case); the boss gives everyone a case (sometimes a box).\n• Wildskeeper Reives: a case per participant, sometimes a box.\n• Lair Reives: a stone each; Colonization Reives: occasionally a stone.\n• Forri-Porri (Western Adoulin): 10 stones for 2,500 Mweya Plasm.\n• Also: high-tier mission battlefields, Unity Wanted coffers, Gobbie Mystery Box, Mog Bonanza coffers (99 stones each).\n• Case = 3–15 stones; box = 15–30.' }, { title = 'Optional: get the afterglow (99 II) first', note = '• The orange Magian Moogle in Port Jeuno has an afterglow trial for each level 99 weapon.\n• Relics and Mythics: trade 250 Vials of Umbral Marrow.\n• Empyreans: trade 3,000 Riftdross or Riftcinder (depends on weapon).' }, { title = 'Step 1: 99 to 119', note = '• Trade Oboro the level 99 weapon plus 150 of its stone.\n• Return after the next Vana\'diel midnight for the level 119 weapon.\n• Trading the 99 II (afterglow) version returns the 119 II instead, which makes Step 2 nearly free.' }, { title = 'Step 2: 119 to 119 III', note = '• Obtain the key item Scintillating Rhapsody by completing the Rhapsodies of Vana\'diel story.\n• Trade Oboro the 119 weapon alone.\n• Pay its stones over any number of trades: 5,000 for a 119, only 1 for a 119 II.\n• Talk to Oboro anytime to check your paid total.\n• Once fully paid, return after the next Vana\'diel midnight for the 119 III.\n• Stones paid are not refunded if you stop; he handles one weapon at a time.\n• Ergon weapons (Epeolatry, Idris) use the same process with Beitetsu.' } } },
    { name = 'Guide: Rhapsodies of Vana\'diel 2-12: Prime Number', group = 'Server', desc = 'Walkthrough for RoV 2-12, which completes on arrival in Alzadaal Undersea Ruins, plus what to do if the scene does not trigger. Source: https://vanadreams.org/wiki/#guide-c_rov_2_12_prime_number', steps = { { title = 'Walkthrough', note = '• Prerequisite: complete 2-11 Take Wing (scene at the Shaharat Teahouse, Aht Urhgan Whitegate).\n• Travel to Alzadaal Undersea Ruins by any route; simplest is the Runic Portal in Whitegate\'s Chamber of Passage to the Nyzul Isle Staging Point.\n• Watch the arrival cutscene with Nashmeira, Tenzen, Iroha and Alexander; the mission completes.\n• Optional: entering The Shrouded Maw afterward plays a brief scene with Volto Oscuro and Diabolos.\n• Next mission: 2-13 From the Ruins; speak to the Imperial Whitegate in Aht Urhgan Whitegate.' }, { title = 'Nothing happens when I enter Alzadaal?', note = '• Tenzen and Aphmau must both be free.\n• Tenzen is busy if your current CoP mission is The Call of the Wyrmking, A Vessel Without a Captain, Desires of Emptiness, The Warrior\'s Path, Garden of Antiquity, When Angels Fall, or Dawn (before its later steps).\n• Aphmau is busy during ToAU up to Imperial Coronation.\n• Advance those storylines; the login message names who is busy.\n• If stuck in a cutscene, type !csfix.' } } },
    { name = 'Guide: Salvage', group = 'Server', desc = 'Party content in the four Remnants beneath Alzadaal Undersea Ruins, cleared one floor at a time for Salvage armor and other loot. Source: https://vanadreams.org/wiki/#guide-c_salvage', steps = { { title = 'Getting in', note = '• Remnants Permit: Zasshal, Aht Urhgan Whitegate, 500 Assault Points from any single Assault area.\n• Limit one per day, resetting at JST midnight; consumed on entry.\n• Gilded Gateway coordinates in Alzadaal Undersea Ruins: Arrapago Remnants (-580, 0, -159); Zhayolm Remnants (-580, 0, -405); Bhaflau Remnants (620, -2, -202); Silver Sea Remnants (580, -2, 442).' }, { title = 'Silver Sea Remnants floors', note = '• Ashu Talif deck: kill Hammerblow Majanun, then the crew that floods the central hall; the porter to the north then opens.\n• Next is the west or east wing at random: west = crew and imps, then Dekka; east = crew and devilets, then Powderkeg Yanadahn.\n• Cells traded into the socket pop Gakke.\n• Rampart halls: break the four ramparts at the arrival point, then those of the west or east hall; Don Poroggo and bonus crates are in the north hall.\n• Next floor: two Archaic Chariots, protected by ramparts and gears.\n• Final: Long-Armed Chariot; a Zhayolm card in the slot pops Citadel Chelonian.' }, { title = 'Salvage armor (Ghanraam, Whitegate)', note = '• Ghanraam converts three Salvage pieces + 10 Imperial Gold Pieces into one set piece for that slot, ready after the next JST midnight.\n• Ares\': Enyo\'s + Phobos\'s + Deimos\'s.\n• Skadi\'s: Njord\'s + Freyr\'s + Freya\'s.\n• Usukane: Hoshikazu + Tsukikazu + Hikazu.\n• Marduk\'s: Anu\'s + Ea\'s + Enlil\'s.\n• Morrigan\'s: Nemain\'s + Bodb\'s + Macha\'s.' }, { title = 'Remnants monster drops', note = '• Remnants mobs now drop their complete loot tables, Salvage plans and armor pieces included (previously only some floor rewards dropped).\n• Bhaflau Reactionary Ramparts never rest, so no HP regain between pulls.\n• Bhaflau Tragopans scatter on spawn instead of stacking on one spot.' }, { title = 'Silver Sea Remnants: the Ashu Talif crew on the deck (floor 1)', note = '• Most crew drop roughly four random cells; two groups have fixed drops.\n• West row of six fomors (south to north): 1st Humilus x3 + Spissatus x1; 2nd Opacus x3 + Pannus x1; 3rd Cumulus x3 + Stratus x1; 4th Incus x3 + Radiatus x1; 5th Praecipitatio x3 + Undulatus x1; 6th Duplicatus x3 + Congestus x1.\n• East large room, eight fomors, one set each: Incus x3 + Pannus x2; Opacus x3 + Radiatus x2; Humilus x3 + Pileus x2; Praecipitatio x3 + Castellanus x2; Undulatus x3 + Cirrocumulus x2; Congestus x3 + Virga x2; Cumulus x3 + Spissatus x2; Duplicatus x3 + Stratus x2.\n• East small rooms: 25% per fomor to leave a crate with one random temporary item (Fighter\'s, Oracle\'s, Assassin\'s, Spy\'s, Braver\'s, Soldier\'s, Champion\'s, Monarch\'s, Gnostic\'s or Cleric\'s Drink, Strange Milk, Strange Juice, Dusty Potion, Dusty Ether, Dusty Elixir).\n• The crate won\'t open for you if you already hold the item it rolled.' }, { title = 'Zhayolm Remnants: Poroggo Madame (floor 3)', note = '• Breaking the floor 3 ramparts pops a Poroggo Madame, who now has loot (previously none).\n• Popped from the south group: 5 Humilus Cells + 5 Spissatus Cells.\n• Popped from the north group: Enyo\'s Gauntlets + Nemain\'s Cuffs.' } } },
    { name = 'Guide: Salvage +1 armor (Mrohk Sahjuuli)', group = 'Server', desc = 'Upgrading the five Salvage sets to +1 with a finished base piece, its Salvage II counterpart, design plans and Imperial Gold Pieces. Source: https://vanadreams.org/wiki/#guide-c_salvage_plus_one', steps = { { title = 'Overview', note = '• Sets: Ares\', Skadi\'s, Usukane, Marduk\'s, Morrigan\'s; base pieces come from Ghanraam (see Salvage).\n• Ares\': Ares\' Cuirass, Gauntlets, Flanchard, Sollerets, Mask.\n• Skadi\'s: Skadi\'s Cuirie, Bazubands, Chausses, Jambeaux, Visor.\n• Usukane: Usukane Haramaki, Gote, Hizayoroi, Sune-Ate, Somen.\n• Marduk\'s: Marduk\'s Jubbah, Dastanas, Shalwar, Crackows, Tiara.\n• Morrigan\'s: Morrigan\'s Robe, Cuffs, Slops, Pgch., Coron.' }, { title = 'Mrohk Sahjuuli', note = '• Location: Aht Urhgan Whitegate, I-11, ground floor, near (23, 0, -88).\n• Trade in one go: base piece + same-slot Salvage II piece + plans + gold; the +1 is given immediately (no day change needed).\n• Talk to her for recipes; trade a single base or Salvage II piece to hear exactly what it requires.\n• Ares\' +1: Ate\'s piece + Copy of Bloodshed Plans (red).\n• Skadi\'s +1: Idi\'s piece + Copy of Umbrage Plans (blue).\n• Usukane +1: Genta piece + Copy of Ritualistic Plans (yellow).\n• Marduk\'s +1: Namru\'s piece + Copy of Tutelary Plans (green).\n• Morrigan\'s +1: Neit\'s piece + Copy of Primacy Plans (purple).\n• Plans needed: head 40, body 50, hands 45, legs 45, feet 40; plus 15 Imperial Gold Pieces per piece.\n• An active server upgrade-cost discount lowers these; ask her for current numbers.\n• Imperial Gold Pieces: Ugrihd in Whitegate, for Imperial Standing.' }, { title = 'Where the Salvage II pieces and plans drop', note = '• Each Remnants\' final chariot: one Salvage II piece fairly often, sometimes two, and always several plans in that Remnants\' colours; listed floor NMs can also drop plans.\n• Zhayolm, Battleclad Chariot: Ate\'s mask/gauntlets/flanchard; Idi\'s jerkin/trousers/ledelsens; Genta kabuto; Namru\'s jubbah/crackows; Neit\'s cuffs. Plans red, blue. Plan NMs: Archaic Chariot, Jakko.\n• Arrapago, Armored Chariot: Ate\'s cuirass; Idi\'s mask/gloves; Genta gote/hakama/sune-ate; Namru\'s tiara; Neit\'s coat/slops/pigaches. Plans red, blue. Plan NMs: Archaic Chariot, Princess Pudding, Migrant Russula.\n• Bhaflau, Long-Bowed Chariot: Ate\'s mask/gauntlets/flanchard/sollerets; Idi\'s mask/jerkin/ledelsens; Genta hara-ate; Namru\'s dastanas/shalwar/crackows; Neit\'s crown/coat/cuffs/slops. Plans yellow, green, purple. Plan NMs: Archaic Chariot, Skirmish Pephredo, Zebra Zachary.\n• Silver Sea, Long-Armed Chariot: Ate\'s cuirass/sollerets; Idi\'s gloves/trousers; all five Genta pieces; Namru\'s tiara/jubbah/dastanas/shalwar; Neit\'s crown/pigaches. Plans green, purple. Plan NMs: Hammerblow Majanun, Powderkeg Yanadahn, Dekka, Citadel Chelonian.\n• Blue (Skadi\'s) plans: Zhayolm and Arrapago only. Yellow (Usukane) plans: Bhaflau only.\n• Retail drops these in level 96+ Remnants II, which this server lacks, so regular Remnants bosses drop them.' } } },
    { name = 'Guide: Salvage run guide', group = 'Server', desc = 'Run walkthrough for Zhayolm, Arrapago, Bhaflau and Silver Sea Remnants: entry rules, cells, pops, floor routes, boss notes and rewards. Permit, gateway positions and Ghanraam sets are on Salvage; +1 sets on Salvage +1 armor. Source: https://vanadreams.org/wiki/#guide-c_endgame_salvage_run', steps = { { title = 'Getting in', note = '• Every player needs a Remnants Permit: Zasshal (Whitegate), 500 points from one Assault area, one per day, consumed on entry; also sold by Clan Centurio\'s Provisioner.\n• Main job level 65+.\n• Leader touches the Gilded Gateway; party members in the zone, within 50 yalms and holding a permit enter. One missing permit or distant member blocks the whole party.\n• The gateway refuses the party if anyone carries an imbued item.\n• No Trusts in any Remnants.\n• Time limit 100 minutes; warnings at 10, 5 and 1 minute.\n• Run fails if everyone is KO\'d for 3 minutes.\n• Each player receives that Remnants\' cage of fireflies on entry; use it to warp out.' }, { title = 'What happens when you enter', note = '• Gear is removed and five restrictions apply for the run unless lifted by cells.\n• Encumbrance: all slots locked; one cell per slot pair.\n• Obliviscence: no support job; Duplicatus Cell.\n• Impairment: no job abilities or weapon skills; Opacus Cell.\n• Omerta: no magic; Praecipitatio Cell.\n• Debilitation: STR, DEX, VIT, AGI, INT, MND, CHR -30 each, max HP/MP -40%; one cell per stat.\n• Equipment cells: Incus main/sub; Castellanus head/neck; Cumulus body; Radiatus hands; Stratus legs/feet; Cirrocumulus waist/back; Undulatus ranged/ammo; Virga earrings/rings.\n• Stat cells: Pannus STR; Fractus DEX; Congestus VIT; Nimbus AGI; Velum INT; Pileus MND; Mediocris CHR; Humilus HP; Spissatus MP.\n• Cells work only inside. A starting crate near the entrance is lotted by the party; in Zhayolm, Arrapago and Bhaflau it holds 2 Incus, 1 Duplicatus, 1 Praecipitatio, 1 Opacus, one more Praecipitatio or Opacus, and 4 random cells. Later cells come from mobs.' }, { title = 'Who gets the cells', note = '• Recommended order: Incus to damage dealers and tank; Praecipitatio to the healer, then other mages; Opacus to weapon-skill damage dealers and the tank.\n• Then Duplicatus, then Humilus and Spissatus, then equipment cells for important slots; stat cells (30 of one stat each) last.\n• Using a magic, ability or stat cell also lifts that restriction from your pet.' }, { title = 'Pops: Sockets and Slots', note = '• Each Remnants has one Socket and one Slot on the route, both optional NMs.\n• Socket: trade 1-5 cells of a single type; its NM drops double the cells traded.\n• Slot: trade one card from another Remnants; its NM always drops a Salvage armor piece.\n• Zhayolm: Socket Poroggo Madame; Slot takes Silver Sea Card, pops Jakko (always Njord\'s Jerkin).\n• Arrapago: Socket Vile Wahzil; Slot takes Bhaflau Card, pops Princess Pudding (always Hoshikazu Gi).\n• Bhaflau: Socket Flux Flan; Slot takes Arrapago Card, pops Demented Jalaawa (always Anu\'s Doublet).\n• Silver Sea: Socket Gakke; Slot takes Zhayolm Card, pops Citadel Chelonian (always Nemain\'s Crown).\n• Zhayolm Cards: Zhayolm\'s Archaic Chariots, Gears and Ramparts (usually a few per full run).\n• Arrapago Cards: Arrapago\'s Archaic Gears, Gear and Ramparts.\n• Bhaflau Cards: Reactionary Ramparts in Bhaflau bonus rooms; rarely its Archaic Chariots and Gear.\n• Silver Sea Cards: no drop; Clan Centurio\'s Provisioner, pop items, 1,000 clan points.' }, { title = 'Zhayolm Remnants', note = '• Entry day matters: Poroggo Madames are immune to that day\'s element (double damage on Darksday), and it decides the floor 4 rampart.\n• Floor 1: open the first door; groups of Puks, Ziz, a Vagrant Lindwurm and Bull Bugards plus some Mamool Ja Zenists roam. Each wiped group pops a Poroggo Gent.\n• Kill the first Gent with no cells used and nobody dead to pop a Poroggo Madame (often drops Enyo\'s Gauntlets, Nemain\'s Cuffs, Anu\'s Brais, Hoshikazu Kyahan or Njord\'s Mask); cell up afterwards. Each of the four doors leads to a different floor 2 corner.\n• Floor 2: clear your corner\'s eight Draco Lizards or Wyverns to pop its Mamool Ja leader; its death clears the floor. Socket and Slot appear, and the other three corners fill with cell-carrying mobs. Take the porter when ready.\n• Floor 3: south and north paths, each a large Mamool Ja group with an Archaic Rampart; wiping one group including its rampart pops a Madame. Then take that path\'s porter.\n• Floor 4 rampart by entry day: Firesday/Earthsday First; Watersday/Windsday Second; Iceday/Lightningday Third; Lightsday/Darksday Fourth.\n• Floor 4 north: pulling any rampart despawns the other three; a wrong pick sends you to the other north room to retry. South: all four stay; kill the correct one.\n• Bonus Madames: reach the south path within 47 minutes of entry for a Madame with a temporary-item crate; reach the north path within 30 minutes for a Madame that always drops Anu\'s Brais, Hoshikazu Kyahan and Njord\'s Mask.\n• Floor 5: two routes, each three rooms of patrolling Archaic Gears (some sleepable, some not), with ramparts and an Archaic Chariot. A Madame pops once enough players have lifted all five restrictions: three on the north route, one on the south.' }, { title = 'Arrapago Remnants', note = '• Floor 1: the first door releases the cell crate; Lamia and Merrow here can break weapons. Ten kills pop an Archaic Rampart; any of four porters goes up.\n• Floor 2: one corner per porter; the Slot (Princess Pudding) is in one corner and the Socket (Vile Wahzil) in another; only your arrival corner\'s pop is reachable.\n• Middle floors: engaged Qiqirn Astrologers flee a set path and vanish unless killed; Qiqirn Treasure Hunters patrol a loop laying mines. Use ranged attacks, Bind or a quick finish.\n• Floor 5: two routes, each with ramparts, an Astrologer and an Archaic Chariot.\n• Floor 6: gears and ramparts; ten kills open the door up. Clear within 7 minutes of arriving for two extra Treasure Hunters on the way.\n• Floor 7: Armored Chariot; 30 seconds after it dies everyone is returned to the Gilded Gateway, so lot fast.' }, { title = 'Bhaflau Remnants', note = '• Open the starting cell crate before anyone uses the first porter; the porter removes the floor\'s crates.\n• Floor 1: pick the east or west entrance (the other seals). Wamouracampa drop equipment cells, Carmine Eruca stat cells, others Incus, Duplicatus, Humilus or Spissatus.\n• Mad Bomber (in half the runs): grows every 20 seconds and self-destructs at about 75 seconds. Killing it first pops a Dormant Rampart that leads to a bonus room.\n• Bonus room Reactionary Rampart: doesn\'t attack; calls an add every 10-15 seconds, losing some HP each time, sometimes an NM; you return when it dies. Main Bhaflau Card source.\n• Floor 2: four Empathic Flans in the centre (two weak to magic, two to weapons). Weapon damage makes one grow spikes; spiked, it ignores weapons and takes heavy magic damage. Kill all four while spiked for a second Dormant Rampart and Reactionary room.\n• Floor 2 west wing first door: 50% chance of the Socket (Flux Flan).\n• Floor 3: four quadrants: Trolls north, Black Puddings south (some resist magic, some weapons). Slot (Demented Jalaawa) is behind the south-centre door.\n• Floor 4: west or east, each with gears and an Archaic Chariot. Optional, but the west chariot\'s death removes 100 defense from the final boss, the east one 100 attack. Melee groups go west; groups struggling to survive go east.\n• Floor 5: Long-Bowed Chariot; afterwards one of two exits lights.' }, { title = 'Silver Sea Remnants', note = '• Full floor order is on Salvage.\n• Floor 1: kill Hammerblow Majanun to open the central hall, then clear the crew that rushes in.\n• Floor 2 west: clear the south rooms, then Dekka in the north room (Socket Gakke is there). East: Powderkeg Yanadahn opens the north room; clear it.\n• Floor 3: break the four arrival ramparts to open the west, east and north halls.\n• North hall (if time allows): Don Poroggo always drops Enyo\'s Breastplate and Nemain\'s Robe and leaves three crates; a Gyroscopic Gear there always drops Anu\'s Gages.\n• Then clear the west or east hall\'s ramparts to light its porter; east hall Gyroscopic Gears always drop Enyo\'s Mask.\n• Floor 4: kill both Archaic Chariots (ramparts and gears nearby) to light the porter.\n• Floor 5: Slot (Citadel Chelonian), then Long-Armed Chariot; exit via the devices to the north.' }, { title = 'Boss strategy', note = '• Chariots keep one facing, turning to their target only around TP moves; melee from sides or rear. Final chariots are immune to Sleep, Bind and Gravity.\n• Battleclad Chariot (Zhayolm): -25% physical and ranged damage taken, high defense, heavy hits. Fight with magic: Praecipitatio for every mage, skillchains for magic bursts. Tank needs at least Incus, Castellanus, Cumulus, Humilus.\n• Armored Chariot (Arrapago): simplest; melee it.\n• Long-Bowed Chariot (Bhaflau): high attack and Regain, so frequent TP moves. Kill the floor 4 chariot first, spread out, keep a fully celled healer.\n• Long-Armed Chariot (Silver Sea): standard hard fight; fully cell the party before opening its room.\n• Archaic Ramparts: add roughly every 15 seconds, briefly close every 30 seconds. Damage the rampart; one player holds adds.\n• Poroggo Madames can\'t be silenced; the current day\'s element does nothing to them.' }, { title = 'Rewards', note = '• Each chariot drops two Salvage armor pieces per kill from its Remnants\' list, plus the fixed drops above. Ghanraam turns three pieces + 10 Imperial Gold Pieces into a set piece (Ares\', Skadi\'s, Usukane, Marduk\'s, Morrigan\'s).\n• Final chariots: one Salvage II piece 60%, a second 25%, and always 3-5 design plan copies; Mrohk Sahjuuli makes +1 pieces.\n• Titles: Battleclad = Star Charioteer, Armored = Sun Charioteer, Long-Bowed = Comet Charioteer, Long-Armed = Moon Charioteer; all four required for An Imperial Heist (first Mythic weapon quest).\n• Alexandrite (for Mythic weapons) drops from Archaic Gears, Gear, Ramparts and Chariots in every Remnants.\n• Some chariots also drop a Cotton or Linen Coin Purse.\n• All NMs here (chariots, gears, ramparts, Madames, Slot and Socket NMs) roll the server\'s upgrade material table; see Endgame materials.' } } },
    { name = 'Guide: Sea: the Jailers and Absolute Virtue', group = 'Server', desc = 'Sea endgame route: take Virtues and Deeds from Jailers and Ix\'aern in Hu\'Xzoi and Ru\'Hmet, pop the Al\'Taieu Jailers, then Jailer of Love and Absolute Virtue. Source: https://vanadreams.org/wiki/#guide-c_endgame_sea', steps = { { title = 'Overview', note = '• Zones: Al\'Taieu, Grand Palace of Hu\'Xzoi, The Garden of Ru\'Hmet.\n• Flow: three Jailers and three Ix\'aern give Virtues and Deeds; combine with an H.Q. organ from Al\'Taieu to pop the three Al\'Taieu Jailers; their Virtues pop Jailer of Love, then Absolute Virtue appears.' }, { title = 'Getting in', note = '• Al\'Taieu: complete Chains of Promathia through The Warrior\'s Path; afterwards Sueleen in Sealion\'s Den sends you on request. Auroral Updrafts take you back down. Al\'Taieu has three home points.\n• Grand Palace of Hu\'Xzoi: unlocked in Garden of Antiquity by killing the three Ru\'aern each Rubious Crystal calls; the gate stays open after the mission.\n• The Garden of Ru\'Hmet: via the Gate of the Gods at the palace\'s far end.\n• No party limit; bring an alliance for Love and Absolute Virtue.\n• No time limits or lockouts in the open zones; Absolute Virtue despawns two hours after Jailer of Love spawns.\n• Trusts allowed in all three zones, normal six per party; in an alliance each party leader calls their own.\n• A ??? is usable again shortly after its NM despawns; every placeholder kill pops its NM.' }, { title = 'The route', note = '• 1. Hu\'Xzoi: Jailer of Temperance for the First Virtue.\n• 2. Hu\'Xzoi: Ix\'aern (MNK) for the Deed of Placidity.\n• 3. Ru\'Hmet: Jailer of Fortitude for the Second Virtue.\n• 4. Ru\'Hmet: Jailer of Faith for the Third Virtue.\n• 5. Ru\'Hmet: Ix\'aern (DRK) for the Deed of Moderation.\n• 6. Ru\'Hmet: Ix\'aern (DRG) for the Deed of Sensibility.\n• 7. Al\'Taieu D-9: Jailer of Hope for the Fifth Virtue.\n• 8. Al\'Taieu F-11: Jailer of Justice for the Fourth Virtue.\n• 9. Al\'Taieu L-8: Jailer of Prudence for the Sixth Virtue.\n• 10. Al\'Taieu K-12: Jailer of Love, then Absolute Virtue.' }, { title = 'The Al\'Taieu Jailers', note = '• Trade all three items at once to the Jailer\'s ???; they are consumed.\n• Jailer of Hope (D-9): First Virtue + Deed of Placidity + H.Q. Phuabo Organ.\n• Jailer of Justice (F-11): Second Virtue + Deed of Moderation + H.Q. Xzomit Organ.\n• Jailer of Prudence (L-8): Third Virtue + Deed of Sensibility + H.Q. Hpemde Organ.\n• Jailer of Love (K-12): Fourth, Fifth and Sixth Virtue only.\n• Absolute Virtue: no trade; it spawns where Love died 10 seconds after Love\'s death, claimed by whoever had the most hate.' }, { title = 'Palace and garden', note = '• Jailer of Temperance: kill stationary (non-patrolling) Eozdei on Hu\'Xzoi\'s first map, e.g. at J-13; the Jailer spawns where one dies, claimed to its killer.\n• Ix\'aern (MNK): trade H.Q. Aern Organs to the ??? in Hu\'Xzoi Map 2 (G-7 or I-7, alternating after each fight). 1 organ: 33% drop, no helpers; 2: 66%, Qn\'aern (RDM); 3: 100%, Qn\'aern (RDM) and Qn\'aern (WHM).\n• Ix\'aern (MNK) drop: usually Deed of Placidity, sometimes Vice of Antipathy.\n• Jailer of Fortitude: trade 12 Ghrah M Chips to its ??? at one of five tower spots in Ru\'Hmet (moves after each fight); spawns with Kf\'ghrah (WHM) and Kf\'ghrah (BLM).\n• Jailer of Faith: trade one H.Q. Euvhi Organ to its ??? at one of five spots on Ru\'Hmet\'s second map (starts at F-11); moves after each fight and occasionally by itself.\n• Ix\'aern (DRK): kill the Aw\'aern next to its ??? (near Map 1 F-12; rotates among four spots). On a \'sheer animosity\' message, click the ??? within ten minutes to spawn it with two Qn\'aern (RNG). Drop: usually Deed of Moderation, sometimes Vice of Avarice.\n• Ix\'aern (DRG): one Aw\'aern among the four groups in Ru\'Hmet\'s Aw\'aern room is its hidden placeholder; when it dies, Ix\'aern (DRG) spawns unclaimed in a room corner. Drop: Deed of Sensibility or Vice of Aspersion.' }, { title = 'Farming the pop items', note = '• H.Q. Phuabo Organ: Ul\'phuabo (rare), Om\'phuabo (very rare), Al\'Taieu.\n• H.Q. Xzomit Organ: Om\'xzomit and Ul\'xzomit, Al\'Taieu.\n• H.Q. Hpemde Organ: Om\'hpemde and Ul\'hpemde, Al\'Taieu.\n• H.Q. Euvhi Organ: Aw\'euvhi in Al\'Taieu and Ru\'Hmet (rare).\n• H.Q. Aern Organ: Aern in Hu\'Xzoi (rare).\n• Ghrah M Chip: Aw\'ghrah in Ru\'Hmet (very rare; 12 needed).\n• Ul\' types cluster in south Al\'Taieu (F-12 to J-13); Om\' types roam the north and edges.\n• Shortcut: Login Moogle (Pop items page) sells every Virtue, all three Deeds, each H.Q. organ above and the Ghrah M Chip for 500 points each; the Clan Provisioner sells them for 1,000 clan points each.\n• Buying all six Virtues skips to the Al\'Taieu Jailers; buying the Fourth, Fifth and Sixth skips to Love.' }, { title = 'Fight notes: palace and garden', note = '• Jailer of Temperance (25,000 HP): immune to magic. Rotates forms: pot = hand-to-hand and blunt only, poles = piercing only, rings = slashing only; bring mixed weapons and swap attackers. At 65-70% and 35-40% it uses Meikyo Shisui plus six consecutive moves.\n• Ix\'aern (MNK) (13,000 HP): once any of the three is under 60%, all use Hundred Fists and hit much harder. Kill order: Qn\'aern (WHM) (uses Benediction), then RDM, then Ix\'aern; helpers despawn when it dies.\n• Jailer of Fortitude (25,000 HP): near-immune to physical, half damage from ranged. While either Kf\'ghrah lives, spells landing on it are reflected to the caster. Kill both Kf\'ghrah (9,000 HP each) first, then nuke. Under 50% it goes invincible every 150 seconds. Kf\'ghrah change shape together every 45 seconds: balls only cast, spiders and birds melee.\n• Jailer of Faith (25,000 HP): flower closed (one minute) = double damage dealt and less taken; open (three minutes) = takes more. Save weapon skills and nukes for open. Manafont at 75, 50 and 25%, casting Quake II only then; also Slowga and Breakga; gains TP from its own nukes.\n• Ix\'aern (DRK) (21,000 HP): kill both Qn\'aern (RNG) first. On death it may reraise at full HP 9 seconds later: 90% with both Qn\'aern alive, 60% with one, 30% with none. Casts Absorb spells, uses Blood Weapon early.\n• Ix\'aern (DRG) (15,000 HP): three Wynavs join 20 seconds in and breathe every time it readies a move; a slain Wynav respawns after 10 seconds. Bracelets on for 30 of each 80 seconds (more attack, accuracy, speed). Wynavs cast Lullaby, Requiem and Elegy and can use Soul Voice; put them to sleep or kite them while the party focuses down the Ix\'aern.' }, { title = 'Fight notes: Al\'Taieu Jailers', note = '• Jailer of Hope (29,200 HP): immune to stun and sleep; melee often stuns. Mighty Strikes near the start and every 90 seconds. Aerial Collision, Spine Lash and Tidal Dive often double up. After Plasma Charge it casts lightning nukes for a minute. Use shadows and a high-HP tank.\n• Jailer of Justice (37,000 HP): calls a Qn\'xzomit every 30 seconds (max six), charms someone every 150 seconds, uses Familiar on pets at 50%. Qn\'xzomit use Mijin Gakure at 20% HP; kill them quickly or keep them from healers. Sleep or kite adds and burn the Jailer.\n• Jailer of Prudence (two, 20,000 HP each): one copies the other\'s weapon skills. Both use Perfect Dodge at 95% and every two minutes; during it one can teleport to its new target. Only the second to die drops loot; the survivor then triple attacks every swing with doubled attack. Lower both evenly and finish them close together.\n• Jailer of Love (57,000 HP): draws in anyone beyond 20 yalms; strong regen, half magic damage. Every 150 seconds calls three pets in fixed order (Qn\'xzomit, Qn\'hpemde, Ru\'phuabo, repeat, then Qn\'xzomit and Qn\'hpemde); from wave ten it drops Ru\'phuabo on its target.\n• Love: killing all nine Qn\'xzomit and all nine Qn\'hpemde stops its regen and raises its magic damage taken. Absorbs and nukes one element at a time, switching each minute. At 45-55% uses Astral Flow and all pets use their strongest move together.\n• Absolute Virtue (66,000 HP): high attack, defence, magic defence, fast cast; regen grows unless all eighteen of Love\'s pets were killed. Uses a two-hour ability every 45-90 seconds.\n• AV: within 15 yalms, use the same two-hour within three seconds of its use to remove it for the fight (Call Wyvern also removes Familiar and Astral Flow). Under 60% bracelets make it much stronger and two-hours come in combinations. Meteor hits everyone within 30 yalms. Bring many two-hour jobs, assign responses, and kill all Love pets first.' }, { title = 'Rewards', note = '• Each Jailer always drops its weapon: Hope Staff, Justice Sword, Prudence Rod, Temperance Axe, Faith Baghnakhs, Fortitude Axe, Love Halberd; each also has a chance at its torque.\n• Jailer of Love also drops Aura of Adulation and Aura of Voracity.\n• Absolute Virtue: three Sins every kill, chance at the rest.\n• Meret (Tavnazian Safehold), after In the Name of Science, exchanges one item per trade: Vice of Antipathy = Merciful Cape; Vice of Avarice = Altruistic Cape; Vice of Aspersion = Astute Cape; Aura of Adulation = Novio Earring; Aura of Voracity = Novia Earring.\n• Sins: Invidiousness = Raphael\'s Rod; Insolence = Mars\'s Ring; Infatuation = Bellona\'s Ring; Intemperance = Minerva\'s Ring; Indignation = Ninurta\'s Sash; Indolence = Aureole; Indulgence = Futsuno Mitama.\n• Every Jailer, all three Ix\'aern and Absolute Virtue roll endgame upgrade materials at 10x the normal rate.\n• Each party member in the zone gets currency: any Jailer = 17 Escha beads + 3,890 Gallimaufry, plus a 6.94% Divergence void for the killer\'s job; Absolute Virtue = 50 Escha beads + 11,670 Gallimaufry, plus Voracious Psyche every time and a 20.83% Divergence void for the killer\'s job.\n• Full drop tables are on each NM\'s page.' } } },
    { name = 'Guide: Seal orb battlefields (BCNM and KSNM)', group = 'Server', desc = 'Seals drop from monsters and buy orbs from Shami, which open level-capped or uncapped battlefields. Source: https://vanadreams.org/wiki/#guide-c_seal_orb_battlefields', steps = { { title = 'Getting an orb', note = '• Seals drop from any non-NM mob that is not Too Weak for the party\'s top-level member; limit one seal per party per 5 minutes.\n• Beastmen\'s Seal: mob levels 1-69. Kindred\'s Seal: 50+. Kindred\'s Crest: 70+.\n• Seals are untradeable and can\'t be sold or auctioned; trade them to Shami, Port Jeuno (-54, 0, 11), to bank them, then talk to him for orbs.\n• Greeter Moogle (Port San d\'Oria, Port Bastok, Windurst Walls) sells any seal for 10 Login Points (Moon Orb = 600 points).\n• At 99, Beastmen\'s and Kindred\'s Seals stop dropping (mobs Too Weak); use Login Points, Level Sync, or a lower-level character.\n• Cloudy Orb: 20 Beastmen\'s Seals, cap 20 (Wings of Fury, Shooting Fish, Crustacean Conundrum, Charming Trio).\n• Sky Orb: 30 Beastmen\'s, cap 30 (Petrifying Pair, Toadal Recall, Carapace Combatants, Dropping Like Flies, Birds of a Feather, Grove Guardians, Let Sleeping Dogs Die, Die by the Sword, Creeping Doom, Harem Scarem).\n• Star Orb: 40 Beastmen\'s, cap 40 (Tails of Woe, Under Observation, Royal Jelly, The Worm\'s Turn, Undying Promise, Factory Rejects, Steamed Sprouts, Royal Succession).\n• Comet Orb: 50 Beastmen\'s, cap 50 (Hostile Herbivores, Eye of the Tiger, 3, 2, 1..., The Final Bout, An Awful Autopsy, Idol Thoughts, Rapid Raptors, Treasure and Tribulations).\n• Moon Orb: 60 Beastmen\'s, cap 60 (Dismemberment Brigade, Shots in the Dark, Grimshell Shocktroopers, Up in Arms, Celery, Demolition Squad, Brothers D\'Aurphe, Legion XI Comitatensis, Jungle Boogymen, Amphibian Assault, Divine Punishers, Wild Wild Whiskers).\n• Clotho Orb: 30 Kindred\'s, no cap (Double Dragonian, Copycat, Come Into My Parlor, Cactuar Suave, Season\'s Greetings).\n• Lachesis Orb: 30 Kindred\'s, no cap (Today\'s Horoscope, Operation Desert Swarm, E-vase-ive Action, Eye of the Storm, Royale Ramble).\n• Atropos Orb: 30 Kindred\'s, no cap (Contaminated Colosseum, Prehistoric Pigeons, Infernal Swarm, The Scarlet King, Moa Constrictors).\n• Themis Orb: 99 Kindred\'s, no cap, up to 18 players (Horns of War, The Hills are Alive, Early Bird Catches the Wyrm).' }, { title = 'Entering', note = '• Put the orb in main inventory (not wardrobe, satchel or sack).\n• Trade it to the arena\'s Burning Circle and choose the fight; the party goes in with you.\n• The orb cracks on entry and is single-use; Shami disposes of cracked orbs.' }, { title = 'Up in Arms (Kraken Club)', note = '• Waughroon Shrine (via Palborough Mines); Moon Orb; cap 60, 3 players, 15 minutes.\n• Boss Fe\'e has six tentacles; each one lost slows its attacks and lowers its TP gain; with none left, Ink Jet becomes its regular attack.\n• Rewards: 15,000 gil shared, Black Pearl, 2 Pearls, 3 Oxblood, Teleport Ring (Altep or Dem), one of Ajari Bead Necklace / Philomath Stole / Walkure Mask; possible gem, ore, log or craft material; small chance of Hi-Reraiser or Vile Elixir +1.\n• Kraken Club: roughly 1 in 2,000 wins.' }, { title = 'Drop rates', note = '• Rare battlefield drops use the server\'s raised monster drop rate; guaranteed rewards (gil, fixed spoils) are not changed.' } } },
    { name = 'Guide: Server rates: EXP, capacity points and drops', group = 'Server', desc = 'Default-mode rates for EXP, capacity points, drops and monster strength on Vanadreams. Source: https://vanadreams.org/wiki/#guide-c_server_rates', steps = { { title = 'Overview', note = '• Default mode uses standard EXP and drop rates with some exceptions below.\n• Classic mode is also standard EXP; Moogle Mode (faster rates) is live — see Rates and modes.' }, { title = 'Experience and Records of Eminence', note = '• Monster EXP/limit points, quest/mission EXP, FoV/GoV page EXP, RoE EXP and sparks: standard.\n• FoV/GoV tabs: 20x.\n• RoE Unity accolades: 2x.\n• Capacity points from all sources: 10x; all capacity bonuses (chains, Corsair\'s Roll, Kupofried, Capacity/Trizek/Endorsement/Facility/Vocation rings, gifts) stack on top.' }, { title = 'Drops and treasure', note = '• Monster item drops: standard.\n• Treasure Casket from about 1 in 2 regular monsters.\n• Bayld from quests, Reives and Coalition Assignments: 3x.' }, { title = 'Monsters', note = '• Regular: +15% HP, +20% base stats.\n• NMs and bosses: +10% HP, +10% base stats.\n• Abyssea regulars: an additional 1.5x HP over the +15%, stats +20%.' }, { title = 'Healing and damage', note = '• See Player damage rates and TP gain.\n• Rates before 22 October 2026: monster EXP 3x, other EXP and RoE 1.33x, capacity 50x, drops 5x, caskets about 1 in 5.' } } },
    { name = 'Guide: Shades of the Lost: playing as a Fomor', group = 'Server', desc = 'Unlock a full-body Fomor appearance that other players see by obtaining a Swift Belt for the Stylist Moogle. Source: https://vanadreams.org/wiki/#guide-c_fomor_look_at_creation', steps = { { title = 'Overview', note = '• Go to the Stylist Moogle at the bazaar hangout (!hangout) and choose A whole Fomor body; she requires a Swift Belt.\n• Kill Fomors in Lufaise Meadows, Misareaux Coast, Phomiuna Aqueducts or the Sacrarium to raise Fomor hate; other monsters there lower it. Resauchamet in Tavnazian Safehold reports your hate level.\n• Obtain a Fomor Codex from tauri in Phomiuna Aqueducts or the Sacrarium.\n• Once hate is high enough (the Stale Draft urges you to leave fast), trade the Codex to your race\'s Stale Draft in the Sacrarium.\n• Defeat the NM that spawns — Balor (Hume), Luaith (Elvaan), Lobais (Tarutaru), Caithleann (Mithra), Indich (Galka) — for the Swift Belt.\n• Trade the Swift Belt to the Stylist Moogle; the guises are permanent.\n• Unlocks: Fomor face and all Fomor bodies — WAR, MNK, SMN, BLM, RDM, THF, PLD, DRK, BST, BRD, RNG, SAM, NIN, DRG (some with a Lufaise variant), Sacrarium Balor/Luaith/Lobais, plus Wajaom Woodlands and Bhaflau Thickets Fomors; any look regardless of job or race.\n• The body persists through gear changes, zoning and logout; gear still functions but is hidden.\n• NPC interaction still works; costumes display over it until they expire; character select shows your normal look.\n• To revert: Stylist Moogle, My own body back, or choose any face.' } } },
    { name = 'Guide: Skillchains and magic bursts', group = 'Server', desc = 'Skillchain timing, combinations, damage multipliers, magic burst rules, and Aeonic Radiance/Umbra on Vanadreams. Source: https://vanadreams.org/wiki/#guide-c_skillchains', steps = { { title = 'Making a skillchain', note = '• An opening weapon skill starts a 10-second window holding all of its properties (max three).\n• A matching weapon skill landing 3+ seconds later, still inside the window, closes it.\n• Each closed chain opens a new window 1 second shorter, allowing continuation.\n• A non-matching weapon skill restarts a fresh 10-second window.' }, { title = 'Combinations (opener, then closer)', note = '• Level 1: Transfixion+Compression=Compression; Transfixion+Reverberation=Reverberation; Compression+Transfixion=Transfixion; Compression+Detonation=Detonation; Liquefaction+Scission=Scission; Scission+Liquefaction=Liquefaction; Scission+Reverberation=Reverberation; Scission+Detonation=Detonation; Reverberation+Induration=Induration; Reverberation+Impaction=Impaction; Detonation+Scission=Scission; Induration+Compression=Compression; Induration+Impaction=Impaction; Impaction+Liquefaction=Liquefaction; Impaction+Detonation=Detonation.\n• Level 2: Transfixion+Scission=Distortion; Liquefaction+Impaction=Fusion; Detonation+Compression=Gravitation; Induration+Reverberation=Fragmentation; Gravitation+Fragmentation=Fragmentation; Distortion+Fusion=Fusion; Fusion+Gravitation=Gravitation; Fragmentation+Distortion=Distortion.\n• Level 3: Gravitation+Distortion or Distortion+Gravitation=Darkness; Fusion+Fragmentation or Fragmentation+Fusion=Light.\n• Level 4: Light+Light=Light (lv4); Darkness+Darkness=Darkness (lv4).' }, { title = 'Skillchain damage', note = '• Damage = closing weapon skill damage x multiplier by level and chain step (1st/2nd/3rd/4th/5th/6th+):\n• Lv1: 0.50/0.60/0.70/0.80/0.90/1.00.\n• Lv2: 0.60/0.75/1.00/1.25/1.50/1.75.\n• Lv3 (Light, Darkness): 1.00/1.50/1.75/2.00/2.25/2.50.\n• Lv4 (incl. Radiance, Umbra): 1.50/1.80/2.10/2.40/2.70/3.00.\n• Multi-element chains use the element the target resists least; that resistance, skillchain bonus gear, day/weather, elemental staves and affinity, Innin (from behind only) and Sengikori all modify damage.' }, { title = 'Magic bursts', note = '• Cast a matching-element spell within the window to burst.\n• Transfixion: Light. Compression: Dark. Liquefaction: Fire. Scission: Earth. Reverberation: Water. Detonation: Wind. Induration: Ice. Impaction: Thunder.\n• Gravitation: Dark, Earth. Distortion: Water, Ice. Fusion: Light, Fire. Fragmentation: Wind, Thunder.\n• Light: Light, Fire, Wind, Thunder. Darkness: Dark, Earth, Water, Ice.\n• Base burst x1.30, plus a bonus scaling with low resistance (+85% vs neutral).\n• Chain-step bonus: +5% at step 1, then +10% per step, max +70% at step 8.\n• Gear and merit burst bonus caps at +40%; job points, Geomancer cardinal chant and Evolith go beyond the cap.\n• Trusts, pets and monsters receive the same step bonus.' }, { title = 'Aeonic weapons, Radiance and Umbra', note = '• Aeonic weapons (from Oboro) add Light or Darkness to their weapon skill while Aeonic Aftermath is active (not on the WS that triggers the Aftermath).\n• Light: Godhands (Shijin Spiral), Lionheart (Resolution), Chango (Upheaval), Heishi Shorinken (Blade: Shun), Dojikiri Yasutsuna (Tachi: Shoha), Tishtrya (Realmrazer), Fail-Not (Apex Arrow), Fomalhaut (Last Stand), Aeneas (Exenterator).\n• Darkness: Tri-edge (Ruinator), Anguta (Entropy), Trishula (Stardiver), Khatvanga (Shattersoul), Sequence (Requiescat).\n• Aeonic Aftermath: 3 minutes; Skillchain Bonus and Magic Burst Bonus (not subject to the 40% cap) by TP spent: <1,500 +3%; 1,500-1,999 +4%; 2,000-2,999 +5% to +9%; 3,000 +10%.\n• Closing a level 4 Light/Darkness with Aftermath up makes Radiance/Umbra if the chain had enough weapon skills: Aftermath lv3 needs 2, lv2 needs 3, lv1 needs 4.\n• Radiance/Umbra use the lv4 damage row and consume the Aftermath.' }, { title = 'Skillchaining with trusts', note = '• Most trusts fire weapon skills immediately, so their chains are random.\n• Ayame saves TP to open; Gessho and Maat save TP to close.\n• Combine an opener and a closer, plus a nuker like Shantotto to burst.' } } },
    { name = 'Guide: Skirmish', group = 'Server', desc = 'Seekers of Adoulin endgame for 1-6 players at level 95+: build a simulacrum, enter a private [U] zone, and complete objectives for coffers. No level sync; trusts allowed; tough at item level 119. Source: https://vanadreams.org/wiki/#guide-c_skirmish', steps = { { title = 'Building a simulacrum', note = '• Oston is at the Goddess\'s Tears café, Eastern Adoulin (G-8), next to Lola.\n• Trade him one Visage, one Faithful\'s Torso and one Faithful\'s Legs for a Rala, Cirdas or Yorcia Simulacrum (the Visage sets the area).\n• Fee: 100 gil per total rank (e.g. Visage III + Torso II + Legs I = 600 gil).\n• One simulacrum per area may be held.\n• Talking to Oston cycles offers: talk again immediately to accept, or wait a few seconds for the next.\n• He disassembles a simulacrum free (needs 3 free slots).\n• Rank I segments for Obsidian Fragments: Rala or Cirdas Visage I 2,600; Yorcia Visage I 3,900; Faithful\'s Torso I 2,400; Faithful\'s Legs I 2,000.\n• Higher ranks come from other content, e.g. Mog Kupons at the Dealer Moogle.' }, { title = 'What each segment does', note = '• Visage: area and stone grade (III-IV may give +1; V may give +1 and +2).\n• Torso: time limit, objective size, open maps (Rala/Cirdas), reward count.\n• Legs: number of Noetic Ascensions (rank + 2) and their blessings.\n• Lola gives one Skirmish tip per conversation.' }, { title = 'Entering', note = '• Leader examines the Augural Conveyor holding the simulacrum, then examines again right away to depart.\n• Conveyors: Rala Waterways (B-6, near the Western Adoulin zone line), Cirdas Caverns (H-3), Yorcia Weald (I-10).\n• Rala\'s conveyor also leads to mission battle "The Charlatan"; each examine names one destination — re-examine at once to go, or wait and examine to hear the other.\n• Only the leader\'s simulacrum is consumed; all level 95+ party members in the zone enter.' }, { title = 'How a run works', note = '• Objective 1 is required and grants everyone a temporary Fenestral Key; progress is announced every 20%.\n• Optional Objective 2 adds one item per personal coffer and one more pool piece.\n• Using the key: monsters leave, KO\'d players get a raise offer, 6 minutes remain, and a named Treasure Coffer appears per player; the first coffer opened fills the pool with weapons/armour.\n• If time expires before the key is used, you leave with nothing.\n• Noetic Ascensions: single use; cycle blessings by waiting and re-examining, take one by re-examining at once; each blessing once per run, party-wide, lasts the run.\n• Blessings by Legs: I Attack/Defense up; II Magic Attack/Magic Defense up; III full TP, full HP/MP; IV Max HP +500, Max MP up; V movement speed.\n• Each monster gives each player 1-5 Obsidian Fragments; Rala NMs and Yorcia Bestial Dens give 10-50.' }, { title = 'Rala Waterways [U]: defeat the notorious monsters', note = '• Torso I: 30 min, 3 maps, Obj1 6 NMs, Obj2 8, 3 personal items, 2 pool weapons.\n• II: 40 min, 4 maps, 7/10, 4, 3. III: 50 min, 4, 8/11, 5, 4. IV: 60 min, 4, 9/13, 6, 5. V: 60 min, 5, 10/15, 7, 6.\n• NMs around the Water Garden Coliseum: Aquifer Leech, Deft Eft, Coreborn Spider, Anklebiter Slug, Ergoprowler, Bonesoaked Bandit, Warmonger and Sorcerer, Bufobrawler, Batroika, Combustible Gel, Citrine Slime, Slashmaw Pugil, Diremite Assailant, Watermarked Crab.\n• Map 1 open at start; each next map needs two more NM kills.\n• Torso III+: map 3 also needs six ordinary monster kills. Torso IV+: map 4 also needs three blessings taken (two with Legs I).\n• Ordinary monsters respawn after one minute.\n• Torso V clear: title Waterway Exemplar.' }, { title = 'Cirdas Caverns [U]: defeat a number of monsters', note = '• Torso I: 30 min, 3 maps, Obj1 50 kills, Obj2 55, 3 items, 2 pool weapons.\n• II: 40 min, 3, 60/66, 4, 3. III: 50 min, 3, 70/77, 5, 4. IV: 60 min, 4, 80/88, 6, 5. V: 60 min, 4, 90/100, 7, 6.\n• Monsters respawn within seconds and some kills spawn extras.\n• All monsters have true sight (Sneak/Invisible useless).\n• Families: bats, acuex, funguar, obdella, umbril, worms, clots, mandragora, spiders, lizards, toads, a marolith.\n• Torso V clear: title Cavern Exemplar.' }, { title = 'Yorcia Weald [U]: defend the Cantonment', note = '• Torso I: 30 min, hold 15 min (Obj1) / 25 min (Obj2), 3 items, 2 pool armour. II: same times, 4, 3.\n• III: 40 min, 25/35, 5, 4. IV: 40 min, 25/35, 6, 5. V: 50 min, 35/45, 7, 6.\n• The Cantonment can\'t be healed; you\'re warned on each hit; if destroyed the run fails.\n• Waves march at the Cantonment and ignore players unless attacked.\n• Bestial Dens (flowers at the edges) each supply 2-3 families; destroying one stops them; dens don\'t fight.\n• Extra blessings: Stockades (Torso rank + Legs rank - 1, max 4, attacked first) and Halve the time (only in the first 3 minutes).\n• After Objective 2 a horde attacks; use the key.\n• Dithering Heartwing: kill before Objective 1 for one extra pool armour; always drops a Lebondopt Wing.\n• Torso V clear: title Weald Exemplar.' }, { title = 'Treasure pool (from the first coffer opened)', note = '• Rala: Crobaci, Faizzeer, Iclamar, Kannakiri, Aedold, Hgafircian, Lehbrailg.\n• Cirdas: Ninzas, Leisilonu, Iztaasu, Iizamal, Qatsunoci, Shichishito, Uffrat, Bocluamni.\n• Yorcia: Cizin, Otronif, Iuitl, Gendewitha, Hagondes sets (head-feet) and Beatific Shield.' }, { title = 'Personal coffers', note = '• Stones: Ghastly (Rala, Cirdas), Verdigris (Yorcia); better Visages add +1/+2.\n• -ra II scrolls (Fira II, Blizzara II, Aera II, Stonera II, Thundara II, Watera II); Indi- plates (Vex, Frailty, Wilt, Gravity, Malaise, Fade).\n• Elemental beads, dragon meat, orichalcum and thokcha ingots, dragon blood.\n• Eudaemon Blade, Cape, Ring, Sash, Shield.\n• Yorcia only: Lebondopt Wings, small chance of Vial of Translurry key item.' }, { title = 'Lola\'s exchanges', note = '• Lebondopt Wings for unowned Yorcia gear: 1 = hands/feet; 2 = head/legs; 3 = body or Beatific Shield.\n• Pulchridopt Wings (trade the exact count; re-talk at once to accept, wait for the next offer): 1 = Vial of Translurry or Wailing Stone +1; 3 = Rala or Cirdas Simulacrum (Visage I, Torso I, Legs I); 6 = Vial of Transmelange or Yorcia Simulacrum; 10 = Wailing Stone +2.\n• 5 Lebondopt Wings convert to 1 Pulchridopt Wing.' }, { title = 'Ornery Dhole\'s stones', note = '• Western Adoulin, Inventors\' Coalition; sells stones for Obsidian Fragments, one offer per talk.\n• Ghastly Stone 50 / +1 100 / +2 500. Verdigris Stone 100 / 200 / 1,000. Wailing Stone 200 / 400 / 2,000.\n• Trade same-type stones for two options: sell back at one fifth of price, or convert 5 into 1 of the next grade.' }, { title = 'Augmenting Skirmish gear', note = '• Trade Divainy-Gamainy (Inventors\' Coalition, Western Adoulin) one item plus one stone; talk at once to proceed. Cost: the stone + 500 Bayld; old augments are replaced.\n• Ghastly: Rala/Cirdas weapons. Verdigris: +1 weapons and Yorcia armour.\n• Weapons always gain DMG plus 1-2 fitting stats (e.g. Ninzas STR/DEX; Lehbrailg INT/MND/Magic Attack Bonus); armour gains 2-3.\n• +1 and +2 stones raise maximum values; Verdigris caps higher than Ghastly.' }, { title = 'Transmuting to +1 and +2', note = '• Trade Divainy-Gamainy the item alone while holding the key item; talk at once to proceed. Costs 5,000 Bayld and the key item; augments are lost.\n• Rala/Cirdas weapon + Vial of Translurry = +1 weapon (item level 113).\n• +1 weapon + Vial of Transmelange = +2 weapon (item level 119).\n• Yorcia armour (Cizin, Otronif, Iuitl, Gendewitha, Hagondes pieces, Beatific Shield) + Vial of Transmelange = +1 piece (item level 119).\n• Vial of Translurry: Lola for 1 Pulchridopt Wing, or occasional Yorcia Weald [U] clear. Vial of Transmelange: Lola for 6 Pulchridopt Wings.\n• Hold max one of each vial.' }, { title = 'Alluvion Skirmish', note = '• With a Eudaemon part (Blade, Cape, Ring, Sash or Shield), Lola and Oston combine it with simulacrum segments into a Eudaemon.\n• The Eudaemon opens Alluvion Skirmish at the same conveyors: floors with Mistmaw guarding Alluvion weapons (Rala, Cirdas) and a lane battle for Alluvion armour (Yorcia). See Alluvion Skirmish.' } } },
    { name = 'Guide: Sky: the four gods and Kirin', group = 'Server', desc = 'Farm eight lesser NMs in Sky for gems and stones, pop the four gods for their seals, then trade the seals to summon Kirin. Source: https://vanadreams.org/wiki/#guide-c_endgame_sky', steps = { { title = 'Getting in', note = '• Areas: Ru\'Aun Gardens, Ve\'Lugannon Palace, The Shrine of Ru\'Avitau, reached via the Shimmering Circle in Hall of the Gods.\n• Requires Rise of the Zilart mission The Gate of the Gods (current or completed); first arrival in Ru\'Aun Gardens completes it.\n• Palace and Shrine connect to Ru\'Aun Gardens through normal doors; no key item.\n• No party limit, time limit or lockout; trusts allowed (max six per party; each party leader calls their own).\n• All NMs respawn ~30 seconds after death; placeholders always pop their NM; a god\'s ??? resets right after the god despawns.\n• Pincerstones open blue portals for 2 minutes; a god\'s yellow island portal closes while that god is up; Warrior of the Crystal title holders can use green portal shortcuts.\n• Home points: five in Ru\'Aun Gardens, one in the Shrine.' }, { title = 'The route', note = '• 1. Ru\'Aun Gardens (H-9/H-10): kill Groundskeepers until Despot pops for Gem of the West.\n• 2. Ve\'Lugannon Palace Map 1: Steam Cleaner (Gem of the East), Zipacna (Gem of the North), Brigandish Blade (Gem of the South).\n• 3. Shrine of Ru\'Avitau Maps 4-5: Mother Globe (Springstone), Faust (Summerstone), Olla Grande (Winterstone), Ullikummi (Autumnstone).\n• 4. Ru\'Aun Gardens god islands: Genbu, Seiryu, Byakko, Suzaku for their seals.\n• 5. Shrine Map 6: Kirin.\n• Lesser NMs and gods always drop their item, sometimes two; one full loop of eight NMs and four gods yields one Kirin.' }, { title = 'Pop the gods', note = '• Trade exactly the gem and stone to the god\'s ??? on its island; the god spawns there.\n• Genbu: Gem of the North + Winterstone, J-5.\n• Seiryu: Gem of the East + Springstone, L-8.\n• Byakko: Gem of the West + Autumnstone, E-5.\n• Suzaku: Gem of the South + Summerstone, E-9.' }, { title = 'Pop Kirin', note = '• Trade Seal of Genbu, Seal of Seiryu, Seal of Byakko and Seal of Suzaku to the ??? at Shrine Map 6 F-9; Kirin spawns claimed to you.' }, { title = 'Gem and stone NMs', note = '• Despot: pops where a Groundskeeper dies in the central garden (H-9, H-10, J-8 area), claimed to that killer.\n• Steam Cleaner: engage a Detector in the Palace; it summons a helper every 10 seconds, which is Steam Cleaner if not already up.\n• Zipacna: patrols Map 1\'s north corridor (~F-4), turning at closed doors; up on arrival.\n• Brigandish Blade: trade a Curtana to the ??? at Map 1 H-12.\n• Mother Globe: roams Map 5 (~J-9) with up to six Slave Globes.\n• Faust: on its ledge at Map 4 G-11.\n• Olla Grande: trade Ro\'Maeve Water to the ??? at Map 4 I-6; Olla Pequena, then Olla Media, then Olla Grande spawn in turn; only Grande drops the stone; trading under Sneak leaves Pequena unclaimed.\n• Ullikummi: trade a Diorite to the ??? at Map 5 G-9.' }, { title = 'Farming the pop items', note = '• Curtana: free from a ??? in one of the Palace\'s four corner rooms if you don\'t have one; it then relocates among 16 spots, hidden 2-3 hours.\n• Ro\'Maeve Water: rare from Aura Pots (Shrine Maps 3-4).\n• Diorite: very rare from Aura Statues (Shrine Maps 1, 5, 6).\n• Login Moogle Pop items page: every gem, stone, seal, Ro\'Maeve Water and Diorite for 500 points each.\n• Clan Provisioner: all of those plus Curtana for 1,000 clan points each.' }, { title = 'Lesser NM tactics', note = '• Despot: Panzerfaust only, 2-5 in a row; fast; immune to Slow and Sleep; tank at its spawn.\n• Steam Cleaner: melee drains 500-1,000 TP; use magic; hand-to-hand deals 25% more.\n• Brigandish Blade: invulnerable at 1% until a Buccaneer\'s Knife added effect lands (steal the knife from it with a Thief); attack rises as HP drops; hits can Terrorize.\n• Zipacna: frequent Crystal Rain and Crystal Weapon, quick TP; pull it away from doors.\n• Mother Globe: constant Shock Spikes, lightning added effect; kill or sleep Slave Globes (600 HP) first; they despawn with it.\n• Faust: Typhoon twice in a row, three times under 50%, with much faster TP under 50%; spread out.\n• Ollas: Pequena nukes; Media drains and dispels; Grande self-heals and casts Holy; all dispel on hit.\n• Ullikummi: near-constant Heavy Strike; use shadows and a solid tank.' }, { title = 'God tactics', note = '• All four are sleep-immune, have elemental added effects, and despawn after 5 minutes unengaged.\n• Throwing items cancel added effects: Genbu - Antarctic Wind (from Suzaku); Seiryu - Zephyr (from Byakko); Byakko - East Wind (from Seiryu); Suzaku - Arctic Wind (from Genbu).\n• Genbu (19,000 HP): attack rises as HP falls, counters, faster TP under 50%.\n• Seiryu (22,000 HP): very fast TP; Hundred Fists at 50-60% (no spells or moves during it).\n• Byakko (22,000 HP): frequent triple attack, high attack and defence.\n• Suzaku (25,000 HP): strongly resists fire and ice; use water nukes.' }, { title = 'Kirin tactics', note = '• 60,000 HP, regen, very fast TP, resists Stun; casts Stonega IV, Stone V, Quake, Rasp, Sleepga.\n• Each move twice in a row (three times under 50%): Heat Breath, Deadly Hold, Great Sandstorm or Great Whirlwind, Tail Swing or Tail Smash.\n• Summons one of the four gods (~10,000 HP each) every 3-5 minutes until all four are out; they link and despawn when Kirin dies.\n• One Astral Flow between 85% and 10%: random avatar (Carbuncle, Ifrit, Titan, Leviathan, Garuda, Shiva, Ramuh).\n• Setup: one tank for Kirin and one for the gods, strong healing with a healer free to wake Sleepga victims, and a group to kill each god; or burn Kirin before god 3 or 4.\n• Despawns with its gods after 3 minutes unengaged.' }, { title = 'Rewards', note = '• Kirin: Kirin\'s Osode, Kirin\'s Pole, Dryadic and Neptunal body abjurations, Wyrmal legs abjuration, high-end ingots and cloth.\n• Gods: Genbu\'s Kabuto, Genbu\'s Shield, Seiryu\'s Kote, Byakko\'s Haidate, Suzaku\'s Sune-Ate, each god\'s axe/sword/scythe, and a head/hands/legs/feet abjuration every time (chance of two).\n• Lesser NMs: Oblivion or Libation abjurations and a weapon each (Ushikirimaru, Shiranui, Tonbo-Giri, Skofnung, Ulfhedinn Axe, Indra Katars, Scarecrow Scythe).\n• Gods and Kirin roll the endgame materials list at 10x.\n• Per kill, each party member in zone: 13 Escha beads and 2,920 Gallimaufry (gods and Kirin).\n• Kirin also adds to the killer\'s pool: Voracious Psyche 25%; Divergence void for the killer\'s job 5.21%.\n• Full drop tables are on each NM\'s page.' } } },
    { name = 'Guide: Sortie: getting a +2 job earring', group = 'Server', desc = 'Sortie job earrings come from Old Cases: each holds a ??? Earring of a random job, which turns into that job\'s earring, stats pre-rolled, when used. Source: https://vanadreams.org/wiki/#guide-c_sortie_earrings_plus2', steps = { { title = 'Overview', note = '• Examples: Boii, Bhikku, Ebers, Wicce and Lethargy earrings.\n• The job is random, not tied to the job you are on; spare earrings can be traded to other characters on the same account.' }, { title = 'Which case gives which earring', note = '• Old Case: ??? Earring, occasionally +1.\n• Old Case +1: ??? Earring +1, occasionally +2.\n• Old Case +2: always ??? Earring +2.\n• An earring you own cannot be upgraded.' }, { title = 'Old Case +2: Subjugate: Aminon', note = '• Accept the Records of Eminence objective Subjugate: Aminon (listed with the Sortie boss objectives).\n• Gather Ra\'Kaznar Fragments #1 to #4 from the Sortie basement bosses.\n• Summon Aminon at the Diaphanous Gadget in sector E, west of the Flan room, and kill it.\n• Reward: Old Case +2, 1,000 sparks, 5,000 EXP, 100 accolades.\n• Once per character; with full bags it only completes after you free a slot and win again.' }, { title = 'Old Case and Old Case +1', note = '• Drop from Sortie chests, caskets, coffers and bosses; basement sources drop them more often.\n• Aminon always drops an Old Case +1 plus a Ra\'Kaz. Starstone.\n• Ruspix, Leafallia (H-8): Old Case for 80,000 gallimaufry.\n• Have a free slot when opening the case and the ??? Earring.' } } },
    { name = 'Guide: Stuck in your Mog Garden?', group = 'Server', desc = 'Type !csfix if the Mog Garden freezes (nothing clickable or a cutscene never ends). Source: https://vanadreams.org/wiki/#guide-c_mog_garden_stuck', steps = { { title = 'Overview', note = '• In the Mog Garden, !csfix closes any open menu or scene and returns you to where you came from: your Mog House city or the Mog Dinghy port.\n• If that place is unavailable you go to your home point.\n• Nothing is lost and the garden remains.\n• Normal exit is still the Green Thumb Moogle: "Leave this Mog Garden".' } } },
    { name = 'Guide: Stylist Moogle', group = 'Server', desc = 'A free NPC that changes your character\'s face at any time. Source: https://vanadreams.org/wiki/#guide-c_stylist_moogle', steps = { { title = 'Where to find it', note = '• !hangout takes you to the Rolanberry bazaar hangout; the moogle is next to the Bonanza Moogle near the arrival point.\n• New characters get a one-time prompt "Customize your look further?" after the opening cutscene; "Yes, show me more looks" opens the same menu.' }, { title = 'How it works', note = '• Talking to it shows your current look.\n• Menu: Face style, Hair colour, Special face, Fomor body, My own body back (as a Fomor), Undo my changes (after a change), All done.\n• Changes apply instantly and others see them; Escape steps back.\n• All done or closing keeps the current look; Undo my changes restores your original look.' }, { title = 'The faces', note = '• Face style: your race\'s 8 creation faces (e.g. "7 Mio" for Mithra), hair colour kept.\n• Hair colour: toggles the face\'s A/B colour, face kept.\n• Special face: Fomor (face only) after quest "Shades of the Lost" (trade the moogle a Swift Belt); Mannequin after owning a full mannequin ("It\'s Raining Mannequins!", Mhaura).' }, { title = 'A whole Fomor body', note = '• Unlocked by "Shades of the Lost"; turns you fully into a Fomor.\n• Groups: Fighters (Warrior, Monk, Samurai, Ninja, Dragoon); Knights and tamers (Paladin, Dark Knight, Beastmaster); Mages (Black Mage, Red Mage, Summoner); Thieves and bards (Thief, Ranger, Bard); Sacrarium lords (Balor, Luaith, Lobais); Aht Urhgan (Wajaom and Bhaflau Fomors). Some have a Lufaise "II" version.\n• Persists through gear changes, zoning and logout; NPCs still talk to you.\n• My own body back reverts it.' }, { title = 'Good to know', note = '• Remove any costume first; the moogle cannot restyle you in costume.' } } },
    { name = 'Guide: Support job lesson (Isacio in Selbina, Vera in Mhaura)', group = 'Server', desc = 'Support jobs are unlocked from character creation, but Isacio and Vera still run the support job lesson as a story quest. Source: https://vanadreams.org/wiki/#guide-c_support_job_lesson', steps = { { title = 'Overview', note = '• Support job level follows the main job: a lower support job stays at its own level (e.g. 10 under a 99 main); a higher one is capped at the main job\'s level.\n• Quest givers: Isacio (Selbina, Elder Memories) or Vera (Mhaura, The Old Lady); doing one locks out the other.\n• Bring the three requested items one at a time, then hear the lesson.\n• Reward: Copper Voucher.\n• Isacio notes Beastmaster and Summoner (main or support) can keep two companions out: a jug pet or charmed mob plus an avatar.' } } },
    { name = 'Guide: The Rolanberry bazaar hangout', group = 'Server', desc = '!hangout (or leaving Lower Jeuno into Rolanberry Fields) puts you in a plaza with market, travel and service NPCs spread over the valley floor. Source: https://vanadreams.org/wiki/#guide-c_hangout', steps = { { title = 'Overview', note = '• Valley mouth: market and travel services.\n• Lone tree: Stylist Moogle, MiniFerrin, Mog Bonanza, Bank of Vana\'diel.\n• West path from the tree: Clan Centurio, bazaar shopkeepers, training ring at the far end.' }, { title = 'Market and travel (the valley mouth, just past the plaza)', note = '• Auction Moogle: Auction House, Mog House menu (storage, delivery box), tips.\n• Login Moogle: Login Campaign exchange with the Greeter Moogle rewards; buy singly or 12 at once for stackables.\n• "More kupons" pages: other kupons for 500 and 1,000 points.\n• Trade Beastmen\'s Seals or Kindred\'s Seals for 10 login points each, any quantity; anything over the 65,535 cap is returned.\n• Survival Guide across the walkway: standard teleports.\n• Home Point crystal beside it: sets home point only, no warps.' }, { title = 'Around the tree', note = '• Stylist Moogle (NW of tree): free faces, hair colours, Fomor and Mannequin looks.\n• MiniFerrin, a black mage automaton beside it: Classic mode desk.\n• Bonanza Pearls (SW): this week\'s pearl for 200,000 gil, Monday 00:00 to Saturday 18:00 server time; pick three digits or random.\n• Bonanza Prizes: after the Saturday 18:00 draw, talk or trade your pearl to see the number and claim a prize; losing pearls get a Bonanza Biscuit.\n• Prize Chest between them: shows 1st, 2nd and 3rd prize lists.\n• Bank Clerk (SE): loans repaid from auction sales; trade gil to pay one down.\n• Bank Vault (gold coffer): shows the gil held by treasurer Rhunek.' }, { title = 'Along the west path', note = '• Montblanc (Clan Centurio): clan registration, weekly NM bills, mark turn-ins, rank rewards.\n• Clan Provisioner next to him: shop paid in clan points.\n• Bazaar shopkeepers on both sides, browsed like player bazaars.' }, { title = 'Training ring (the far end of the west path)', note = '• Talk to the Training Moogle to spawn a Training Crab.\n• Options: My level, Five above me, Ten above me, or Pick a level (10, 20, 30, 40, 50, 60, 70, 75, 80, 90, 99, 119).\n• The crab never attacks, moves, acts, dies (HP refills) or drops items.\n• Higher crabs skill you up faster as long as you can still hit them.\n• One per player: a new request replaces it, Send my crab away dismisses it, and it leaves after 10 minutes without being hit.' } } },
    { name = 'Guide: The Ygnas Directives and The Arciela Directive', group = 'Server', desc = 'Seven one-time Records of Eminence quests (records 955 to 961) about Ygnas, Arciela\'s leafkin companion, sent by Fremilla through Ploh Trishbahk at the Castle Adoulin gate, Eastern Adoulin (K-9). Source: https://vanadreams.org/wiki/#guide-c_ygnas_directives', steps = { { title = 'How to start', note = '• Requires the RoE tutorial First Step Forward and all Seekers of Adoulin missions (through The Light Within).\n• All reports go to Ploh Trishbahk.\n• When Ploh issues a directive, set the record yourself (Other > RoE Quests); a report only counts while it is set.\n• Each directive unlocks after the previous; 3, 5 and the Arciela Directive also need a new Vana\'diel day since your last report.\n• Each record pays base 1,000 sparks and 5,000 EXP, scaled by server RoE rates; first clear gives triple sparks.\n• Dialogue appears in the chat log.' }, { title = 'The Ygnas Directive 1 (record 955)', note = '• Talk to Ploh.\n• Speak with Chalvava in Rala Waterways (F-11); enter from Western Adoulin (I-12), SE of the Mog House.\n• Report to Ploh.' }, { title = 'The Ygnas Directive 2 (record 956)', note = '• Talk to Ploh.\n• Examine the Mischief Marker, Western Adoulin (J-11).\n• Speak with Virsaint at the fountain plaza, Western Adoulin (H-8).\n• Report to Ploh.' }, { title = 'The Ygnas Directive 3 (record 957)', note = '• After a Vana\'diel midnight, talk to Ploh.\n• Speak with Roskin at the Statue of the Goddess, Eastern Adoulin (H-8); he wants Copse Candy.\n• Speak with Runje Desaali, Eastern Adoulin (J-10), and refuse her first price; she will make it for Jungle Nectar plus 10,000 bayld.\n• Buy Jungle Nectar from Soupox in Leafallia for 1,000 bayld.\n• Trade the Nectar to Runje with 10,000 bayld on hand to get Copse Candy (replacement costs 10,000 bayld).\n• Trade the Copse Candy to Roskin, then report to Ploh.\n• Reward: Delegate\'s Cuffs.' }, { title = 'The Ygnas Directive 4 (record 958)', note = '• Talk to Ploh.\n• Speak with Levil, Pioneers\' Coalition, Western Adoulin (E-8).\n• Speak with Masad, Mummers\' Coalition, Western Adoulin (G-10); Sangy challenges you to Boom or Bust.\n• Win 3 rounds, one per talk to Masad: both roll toward 11, over 11 busts, closest wins, ties replay, losses cost nothing.\n• Optional after 2 losses: buy key item Grunt Heard \'Round the World from Runje Desaali (J-10) for 30,000 bayld; Sangy then rolls until he busts. You keep it.\n• Report to Ploh.\n• Reward: Delegate\'s Garb.' }, { title = 'The Ygnas Directive 5 (record 959)', note = '• After a Vana\'diel midnight, talk to Ploh.\n• Examine Amchuchu\'s Laboratory, Inventors\' Coalition, Western Adoulin (J-10).\n• Examine the Contemplation Site on the dock by the Adoulin Waterfront waypoint, Western Adoulin (I-5).\n• In Yorcia Weald (I-8), examine the ??? by the Ergon Locus north of the Frontier Station; once smoke rises, examine again after 11 seconds (10 to 12 counts). Misses reset; retry freely.\n• Report to Ploh.\n• Reward: 20 High-Purity Bayld.' }, { title = 'The Ygnas Directive 6 (record 960)', note = '• Talk to Ploh.\n• Speak with Zaffeld, Eastern Adoulin (J-8).\n• In Yorcia Weald (J-6), examine the Occultist Footprints NW of the Frontier Station (Nashu waits there), then examine again to enter; nearby party members who cleared Directive 5 join.\n• Win, then report to Ploh.\n• Reward: 30 High-Purity Bayld and key item Ygnas\'s Insignia.' }, { title = 'The battle', note = '• Yorcia Weald [U], 30-minute limit, Trusts allowed.\n• Ygnas and Nashu join once you engage a Velkk; Ygnas casts Haste and Cure on the party.\n• You lose only if Nashu dies; a party wipe is fine while Nashu stands.\n• Kill all seven Velkk (50,000 to 80,000 HP each, fast TP gain):\n• Gramk-Droog (WAR, leader): repeated Mighty Strikes.\n• Ymmr-Ulvid Gloomlight (DRK): Blood Weapon.\n• Ignor-Mnt Stealthslayer (WAR): very high evasion.\n• Durs-Vike Deathspell (BLM): Meteor every 90 s; kill first or keep Shell up.\n• Tryl-Wuj Wingrip (BST) with pet Tryl-Wuj\'s Peapuk (immune to sleep and petrify).\n• Liij-Vok Waxwane (WHM): Benediction when low; kill early.\n• Dark-element sleep lands; light-element sleep is resisted.\n• After clearing Directive 6 you can lead or join again; helpers get 10,000 bayld once per Vana\'diel day.' }, { title = 'The Arciela Directive (record 961)', note = '• After a Vana\'diel midnight, talk to Ploh and answer Fremilla\'s questions; she asks for a Chocolate Crepe and a pot of White Honey.\n• Buy both from Runje Desaali, Eastern Adoulin (J-10): Crepe 10,000 bayld, Honey 1,000 bayld, one talk per item.\n• Trade both to Ploh together.\n• Reward: 50 High-Purity Bayld and title Servant to the Servant.' }, { title = 'Trust: Ygnas', note = '• With a Trust permit, examine the Sandy Overlook in Ceizak Battlegrounds (J-10); nearest warp is Frontier Bivouac #1.\n• You learn Trust: Ygnas and receive key item Ygnas\'s Leaf.' } } },
    { name = 'Guide: TP gain', group = 'Server', desc = 'All entities now gain TP at the standard rate. Source: https://vanadreams.org/wiki/#guide-c_tp_gain', steps = { { title = 'Overview', note = '• Players, pets, trusts, fellows and monsters use standard TP gain from melee and ranged hits landed, hits taken and weapon skill hits; Store TP stacks on top.\n• Before late October 2026: players, pets and trusts got 1.25x; monsters 0.85x.\n• Trusts earn TP like players; every Trust TP move, including former fight openers, needs 1,000 TP the Trust built itself.' } } },
    { name = 'Guide: Treasure Caskets', group = 'Server', desc = 'Regular field and dungeon monsters have roughly a 50% chance to leave a Treasure Casket on death. Source: https://vanadreams.org/wiki/#guide-c_treasure_caskets', steps = { { title = 'Overview', note = '• Message: "The monster was concealing a treasure chest!"; the casket appears at the kill spot.\n• Owned by the killing party or alliance; disappears after a few minutes.\n• Some open at once; locked ones need a two-digit code with limited guesses; examine for hints first.\n• Loot: crystals, medicines, scrolls, ores, zone-themed materials, temporary items.\n• "Increased Treasure Casket Discovery" prowess (Grounds or Fields of Valor pages): +4% per stack, max 5 stacks.' }, { title = '+1 gear in item caskets', note = '• Item caskets (not temporary-item ones): 5% chance of one extra +1 or HQ gear piece.\n• Wearable by the opener\'s main job, roughly 6 levels below to 3 above the monster.\n• Rings, earrings, belts, backs and necks are 3x as likely.\n• 1 in 3 carries a random augment; armour never rolls weapon-only augments (damage, delay, etc.); single-point augments (STR+1, HP+1, ...) roll higher on higher-level pieces.' } } },
    { name = 'Guide: Treasure Chests and Coffers: extra rewards', group = 'Server', desc = 'Treasure Chests and Coffers opened with a key or a successful pick can give two bonus rewards on top of normal loot. Source: https://vanadreams.org/wiki/#guide-c_treasure_chests_and_coffers', steps = { { title = 'A Gobbie Mystery Box prize', note = '• When regular loot (gil or item) is given, chance of one Gobbie Mystery Box Special Dial prize: Treasure Coffer 25%, Treasure Chest 10%.\n• With full bags the prize goes to the treasure pool.\n• Opens that give artifact armour, a quest item or a map get no draw.' }, { title = 'Endgame upgrade materials', note = '• Every open also rolls the endgame upgrade material list: chests at 3x an NM\'s rate, coffers at 5x.\n• Drops go to the treasure pool, or straight to your bags when solo.\n• Failed picks, traps, mimics and illusions give neither extra.' } } },
    { name = 'Guide: Trust engage modes and the Lieutenant', group = 'Server', desc = 'Control how your Trusts engage; in Lieutenant mode one Trust picks targets and the others follow it, so the group can hunt by itself. Source: https://vanadreams.org/wiki/#guide-c_trust_lieutenant', steps = { { title = 'The three engage modes', note = '• !trustengage <number>: 0 Standard (engage after you engage and attack), 1 Attack (engage as soon as you engage), 2 Lieutenant (chosen Trust picks targets, others assist).\n• !trustengage alone lists modes and your current one.' }, { title = 'Choosing your Lieutenant', note = '• !trustlead <name> (alias !trustlieutenant) picks the leader from your summoned Trusts; a name prefix works, e.g. !trustlead Zeid.\n• !trustlead first restores the default: the first Trust called.\n• If the Lieutenant is dismissed, the first-called Trust takes over.' }, { title = 'Telling it what to fight', note = '• !trustaggro <order>: ep Easy Prey; dc up to Decent Challenge; em up to Even Match (default); t up to Tough; vt up to Very Tough; it up to Incredibly Tough; all includes Too Weak; defend only monsters attacking you.\n• Con is checked against your level; targets must be unclaimed and able to detect the Lieutenant.\n• In defend, it only goes after monsters targeting you.' }, { title = 'Example', note = '• Summon your Trusts, then: !trustengage 2, !trustlead Valaineral, !trustaggro t.\n• Valaineral then pulls detecting monsters up to Tough and the others assist.' } } },
    { name = 'Guide: Trusts (Alter Egos)', group = 'Server', desc = 'Vanadreams has all 122 Trusts, each with its own job, spells, abilities and weapon skills; see Alter Ego Points for upgrades. Source: https://vanadreams.org/wiki/#guide-c_trusts', steps = { { title = 'The basics', note = '• Start with your nation\'s Trust quest: Gondebaud (Southern San d\'Oria), Clarion Star (Port Bastok) or Wetata (Windurst Woods) for a permit and first Trusts.\n• Learn ciphers by trading them to those NPCs.\n• Cap: 3 Trusts; 4 with Rhapsody in White (Rhapsodies 1-5); 5 with Rhapsody in Crimson (Rhapsodies 2-13).\n• Party leader only, with no monster enmity; not while seeking a party or within 2 minutes of a member joining.\n• Alliances work; each leader\'s Trusts stay in that leader\'s party (see Alliances with Trusts).\n• No duplicates and no two versions of one Trust (e.g. Shantotto and Shantotto II).\n• Allowed: most field/dungeon zones, missions, quests, Abyssea, Dynamis and Dynamis [D], Omen, Odyssey, Ambuscade, Voidwatch, Walk of Echoes, Vagary, Skirmish, Domain Invasion, Reives, Limbus (max 3).\n• Not allowed: cities, Assault, Salvage, Nyzul Isle, Sortie, Einherjar, battlefields that forbid them.\n• At level 99, Trusts match your average item level (up to 119).' }, { title = 'How to get each Trust', note = '• Nation quest follow-ups (talk to the Trust NPCs again): Shantotto, Naji, Kupipi, Excenmille, Ayame, Nanaa Mihgo, Curilla, Volker, Ajido-Marujido, Trion, Iron Eater.\n• Login campaign (Greeter Moogle) ciphers: Zeid, Lion, Naja, Lehko, Luzaf, Najelith, D. Shantotto, Star Sibyl, Karaha-Baruha, Areuhat, Uka Totlihn, Kuyin Hathdenna, Abenzio, Rughadjeen, Lhe Lhangavo, Mayakov, Brygid, Mildaurion, Rongelouts, Robel-Akbel, Teodor, Ullegore, Darrcuiln, Shantotto II.\n• Mog Pell (Ochre): 100 login points at the Greeter Moogle; trade to a Festive Moogle (Port San d\'Oria, Port Bastok, Windurst Walls) for one of 60 ciphers. Only source for Aldo, Moogle, Fablinix, Kupofried, Elivira, Noillurie, Lhu Mhakaracca, Leonoyne, Maximilian, Kayeel-Payeel, Babban, Mumor, Mumor II.\n• Sparks of Eminence shop: Cid, Gilgamesh, Ferreous Coffin, Qultada, King of Hearts.\n• Conquest Overseers: Tenzen, Rahal, Kukki-Chebukki, Makki-Chebukki.\n• Besieged: Mihli Aliapoh. Campaign: Valaineral, Adelheid. Abyssea: Joachim.\n• Assault: Ovjang, Mnejing. Training regimes: Sakura, Koru-Moru.\n• Ujlei Zelekko (Eastern Adoulin, bayld): Margret, Amchuchu, Morimar.\n• RoE "Call Forth an Alter Ego" chain: Valaineral, Mihli Aliapoh, Tenzen, Adelheid, Joachim.\n• RoE "Always Stand on 117": Koru-Moru.\n• RoE "Filled to Capacity", "Over Capacity", "Way Over Capacity" (500,000 capacity points with a Trust in party, outside Abyssea): Ingrid II, Rosulatia, August in order; then Marjory in the Archduke\'s house (Ru\'Lude Gardens, H-5) gives Marjory\'s Thesis.\n• A.M.A.N. Validator deeds: Monberaux.\n• Rhapsodies of Vana\'diel: Semih Lafihna, Halver, Lion II, Zeid II, Tenzen II, Prishe II, Abquhbah, Nashmeira II, Lilisette II, Balamor, Selh\'teus, Arciela II, Iroha, Iroha II.\n• Seekers of Adoulin: Ingrid; after the final mission, examine the Sandy Overlook in Ceizak Battlegrounds for Arciela.\n• Treasures of Aht Urhgan: Nashmeira.\n• Chains of Promathia, during or after "Dawn": Prishe (Walnut Door, Tavnazian Safehold), Ulmia (Dilapidated Gate, Misareaux Coast); Shikaree Z and Cherukiki from their own NPCs.\n• Aht Urhgan Whitegate: Gessho (examine the Cushion in Shararat Teahouse once ToAU mission "Passing Glory" is offered); Gadalar (Fari-Wari after "Embers of His Past"); Zazarg (Fari-Wari after "Fist of the People").\n• Wings of the Goddess and later entries: list is cut off here; see the source.' }, { title = 'What each Trust does', note = '• Ygnas: WHM; strong ranged Cures, Phototrophic Blessing at 3+ hurt members; keeps Protect, Shell, Haste up; removes ailments.\n• Pieuje (UC): WHM; cures at 75%, removes ailments (party Esuna under Afflatus Misery), keeps Protectra, Shellra, Auspice, Haste; scales with Unity rank.\n• Yoran-Oran (UC): WHM, large MP, Nott restores MP; scales with Unity rank.\n• Cherukiki: WHM; Cure, Protect, Shell; enfeebles and Hastes above half MP; Meteor with Makki and Kukki.\n• Karaha-Baruha: WHM/SMN; cures at 75%, Hastes melee, Spirit Taker when low MP; holds TP to close skillchains.\n• Nashmeira II: single Cures; Curaga only when 3+ members are at 75% or less.\n• Ingrid: battle WHM; Hastes melee, highest Banish, Cursna, strong vs undead.\n• Invincible Shield (UC): great axe tank, constant Provoke, 20% less damage taken; Retaliation, Warcry, Blood Rage, Restraint.\n• Halver: Berserk polearm DD; tanks (Sentinel, Rampart, Provoke, Flash, Cure) when someone falls to 40% HP or is slept.\n• Arciela: light mode (Haste, Refresh, Protect, Shell on you and herself) alternating with dark mode (Slow, Paralyze, Dispel, Addle); Guiding Light party buff, Illustrious Aid party heal.\n• Arciela II: swaps modes every 90 s; Haste for melee, Refresh for casters and tanks; dark-mode enfeebles, magic bursts, one full recovery via Naakual\'s Vengeance.\n• King of Hearts: RDM; keeps Dia, Shuffle removes enemy buffs, Haste and Refresh on you, Phalanx II on the tank, cures at 50%, Firaga IV bursts from level 92.\n• Qultada: always Chaos Roll; second roll priority: Corsair\'s Roll (EXP/CP bonus active: Dedication, Commitment, Kupofried), Evoker\'s Roll (anyone at 66% MP or less), Hunter\'s Roll (poor accuracy), else Fighter\'s Roll; swaps when conditions change, Double-Ups toward lucky or 11, Snake Eye when one pip short.\n• Remaining Trusts: list is cut off here; see the source.' }, { title = 'Trust fixes (October 2026)', note = '• Bards: Ulmia now has MP (its absence caused needless Refresh casts); Joachim\'s MP corrected; each bard keeps two distinct songs, so two bards give four (they used to repeat Blade Madrigal and Victory March).\n• Kupipi, Curilla, Excenmille, Fablinix, Trion, Adelheid: cure the hate holder at 75%, others at 50% (or 66%).\n• Iroha, Pieuje (UC), Yoran-Oran (UC): cast the -ra spell once, then single Protect/Shell for out-of-range members.\n• Arciela\'s Illustrious Aid and Lilisette\'s waltz need 2+ hurt members or a sleeping one; Apururu (UC) Curagas at 3+.\n• Aldo, Aldo (UC), Jakoh (UC), Romaa Mihgo, Ark Angel MR: Sneak Attack only from behind.\n• Ark Angel HM tanks with Yonin when you lack a tank, attacks with Innin otherwise. Rughadjeen raises again. Mnejing gets full 37.5% damage reduction. Naji Provokes every recast. Nanaa Mihgo uses Mug.\n• Added: Karaha-Baruha ailment removal; Yoran-Oran (UC) Protect, Shell, Stoneskin; Rainemard Composure, Haste II, Refresh II; Zeid Souleater with a WHM in party; Iron Eater Berserk and Restraint; Invincible Shield (UC) Tomahawk on physical-resistant foes.\n• HP/MP fixed: Darrcuiln, Morimar, Noillurie, Teodor, Shikaree Z, Abenzio.\n• Healers, bards and mages now stand on your side of the target and return if they drift too far.' }, { title = 'Trust abilities', note = '• Ability timers are shared like a player\'s (all Waltzes, Sambas, Quick Draws); abilities are level-gated.\n• Steal or Despoil loot goes to your inventory.\n• A buff that keeps failing on the same target backs off: immediately, then 6, 12, 24, 48 and 60 s apart.' }, { title = 'TP, stats and gear (22 October 2026)', note = '• Every TP move needs 1,000 self-built TP, including Valaineral\'s Uriel Blade, AAEV\'s Shield Strike, Lion\'s Grapeshot, Trion\'s Royal Bash, Lehko Habhoka\'s Inspirit, Arciela\'s Illustrious Aid, Arciela II\'s Naakual\'s Vengeance, Rosulatia\'s Dryad\'s Kiss, Morimar\'s Vehement Resolution.\n• TP moves scale with the Trust\'s own STR, DEX, VIT, AGI, INT, MND or CHR; moves named like a player weapon skill use its stats; gear given via vanagear raises their damage.\n• Trust nukes use the player formula (gear INT counts fully); -ga, -ja and -ra spells lose damage per extra target; Cherukiki\'s and Kukki-Chebukki\'s Meteor matches a player\'s.\n• Shantotto II: +495 spell damage at 99 (halved), still grows with item level.' }, { title = 'Choosing what a Trust uses', note = '• A disabled action stays off while the Trust is out and on every later call.\n• With vanagear: each called Trust has a tab in the /vg window; untick actions under "Uses".\n• Without it, use the party-list name: !trustuse <trust> lists disabled actions; !trustuse <trust> off <action> (e.g. !trustuse Ulmia off Valor Minuet); !trustuse <trust> on <action>; !trustuse <trust> reset.\n• Categories usable in place of one action: cure, nuke, enfeebling, enhancing, dark, divine, song, ninjutsu, bluemagic, geomancy, summoning, magic, ability, weaponskill.' } } },
    { name = 'Guide: Unity Concord: warp to a Wanted area', group = 'Server', desc = 'Unity Concord NPCs warp you to Wanted encounter areas for accolades. Source: https://vanadreams.org/wiki/#guide-c_unity_concord_wanted_warp', steps = { { title = 'Overview', note = '• Requires 10 cleared Records of Eminence and Unity membership.\n• Unity Concord locations: Southern San d\'Oria, Bastok Markets, Windurst Woods, Western Adoulin.\n• Choose "Bring me to a Wanted encounter area"; 100 accolades per trip.\n• Level groups: 99 and below, 119, 122, 125, 128, 135, 145.\n• 135: Behemoth\'s Dominion, Boyahda Tree, Valley of Sorrows, Wajaom Woodlands, Mount Zhayolm, Caedarva Mire.\n• 145: Aydeewa Subterrane.\n• Boarding Permit needed for Wajaom Woodlands, Caedarva Mire and Alzadaal Undersea Ruins.' } } },
    { name = 'Guide: Unity: Wanted Battles and Gear Upgrades', group = 'Server', desc = 'Unity Wanted NM fights at Ethereal Junctions, how to turn their drops into +1 gear, and how to rank that gear up with Lustreless materials. Source: https://vanadreams.org/wiki/#guide-c_unity', steps = { { title = 'Unity Wanted', note = '• 56 Wanted NMs, split into three lists spanning CL 75 to 145; each call-out costs 200-4,100 Unity accolades.\n• Examine an Ethereal Junction to summon the NM; nearby alliance members in a Unity also join and pay.\n• Time limit 15 minutes; HP and MP are refilled at the start.\n• Every payer receives a coffer: one unique NM item, material, spell scroll or gil.\n• If inventory is full, the coffer waits; examine any Ethereal Junction to claim it.\n• Coffer gear always drops as +1.\n• No Rare duplicates (Mog Safe and wardrobes are checked); the NM\'s upgrade material drops 1-3 per coffer.\n• A win also clears that NM\'s Subjugation (UC) objective if set.' }, { title = 'Upgrading Wanted gear (+1)', note = '• Trade NQ item + its NM material + accolades to a Unity Concord NPC: Urbiolaine (Southern San d\'Oria), Igsli (Bastok Markets), Teldro-Kesdrodo or Yonolala (Windurst Woods), Nunaarl Bthtrogg (Western Adoulin).\n• IL119: 50 materials, 10,000 accolades.\n• Level 99: 30 materials, 5,000 accolades.\n• Level 98 and below: 3 materials, 1,000 accolades.\n• Pick up the item from any of these NPCs after the next Vana\'diel midnight; one item in progress at a time.' }, { title = 'Augment ranks (Rank 1-15)', note = '• 107 upgraded Wanted items accept augment ranks.\n• Lustreless scale: CL119-122 gear, requires Sheol A exit objective.\n• Lustreless hide: CL125-128 gear, requires Sheol B exit objective.\n• Lustreless wing: CL135-145 gear, requires Sheol C exit objective.\n• For Rank 1, hand any Unity Concord NPC the +1 piece, 30,000 accolades and a single unit of its Lustreless material.\n• Further ranks: trade only the material; 1,190 more materials to reach Rank 15.\n• The NPC accepts only what the next rank needs and reports the remainder.\n• Extra augment lines open around Rank 6 and Rank 11.' } } },
    { name = 'Guide: Unlocking Master Levels', group = 'Server', desc = 'How to unlock Master Levels (up to 50) on a mastered level 99 job and earn Exemplar Points. Source: https://vanadreams.org/wiki/#guide-c_master_levels', steps = { { title = 'Overview', note = '• Master Levels take a mastered job beyond 99, capped at Master Level 50.\n• Per level: +1 all stats, +1 skill caps, +7 HP, +2 MP.\n• Automatons, avatars and wyverns gain accuracy, attack, defense and evasion per level.\n• Support job already matches main job level on Vanadreams (see Jobs, Subjobs and Level Limits).' }, { title = 'What you need', note = '• Main job at 99 with the Job Breaker key item, given on first talk at 99 by the Nomad Moogle or Maat (Ru\'Lude Gardens).\n• The job mastered: all 2,100 Job Points spent (via the Mog House menu).' }, { title = 'How to unlock', note = '• Talk to the Nomad Moogle or Maat in Ru\'Lude Gardens on the mastered job at 99 to receive the Master Breaker key item.\n• Since the 18 Oct update they report your spent Job Points out of 2,100 if not yet mastered.\n• Since the 18 Oct update, logging in on a mastered 99 job also grants Master Breaker.\n• Master Breaker is account-wide across jobs, but Master Levels apply only to mastered jobs.' }, { title = 'Earning Exemplar Points', note = '• Kills on a mastered job yield Exemplar Points (EP) rather than EXP.\n• EP come from mobs at or above your effective level (119 + Master Level / 5); Sheol, Apex, Locus and High Apex mobs give far more.\n• Master chains: +2% EP per chain, max +100% at chain 50.\n• Only Corsair\'s Roll boosts EP; Lungo-Nango\'s Thesis grants 4,000-6,000 EP.\n• KO costs 2% of next-level EP and can de-level; Raise recovers part.\n• Ambuscade gives no EP; level sync under 99 disables Master Levels.' }, { title = 'Mastery and your support job', note = '• Since the 18 Oct update, the +1 skill per Master Level also applies to support-job-only skills (e.g. Ninjutsu on WAR/NIN).\n• A mastered (2,100 JP) support job at 99 also grants its Job Point gifts; Superior rank and Capacity Point Bonus come only from the main job.' } } },
    { name = 'Guide: Vagary rewards: the Odyssean Passage', group = 'Server', desc = 'Trade the five Vagary wards at the Odyssean Passage in Leafallia for a chosen or random reward. Source: https://vanadreams.org/wiki/#guide-c_vagary', steps = { { title = 'Overview', note = '• Location: Odyssean Passage, Leafallia.\n• Gather the five fabricated wards from Outer Ra\'Kaznar [U]: Impurity, Miasma, Biting Winds, Ashen Wings, False King.\n• Talk to the Passage; the imps exchange all five for one reward.' }, { title = 'Choosing your reward', note = '• Option 1: any one of 31 equipment pieces.\n• Option 2: any one of 11 materials.\n• Option 3 ("Whatever the master deems worthy"): random pick from both lists plus Tartarus Platemail, a Codex of Etchings and an Etched Memory; 45 entries at 2.2% each, Codex of Etchings listed twice (4.4%).\n• Wards are consumed only if the item fits in your bags.\n• Equipment: Count\'s Garb, Count\'s Cuffs, Etiolation Earring, Enervating Earring, Befouled Crown, Odium, Incarnation Sash, Achiuchikapu, Rhadamanthus, Punchinellos, Defiant Collar, Soulcleaver, Acclimator, Crusher\'s Gauntlets, Rumination Sash, Miasmic Pants, Cryptic Earring, Mindmelter, Devivifier, Focal Orb, Limbo Trousers, Feast Hose, Famine Sash, Umbra Strap, Meekculler, Brahmastra, Rabid Visor, Supay Weskit, Avatara Slops, Deviant Necklace, Vengeful Ring.\n• Materials: Tartarian Chain, Tartarian Soul, Chunk of Dark Matter, Hades\' Claw, Vial of Defiant Sweat, Macuil Plating, Vial of Plovid Effluvium, Chunk of Plovid Flesh, Macuil Horn, Defiant Scarf, Codex of Etchings.' }, { title = 'Handing over the Fabricated Pearl of the False King', note = '• Use "Hand over" in the imps\' menu to trade the Fabricated Pearl of the False King for one random item from the random list, same odds.\n• Only taken if the item fits in your bags.' }, { title = 'Monster drops', note = '• Vagary bosses and regular mobs drop Etched Memories, occasionally a Codex of Etchings, and bosses drop their own gear; check each drop table.' } } },
    { name = 'Guide: Vana\'bout', group = 'Server', desc = 'Vana\'bout is a Records of Eminence event: objectives earn plaudits for monthly tiered rewards from the Coordinator Moogle, and Curator Moogles exchange material sets for rare items. Source: https://vanadreams.org/wiki/#guide-c_vana_bout', steps = { { title = 'How to start', note = '• Finish the RoE objective Stepping into an Ambuscade to unlock the Vana\'bout objectives.\n• Period objectives reset monthly; daily ones reset daily.' }, { title = 'Coordinator Moogle (Mhaura, G-8)', note = '• Shows plaudits and hands out rewards: one per reached tier, once a month; plaudits are not spent.\n• First claim grants the title Venerated Adventurer.\n• Speaking to it with 400+ plaudits completes the objective Plaudits!' }, { title = 'Silver tier (200 plaudits)', note = '• Choose one: Green Mog Pell x5, Mog Kupon W-Eth, Mog Kupon I-Aby x3, Super Reraiser Tank, Marble Mog Pell, Dial Key #Fo x3, Mog Kupon I-Amb x3.' }, { title = 'Gold tier (700 plaudits)', note = '• Choose one: 100 deeds of heroism, Abdhaljs Seal x3, Gold Mog Pell, Silver Mog Pell, Montiont Silverpiece, One Hundred Byne Bill, Lungo-Nango Jadeshell, Linen Coin Purse (alexandrite) x3, Mog Kupon A-AF+3.' }, { title = 'Limit Break tier (1,200 plaudits)', note = '• Choose one: 10,000 exemplar points (99 Job Master with Master Breaker), 10,000 EXP, 10 job points (99 with Job Breaker), Moogle Memorandum, Rakaznar Ingot, Old Case +1 x3, Umbral Marrow x2, Mulcibar\'s Scoria.' }, { title = 'Curator Moogles', note = '• Locations: Chateau d\'Oraguille (H-9, left just inside), Metalworks (J-8, room right of the President\'s office), Heavens Tower (Secretary\'s room).\n• Talk for recipes, then trade all of a recipe\'s items together; each exchange counts toward Thanks and Come Again! (3 exchanges).\n• Shadow Lord Shirt: Lament, Extinction, Cotton Cloth x3, Galkan Sausage.\n• Pungent Powder III: Carbuncle\'s Ruby, Glass Fiber x2.\n• Alexander Statue: Fafnir\'s Scale, Kirin\'s Mane, Iron Giant Shard, Bronzite x3.\n• Archduke\'s Sword: Kamlanaut\'s Sword, Acolyte\'s Grief, scroll of Enlight, scroll of Endark, Red Curry.\n• Archduke\'s Shield: Kamlanaut\'s Shield, Autumn\'s End in Gustaberg, scroll of Refresh II, Pamama au Lait.\n• Moogle Masque: Mandragora Masque +1, Lycopodium Mallet, Pom-pom Fruit, Black Ink, Wool Cloth.\n• Fafnir Statue: Fafnir\'s Scale, Summer Uchiwa, Lungo-Nango Jadeshell.\n• Red/Clear/Green/Yellow/Purple/Blue/White/Black Chip: Bronzite + Fire/Ice/Wind/Earth/Lightning/Water/Light/Dark Cluster.\n• Sea Monk Venom: One Byne Bill, Poison Dust.\n• Rare items are refused if you already hold one.' } } },
    { name = 'Guide: Vanafish', group = 'Server', desc = 'Vanafish (v0.1.4) is the Vanadreams auto-fishing addon: it casts, judges each bite against your keep rules, finishes the fight and recasts, halting for full bags, no bait, tells or zoning. Source: https://vanadreams.org/wiki/#guide-c_vanafish_addon', steps = { { title = 'Getting started', note = '• Launcher > Addons: select vanafish, Install, tick, Save (or tick Load the fishing addon at startup on the Fishing page); the launcher auto-updates it on Play.\n• Log in; chat shows [vanafish] loaded.\n• At water, equip a rod (ranged) and bait (ammo).\n• Press Start fishing or type /vanafish start; stand still.\n• Press Stop or type /vanafish stop to take over.\n• Moving over 2 yalms from the start spot stops it.' }, { title = 'The window', note = '• Window "Vanadreams fishing", toggled with /vanafish.\n• States: idle, casting, waiting for a bite, hooked, ending the fight, resolving, cooldown, stopped (with stop reason and countdown).\n• Rod/Bait drop-downs list items from inventory and Wardrobes 1-4, best first, tagged [best]; picking one equips it.\n• Shows skill (whole points), free slots, counters (Casts, Bites, Catches, Releases, Lost, Breaks, Nothing, Skill-ups), last bite details and last result.\n• Folding sections: What to keep, Timing, Stop when; saved per character instantly.' }, { title = 'In the launcher', note = '• Fishing page Catch log: last 500 results with time, result, item, bite kind and feeling; totals for catches, lost fish, skill-ups, and top three fish.\n• Open catch log folder opens the plain-text table (spreadsheet-readable).' }, { title = 'What the bot does', note = '• Casts with /fish and waits for the game\'s bite timer; the server sends stamina and time limit on bite.\n• Reads the bite and feeling chat lines, then keeps or releases per your rules.\n• After a random reel delay (min-max, never later than 3 s before the time limit) it ends the fight; keeping triggers the server catch roll.\n• Waits the between-cast delay, then recasts.' }, { title = 'Bites and feelings', note = '• "Something caught the hook!" = small fish; "Something caught the hook!!!" = large fish; "You feel something pulling at your line" = item; "Something clamps onto your line" = monster.\n• Good feeling: no disadvantage.\n• Bad feeling: fish outclasses the rod; snap/break chance under 45%.\n• Terrible feeling: chance 30% or more (45%+ is always terrible).\n• "Not sure you have the skill" / "don\'t have the skill": fish above your skill.\n• Angler\'s sense (Keen Angler\'s Sense): kept under normal rules.' }, { title = 'What to keep', note = '• Small fish on; Large fish on; Items on; Monsters off (unkept monsters released).\n• Release when you don\'t have the skill: on.\n• Release anyway, % of bites: 0 (range 0-50%).\n• Releasing uses up bait; lures are kept.' }, { title = 'Timing', note = '• Reel after: min 4 s, max 12 s (range 2-60).\n• Between casts: min 6 s (5-60), max 10 s (5-120).\n• Server limit is one cast per 5 s.' }, { title = 'Stop when', note = '• Auto-equip next rod or bait: on.\n• Free slots at or below: 1 (0-10).\n• A tell arrives: on. You move (over 2 yalms): on.\n• Casts: 0; Minutes: 0; Skill reaches: 0 (0 = no limit).\n• Nothing bites, in a row: 15 (0 = off; any bite resets).\n• Command when stopped: empty (e.g. /echo fishing stopped).\n• Also stops on zoning, logout, server bag-full, no rod, no bait, or addon unload.' }, { title = 'Rod and bait recovery', note = '• With auto-equip on, broken rods or spent bait are replaced from inventory or Wardrobes 1-4 only (not Satchel, Sack, Case, Storage, Mog Safe).\n• Rod priority: Judges Rod, Ebisu Fishing Rod +1, Ebisu Fishing Rod, Lu Shang\'s Fishing Rod +1, Lu Shang\'s Fishing Rod, Composite, Mithran, Single Hook, Clothespole, Halcyon Rod, Glass Fiber, Carbon, Hume, Tarutaru, Fastwater, Bamboo, Yew, Willow; Maze Monger Fishing Rod and Goldfish Basket last.\n• Bait priority: consumable bait first, largest stack first, then lures.\n• With auto-equip off, it stops instead.' }, { title = 'Skill-ups', note = '• Set Skill reaches to fish until a target skill.\n• One roll per kept fish; items, monsters and released fish never give skill-ups.\n• Fish must be above your skill and at most 50 levels above; best odds around 11 levels above.\n• Vanadreams doubles the skill-up chance; usual gain 0.1, up to 0.3 when far above.\n• Fishing outside cities and below skill 50 helps; Pelican Ring adds extra rolls.\n• No Fishermen\'s Guild rank-ups needed; only the normal skill cap applies.\n• Early on, keep everything; move to higher-level fish once you outlevel a spot.' }, { title = 'Rods', note = '• Small fish: Willow 5, Yew 6, Fastwater 7, Bamboo 8, Tarutaru 9, Hume 10, Glass Fiber 12, Carbon 13, Halcyon Rod 18.\n• Large fish: Clothespole 16, Mithran 18, Single Hook 22, Composite 24.\n• Both: Lu Shang\'s (+1) 28, Ebisu (+1) 30, Judges Rod 40.\n• Strength = toughest fish handled safely; beyond it, snap/break odds rise with the gap, max 55%.\n• Ebisu rods and Judges Rod never break; others become broken rods.\n• Wrong size rod can lose the fish ("too big"/"too small", up to 50%); not an issue for Lu Shang\'s, Ebisu, Judges. Untick Large fish when using a small-fish rod.' }, { title = 'Bait and lures', note = '• Bait is consumed per fish kept, released or lost.\n• Lures (Robber Rig, Rogue Rig, Sabiki Rig, Minnow, Sinking Minnow, Lizard Lure, Shrimp Lure, Frog Lure, Worm Lure, Fly Lure, etc.) are lost only on snap or break.\n• Bait power 1-3 per fish; lures slightly weaker than equal-power bait.\n• Crayfish: Peeled Crayfish or Little Worm. Moat Carp: Ball of Insect Paste, then Little Worm. Bastore Sardine: Sabiki Rig, then Lugworm. Quus: Lugworm, then Sabiki Rig. Robber Rig and Rogue Rig: power 1 on all of these.\n• The bot never picks bait for the fish; it uses your equipped bait until gone.' }, { title = 'What decides the catch', note = '• Server roll order: fish lost (0.8% per level the fish is above your skill beyond 7, max 55%, plus "too big" on small rods), then line snap, then rod break (both only if fish outclasses rod), else caught.\n• Fish stays hooked only for its time limit; no fatigue, daily cap or cadence check besides the 5 s cast lock and spot stock.' }, { title = 'Starter fish', note = '• Crayfish (7): Windurst Waters/Walls/Woods, Port San d\'Oria, Bastok Markets, La Theine Plateau, West Ronfaure (Knightwell), East Ronfaure.\n• Bastore Sardine (9): Port Bastok, Port Windurst, Selbina, Mhaura, Kazham, Valkurm Dunes.\n• Moat Carp (11): Windurst Waters/Walls/Woods, Port San d\'Oria, Bastok Markets, La Theine Plateau, West Ronfaure (Knightwell), West Sarutabaruta (Pond), East Sarutabaruta (Lake Tepokalipuka).\n• Greedie (14): Selbina, Valkurm Dunes.\n• Copper Frog (16): Bastok Mines, North Gustaberg, Zeruhn Mines, Pashhow Marshlands.\n• Quus (19): Port Bastok, Port Windurst, Selbina, Kazham, Valkurm Dunes.\n• Each spot has a finite stock that regenerates over time.' }, { title = 'Fishing records', note = '• Kept catches count toward fishing Records of Eminence and the in-game catch log (see Fishing Records and the Catch Log).' }, { title = 'Limitations', note = '• No walking, spot selection or following.\n• No buying/crafting rods or bait; no bait choice per fish.\n• No equipping from Satchel, Sack, Case, Storage, Mog Safe.\n• Does not release on bad/terrible feelings, only on lacking skill.\n• Never auto-restarts; no tell replies or zone reactions; stops on zoning.\n• Ignores the minigame gauge; the 5 s cast lock cannot be bypassed.' } } },
    { name = 'Guide: Vanagear', group = 'Server', desc = 'Vanagear is the Vanadreams gear-swap addon: it assembles job- and level-appropriate sets from the gear you carry, swaps them automatically, runs your own multi-line commands and can gear your trusts. Source: https://vanadreams.org/wiki/#guide-c_vanagear', steps = { { title = 'Overview', note = '• Enable it on the launcher\'s Addons page: tick vanagear, press Save, then Play; in game type /vg.\n• Current version 0.1.19; the launcher updates it automatically at startup.\n• It is based on LuAshitacast (ThornyFFXI) and replaces it; old LuAshitacast profiles and /lac commands still work.\n• Do not enable the separate luashitacast addon alongside it.' }, { title = 'Getting started', note = '• After zoning, vanagear builds and swaps nothing until you have stood in the zone for 10 seconds.\n• /vg opens the window on the Your sets tab, already filled from inventory and wardrobes.\n• /vg help lists the commands relevant to your current job.' }, { title = 'How vanagear picks your gear', note = '• Sources: inventory plus all eight wardrobes; Mog Safe, Storage, Locker, Satchel, Sack and Case are never used.\n• Only gear your job, level and race can equip is considered.\n• Each set weights stats and caps some; past 25% gear haste or -50% damage taken, further slots go to other stats.\n• Automatic rebuild on job, support job, level or weapon change and on every zone; newly obtained or moved gear counts from the next zone.\n• /vg build forces an immediate rebuild.\n• Gear equipped by hand from the equipment menu stays on until you zone.' }, { title = 'The window (/vg)', note = '• Header: job, level and time the sets were built.\n• Tabs: Your sets (all built sets and your edits), Your commands (create/run/edit/delete commands), How to (command and Lua help), plus one tab per active trust.\n• Bottom bar: name box, New set, Dress; on a trust tab: New set for <trust> and Send all again.' }, { title = 'Your sets tab', note = '• Left list: Idle, Resting, Dt, Movement, Engaged with hybrid and accuracy variants, Precast, one set per usable weapon skill, ability sets and more; Your spells holds a set for each learned, castable spell (main or support job).\n• Right side: the 16 slots, each a dropdown with Built: <piece> (revert to auto pick), Nothing (take it off), or any carried piece that fits, support-job gear included.\n• * marks your own pick; a green +number shows a built piece\'s contribution; hover to see the next three candidates.\n• Lock my look to this set keeps your appearance fixed per job while swaps continue unseen; untick or use /vg look off.\n• Wear it (stays until /vg wear off), Take what I wear, Undo my changes, Delete this set.' }, { title = 'Weapons', note = '• Default /vg weapons off: Main, Sub and Range are never swapped, since swapping costs TP.\n• In that mode those three slots are one job-wide choice: Leave it alone, Nothing (take it off), or a weapon you carry.\n• /vg weapons on lets vanagear pick weapons too.' }, { title = 'Built-in swaps', note = '• Engaged when fighting, Idle otherwise, Resting when resting.\n• Idle_Regen below 60% HP, Idle_Refresh below 70% MP, Movement while walking.\n• Spells: Precast at cast start, then the magic-type set and the spell\'s own set on release (e.g. Cure_Precast, Song_Precast).\n• Weapon skills use their own set (e.g. SavageBlade) or Ws_Default.\n• Job abilities use their own set when vanagear knows the gear stat involved (e.g. BloodRage); BST Ready, Reward, Charm, Call Beast, COR rolls and Quick Draw, and SMN blood pacts have sets.\n• Preshot and Midshot for ranged attacks; pet sets for pet jobs during pet combat and moves.\n• Hachirin-no-Obi, if carried, on nukes matching the day or weather.\n• Your manual Idle (or Resting) slot picks win over automatic Movement/Idle_Regen/Idle_Refresh unless those sets have their own pick for that slot; action sets always go on top.' }, { title = 'Modes and overlays', note = '• Chat toggles that persist until changed or until vanagear reloads; an on/off switch with no argument flips.\n• /vg dt, /vg kite, /vg th: put damage-taken, movement or Treasure Hunter gear over everything.\n• /vg tp default / hybrid / acc: choose the Engaged set (no argument cycles).\n• /vg idle auto / regen / refresh / speed: idle mode; auto uses the HP/MP thresholds.\n• /vg nuke power / acc: damage vs accuracy for nukes and enfeebles.\n• /vg burst: magic burst gear on nukes.\n• /vg stage: precast gear, then defensive gear mid-cast, then spell gear just before landing.\n• /vg pet tp / dt / acc: what your gear boosts for your pet.' }, { title = 'Gear you use from the slot', note = '• /vg <word> equips the item, waits its equip delay, uses it, then returns the slot to your sets.\n• xp: Empress Band, Emperor Band, Chariot Band, Kupofried\'s Ring, Resolution Ring.\n• cp: Capacity Ring, Trizek Ring.\n• vocation, tav: Vocation Ring, Tavnazian Ring.\n• holla, dem, mea: the Dimensional Rings.\n• Anything else: first word of the item name (Warp Ring = /vg warp).\n• /vg help shows the words for items you carry.' }, { title = 'Beastmaster', note = '• /vg call <jug>: loads the jug and uses Call Beast; partial names work (/vg call fizzy); no argument repeats the last jug.\n• /vg loyal <jug>: same with Bestial Loyalty.\n• /vg reward [food]: loads pet food and uses Reward; food = alpha to theta, roborant, poultice, or debuff (Pet Roborant, else Pet Poultice); no argument picks the best biscuit for your level.\n• /vg jugs and /vg foods list what you carry.' }, { title = 'Help with your gear', note = '• /vg status: zone-wait state, active profile, set/piece counts, and pieces named in sets that you lack.\n• /vg why <set> <slot>: winning piece plus the next three, e.g. /vg why Tp_Default Ring1.\n• /vg upgrades: Mog Safe or Storage items that would win a slot; only readable in your Mog House or near a Nomad Moogle.' }, { title = 'What a template is', note = '• Each job has a template listing its sets and the stat weights/caps of each; weights use gear units (1 STR, 1% haste, 1% damage taken).\n• Fighting jobs: Idle, Idle_Regen, Resting, Dt, Movement, three Engaged sets, Ws_Default.\n• White Mage, Black Mage, Scholar, Geomancer, Summoner and Bard get the standing sets but no Engaged or weapon skill sets unless the template adds them at that level.\n• Magic users (main or support) get Precast, a casting set and one set per magic type; pet jobs get pet sets; all jobs get a Treasure Hunter set.\n• Level bands: 1-30, 31-60, 61-75, 76-99.\n• Weapon skill sets start from the stats the Vanadreams WS script reads, plus crit rate for TP-crit WS, attack for Tachi: Fudo, Tachi: Kaiten, Iron Tempest and Sturmwind, and accuracy where accuracy drops with TP.\n• Spell sets follow the spell\'s kind; ability sets follow what the ability reads from gear.\n• Ninja, Paladin and Rune Fencer are geared as tanks.\n• Templates live in the addon\'s jobs folder and are overwritten on update; your own sets survive updates.' }, { title = 'Making your own: sets of your own', note = '• A set named like a built set (Idle, Tp_Default, Reward, CallBeast, SavageBlade, CureIV) overrides only the slots you picked; other slots stay automatic.\n• Any other name is a standalone set, worn only via /vg wear, /vg with, /vg look, /gs equip or a custom command.\n• Aliases: Engaged/TP/Melee = Tp_Default; Hybrid = Tp_Hybrid; Acc = Tp_Acc; WS = Ws_Default; FastCast = Precast; Midcast = Interim; Rest = Resting; DT/PDT = Dt; Kite = Movement.\n• Spaces and punctuation in names are ignored (Call Beast = CallBeast).' }, { title = 'Make, save and use one', note = '• From worn gear: /vg dress (pauses swapping), equip from the menu, then /vg save <name> (or name box + New set) to resume.\n• Weapons are excluded from saved sets unless /vg weapons on.\n• Per slot: choose in the Your sets tab, or /vg set <name> <slot> <item>, e.g. /vg set Reward Body Totemic Jackcoat +1; item built reverts the slot.\n• Slot names: Main, Sub, Range, Ammo, Head, Body, Hands, Legs, Feet, Neck, Waist, Ear1, Ear2, Ring1, Ring2, Back.\n• Edits save to disk instantly; /vg sets lists your sets with piece counts.\n• /vg wear <name> (until /vg wear off), /vg with <name> <command> (one action), /vg look <name> (appearance lock), /vg remove <name> (delete).' }, { title = 'Where they are kept and sharing', note = '• Folder: Ashita config\\addons\\vanagear\\; open it with /vg folder or Open the folder.\n• sets\\<JOB>.lua (e.g. sets\\BST.lua), commands\\<JOB>.lua, commands\\ALL.lua, trusts.lua, prefs.lua (weapons, locked slots, look, zone wait, etc.).\n• A sets file returns a table of set name to slot = "item name", e.g. ["Reward"] = { Body = "Totemic Jackcoat +1" }; the item remove empties a slot.\n• To share: give the set or whole job file; the recipient puts it in their config\\addons\\vanagear\\sets\\ job file and runs /vg mine reload.\n• Shared sets only equip pieces the recipient has in inventory or wardrobes.' }, { title = 'Command reference: window and sets', note = '• Every /vg command also works as /vanagear and as /gs c <word>.\n• /vg (toggle window), /vg help, /vg build, /vg status, /vg why <set> <slot>, /vg upgrades.\n• /vg dress / /vg dress off, /vg save <name>, /vg set <name> <slot> <item>, /vg sets.\n• /vg wear <name> / off, /vg look <name> / off, /vg remove <name> (removes a command first, else a set).\n• /vg lock <slot> / /vg unlock <slot>: hold a slot as is and build around it.\n• /vg weapons on / off; /vg weapon main|sub|range <item> sets the job-wide weapon (none = leave alone, remove = unequip).\n• /vg wait <seconds>: zone wait time (default 10).' }, { title = 'Trusts', note = '• /vg trusts on / off: send gear sets to called trusts (on by default).\n• !trustgear <trust> lists sets; !trustgear <trust> <set> shows one; add clear to delete one; !trustgear <trust> clear deletes all.\n• !trustuse <trust> lists disabled actions; !trustuse <trust> off <action> / on <action> toggles a spell, ability, weapon skill or kind; !trustuse <trust> reset re-enables all.\n• ! commands are server-side and work without vanagear; use the trust name shown in the party list.' }, { title = 'LuAshitacast and GearSwap compatibility', note = '• /vg takeover copies your LuAshitacast profile\'s sets for this job into vanagear sets and hands the job to vanagear (profile file untouched).\n• /vg profile on / off: use or ignore your profile for this job.\n• /vg underlay on / off: fill slots your profile leaves empty with vanagear\'s built pieces.\n• /lac commands (load, reload, equip, disable, enable, fwd, etc.) behave as in LuAshitacast; unknown /vg words go to the profile\'s command handler.\n• GearSwap: /gs c <word> = /vg <word>; /gs c cycle OffenseMode, HybridMode, WeaponskillMode, RangedMode = /vg tp; /gs c cycle IdleMode = /vg idle; /gs c cycle CastingMode = nuke power/acc.\n• /gs c set DefenseMode ... / reset DefenseMode toggles DT gear; /gs c toggle Kiting toggles movement gear; /gs equip <set>; /gs validate lists missing pieces.\n• /vg keys mote / off binds or unbinds Motenten-style F9-F12 keys.' }, { title = 'Making your own commands', note = '• A custom command is one word that sends several lines in order; run it with /<word> or /vg <word>.\n• Line types: any game command (e.g. /ma "Cure IV" <stpc>), any vanagear command (runs immediately), wait 3 (pause 3 s).\n• then <command>: waits for the previous action to start and finish plus 3.3 s (skillchain gap).\n• burst <command>: waits for the previous action to finish, then fires with no gap (magic burst).\n• then and burst can follow /ws, /ja, /ma and /pet lines with the action name in quotes.\n• Window: /vg mine (or Your commands tab), enter the word, one line per row, tick jobs (none = this job only), Save; Examples has Use buttons; saved commands have Run, Change, Delete.\n• Chat: /vg add <word> <line>; <line> for this job, /vg add all <word> ... for every job, e.g. /vg add buffs /ma "Haste" <me>; wait 4; /ma "Refresh" <me>.\n• /vg remove <word>, /vg stop (halt a running command), /vg with <set> <command>.\n• By hand: edit commands\\<JOB>.lua or commands\\ALL.lua (word = list of lines, quotes escaped as \\"), then /vg mine reload or Read the files again; a job file entry beats the same word in ALL.lua.' } } },
    { name = 'Guide: VanaNews on Discord', group = 'Server', desc = 'Messages in the VanaNews linkshell are mirrored within seconds to the VanaNews thread on the Vanadreams Discord; the mirror is one-way. Source: https://vanadreams.org/wiki/#guide-c_vananews_discord', steps = { { title = 'Overview', note = '• VanaNews linkshell chat appears in the Discord VanaNews thread a few seconds after it is said.\n• Discord posts are not relayed into the game; reply from in game.\n• Tells are never posted.' } } },
    { name = 'Guide: VanaTunes on the website', group = 'Server', desc = 'The VanaTunes web player in the Music section of the vanadreams.org front page plays the same Vanadreams playlist heard in game and can float over the wiki. Source: https://vanadreams.org/wiki/#guide-c_vanatunes_web_player', steps = { { title = 'Overview', note = '• Location: Music section of the vanadreams.org front page, beside the downloads.\n• Pop-out button (arrow leaving a box) turns it into a floating window; drag by the title bar; it keeps its position and keeps playing while you browse the wiki.\n• Return it with the house button or "Bring the player back here" in the Music section.\n• The note button shrinks it to just a play button.\n• The wiki\'s gold "Home & download" button returns to the front page.' } } },
    { name = 'Guide: Venture Roll (Lower Jeuno Game Tables)', group = 'Server', desc = 'Venture Roll is a 2-4 player dice game at the Lower Jeuno Game Tables (H-8); the winner collects all entry fees. Source: https://vanadreams.org/wiki/#guide-c_venture_roll', steps = { { title = 'Tables', note = '• 2 players, 500 gil each: table across from the Merry Minstrel\'s Meadhouse.\n• 3 players at 2,000 gil each and 4 players at 3,000 gil each: the two tables across from Waag-Deeg\'s Magic Shop.' }, { title = 'How to play', note = '• Touch a table and pick Take a seat; the fee is charged on sitting.\n• If seats do not fill within one minute, the game is cancelled and fees refunded.\n• Once full, each player rolls one d6; these opening rolls are shown to all.\n• You then have one minute to choose at the table: Double Up (add another private d6 roll, repeatable) or Hold Fast (keep your total).\n• Exceeding 11 eliminates you immediately; anyone still in at the time limit holds automatically.' }, { title = 'Winning', note = '• Highest total of 11 or less takes the pot.\n• A tie for best total is a draw and all fees are refunded.\n• If every player busts, all fees are refunded.' } } },
    { name = 'Guide: Visiting a friend\'s Mog House', group = 'Server', desc = 'Hosts can open their Mog House to their party or alliance so others can come in and visit. Source: https://vanadreams.org/wiki/#guide-c_mog_house_visits', steps = { { title = 'Inviting (host)', note = '• Use your home-nation Mog House (not a rent-a-room) and stand on the floor to show (1F, or 2F if owned).\n• Mog House menu > Invite opens it to party and alliance, up to 17 guests.\n• Stop inviting ejects all guests; leaving, switching floors or logging out also ends the invitation.\n• You are notified whenever a guest enters.' }, { title = 'Visiting (guest)', note = '• Be in the host\'s party or alliance and in the same city.\n• Enter the Mog House entrance and choose Visit a party member\'s Mog House, then the host (Enter my Mog House goes to your own).\n• Examine the door to leave.\n• Guests may remain after the party disbands or after relogging, while the host stays inside.' }, { title = 'What guests can do', note = '• Allowed: look around, chat, trade, check bazaars.\n• Not allowed: moving furniture, gardening, using the host\'s storage; the host\'s moogle ignores guests.\n• The host\'s room and items are never affected.\n• Guests see the host\'s room style and floor, but furniture is rendered from the guest\'s own furnishings, so the host\'s decor may not appear.' } } },
    { name = 'Guide: Voidwatch Quests', group = 'Server', desc = 'The Voidwatch storyline is 19 Wings of the Goddess quests (Guardian of the Void to Ad Infinitum) ending in Provenance, plus two Aht Urhgan operations; these quests are how white and amber abyssite tiers are advanced. Source: https://vanadreams.org/wiki/#guide-c_voidwatch_quests', steps = { { title = 'Overview', note = '• 19 quests in the Wings of the Goddess (Crystal War) log, plus two Aht Urhgan log operations that open the Near East rifts.\n• White (Jeuno) and amber (Aht Urhgan) stratum abyssite tiers come from these quests; Atmacite Refiners only upgrade white I to II and IV to V.' }, { title = 'Before you start', note = '• Be level 75.\n• Join at an officer in Southern San d\'Oria, Bastok Markets or Windurst Waters, max out the crimson, indigo and jade abyssites, and defeat a Voidwalker at each; then Guardian of the Void opens.\n• Carry voidstones (from officers); every Voidwalker fight uses one.\n• Any Voidwatch Officer on the quest\'s side of time lists which required Voidwalkers remain; your log notes each qualifying kill.\n• If your abyssite already exceeds a quest\'s tier, its Voidwalkers count as done.' }, { title = '1. Guardian of the Void', note = '• Begin at the Veridical Conflux, Pashhow Marshlands [S] (J-9) near the gate crystal, with Cait Sith and Kupofried.\n• Talk to a Voidwatch Officer in present-day Southern San d\'Oria, Bastok Markets or Windurst Waters (no other officers).\n• Reward: Voidwatch alarum.' }, { title = '2. Drafted by the Duchy', note = '• Report to the Audience Chamber door, Ru\'Lude Gardens (H-6), or the Bulwark Gate, Sauromugue Champaign [S] (F-6).\n• Rewards: white stratum abyssite, Voidwatcher\'s emblem: Jeuno, periapt of emergence (second atmacite slot).' }, { title = '3. Battle on a New Front', note = '• Defeat the six tier I Voidwalkers: Cherufe (Batallia Downs), Taweret (Batallia Downs [S]) at G-8, I-9, J-10; Yatagarasu (Rolanberry Fields), Agathos (Rolanberry Fields [S]) at E-10, F-8, G-7; Goji (Sauromugue Champaign), Gugalanna (Sauromugue Champaign [S]) at G-6, I-6, K-10.\n• Upgrade to white stratum abyssite II at any Atmacite Refiner.\n• Defeat the six tier II Voidwalkers: Gasha (The Eldieme Necropolis), Giltine (The Eldieme Necropolis [S]), Mellonia (Crawlers\' Nest), Nympha Eunomia (Crawlers\' Nest [S]), Roly-Poly (Garlaige Citadel), Laidly Laurence (Garlaige Citadel [S]).\n• Get a Voidwatch alarum from any Voidwatch Officer, present or past (not Kieran, Owain or other named field officers).\n• Report to the Audience Chamber, Ru\'Lude Gardens.\n• Rewards: white stratum abyssite III, Voidwatcher\'s emblem: Qufim.\n• Then collect 30,000 gil from the Bulwark Gate sentries in Sauromugue Champaign [S] before No Rest for the Weary, which starts from it.' }, { title = '4. VW Op. 126: Qufim Incursion', note = '• Defeat the tier III Voidwalkers: Kaggen (Qufim Island G-6, H-6, I-7), Akvan (Lower Delkfutt\'s Tower: Basement G-9, 2F F-5/6, 3F I-6), Pil (Behemoth\'s Dominion E-7, H-8, J-10).\n• Get a Voidwatch alarum from a present-day officer.\n• Report to the Audience Chamber, Ru\'Lude Gardens.\n• Reward: 50,000 gil.' }, { title = '5. A Cait Calls', note = '• Examine the Veridical Conflux in Pashhow Marshlands [S].' }, { title = '6. The Truth Is Out There', note = '• Talk to any present-day Voidwatch Officer.\n• Reward: Voidwatch alarum.' }, { title = '7. Re-Drafted by the Duchy', note = '• Report to the Audience Chamber, Ru\'Lude Gardens.\n• Rewards: white stratum abyssite IV, tricolor Voidwatcher\'s emblem.' }, { title = '8. A New Menace', note = '• Defeat the tier IV Voidwalkers: Lancing Lamorak (West Ronfaure H-6, H-8, H-10), Bhishani (South Gustaberg J-10, K-7, L-9), Rw Nw Prt M Hrw (East Sarutabaruta G-11, H-6, J-5).\n• Upgrade to white stratum abyssite V at any Atmacite Refiner.\n• Defeat the tier V Voidwalkers: Stachysaurus (La Theine Plateau E-5, I-11, L-8), Gwynn Ap Nudd (Konschtat Highlands G-4, I-11, J-8), Smierc (Tahrongi Canyon I-9, I-12, J-6).\n• Get a Voidwatch alarum from a present-day officer.\n• Report to the Audience Chamber, Ru\'Lude Gardens.\n• Reward: 50,000 gil.' }, { title = '9. No Rest for the Weary', note = '• If not yet done, collect the sentries\' 30,000 gil at the Bulwark Gate, Sauromugue Champaign [S] (F-6).\n• After the next Vana\'diel day, get a Voidwatch alarum from a past (S) Voidwatch Officer.\n• Report to the Bulwark Gate.\n• Rewards: white stratum abyssite VI, starlight Voidwatcher\'s emblem.' }, { title = '10. A World in Flux', note = '• Defeat the tier VI Voidwalkers: Gaunab (Vunkerl Inlet [S] F-5, G-8, G-13), Ocythoe (Grauberg [S] D-14, G-7, G-11), Kalasutrax (Fort Karugo-Narugo [S] D-12, I-11, K-8).\n• Get a Voidwatch alarum from a past (S) officer.\n• Report to the Bulwark Gate, Sauromugue Champaign [S].\n• Reward: 30,000 gil.' }, { title = '11. Between a Rock and Rift', note = '• Examine the Veridical Conflux in Pashhow Marshlands [S].' }, { title = '12. A Farewell to Felines', note = '• After the next Vana\'diel day, talk to any Voidwatch Officer.\n• Reward: Voidwatch alarum.' }, { title = '13. Third Tour of Duchy', note = '• Report to the Audience Chamber, Ru\'Lude Gardens, or the Bulwark Gate, Sauromugue Champaign [S].' }, { title = '14. Glimmer of Hope', note = '• With at least one voidstone, examine the Pashhow Marshlands [S] Veridical Conflux to reach the Walk of Echoes.\n• Examine the faint glimmer (???) just north of the arrival point; it consumes the voidstone.\n• Reward: Kupofried\'s corundum.' }, { title = '15. Brace for the Unknown', note = '• Examine the glimmer again (or the Pashhow conflux if you left) to enter Provenance.\n• Rewards: the Clairvoy ant; the Pashhow conflux now grants Provenance access.' }, { title = '16. Provenance', note = '• Collect the three petrifacts, rare finds in Jeuno path pyxides and these city/region pyxides: Beguiling (Zilart), Seductive (Tavnazia), Maddening (Aht Urhgan).\n• Alternatively buy a missing one from a Voidwatch Officer for 330,000 cruor (talk twice to confirm).\n• After each petrifact, examine the Regal Pawprints at the Provenance entrance; several at once show all visions together.\n• With all three, examine the Provenance Protocrystal next to the entrance.' }, { title = '17. Crystal Guardian', note = '• Defeat Pil first to open the Watcher\'s protocrystal.\n• Defeat the Provenance Watcher while holding all three petrifacts; they are consumed on the kill and players missing any get no credit.\n• Examine the Regal Pawprints.\n• Reward: title Witness to Provenance.\n• Officers sell replacement petrifacts for another attempt.' }, { title = '18. Endings and Beginnings', note = '• Exit Provenance via the Planar Rift at the entrance.' }, { title = '19. Ad Infinitum', note = '• Final quest; it remains in your current quest list permanently.' }, { title = 'VW Op. 050: Aht Urhgan Assault', note = '• Requirements: level 75 and the Adventurer\'s Certificate.\n• Leave Aht Urhgan Whitegate through the Ironbound Gate (H-10) and talk to Camille in Wajaom Woodlands (M-7) for the amber stratum abyssite.\n• Defeat the Near East Voidwalkers: Dimgruzub (Arrapago Reef G-8, G-10, I-10), Brekekekex (Caedarva Mire F-11, I-9, I-11), Yalungur (Mamook I-7, J-8, L-8), Vanasarvik (Mount Zhayolm M-6, J-8, L-8).\n• Report to Camille; VW Op. 068 begins immediately.\n• Reward: amber stratum abyssite II.' }, { title = 'VW Op. 068: Subterranean Skirmish', note = '• Defeat Morta in Aydeewa Subterrane and report to Camille.\n• Afterward, Sujyahn in Al Zahbi sends new Voidwatchers to Camille rather than giving out amber abyssite.' } } },
    { name = 'Guide: Walk of Echoes Weapons (Magian Trials)', group = 'Server', desc = 'Fourteen Walk of Echoes weapons come from Magian Trials, either from free "-1" starter weapons or by upgrading level 80 coin weapons. Source: https://vanadreams.org/wiki/#guide-c_walk_of_echoes_weapons', steps = { { title = 'Overview', note = '• Weapons: Dumuzis, Khandroma, Brunello, Xiphias, Sacripante, Shamash, Umiliati, Daboya, Kasasagi, Torigashira-no-Tachi, Rose Couverte, Paikea, Circinae, Mollfrith.' }, { title = 'Where', note = '• Zone: Ru\'Lude Gardens, west side near the palace stairs (approx. H-5, position -12, 118).\n• Magian Moogle (orange, weapons): begins and completes trials; first talk grants the Magian Trial Log (level 75+).\n• Delivery Crate: turn in trial items here.\n• Splintery Chest: free starter weapons; the "-1" Walk of Echoes weapons are on page 3.' }, { title = 'Easy route: the "-1" weapons (3 trials)', note = '• Take your chosen "-1" weapon (e.g. Dumuzis -1) from page 3 of the Splintery Chest at no cost.\n• Trade it to the Magian Moogle and accept trial 1.\n• Trade weapon + 30 coins to the Delivery Crate, then return the weapon to the Moogle; result: Attack +3 (Ranged Attack +3 on Circinae/Mollfrith).\n• Begin trial 2 at the Moogle, turn in 100 Devious Dice at the Crate, complete at the Moogle (Attack +5).\n• Begin trial 3, turn in 100 Liminal Residue at the Crate, complete at the Moogle to receive the finished weapon.\n• Items may be turned in over multiple trades, any quantity per trade.\n• Weapon | Coin | Trial numbers\n• Dumuzis (H2H) | Coin of Advancement | 3643, 3644, 3645\n• Khandroma (Dagger) | Coin of Birth | 3647, 3648, 3649\n• Brunello (Sword) | Coin of Glory | 3651, 3652, 3653\n• Xiphias (Great Sword) | Coin of Decay | 3655, 3656, 3657\n• Sacripante (Axe) | Coin of Advancement | 3659, 3660, 3661\n• Shamash (Great Axe) | Coin of Glory | 3663, 3664, 3665\n• Umiliati (Scythe) | Coin of Birth | 3667, 3668, 3669\n• Daboya (Polearm) | Coin of Advancement | 3671, 3672, 3673\n• Kasasagi (Katana) | Coin of Glory | 3675, 3676, 3677\n• Torigashira-no-Tachi (Great Katana) | Coin of Decay | 3679, 3680, 3681\n• Rose Couverte (Club) | Coin of Decay | 3683, 3684, 3685\n• Paikea (Staff) | Coin of Ruin | 3687, 3688, 3689\n• Circinae (Archery) | Coin of Decay | 3691, 3692, 3693\n• Mollfrith (Marksmanship) | Coin of Birth | 3695, 3696, 3697' }, { title = 'Long route: the coin weapons (+1 / +2 / +3)', note = '• Upgrade path from an owned level 80 coin weapon (e.g. Revenant Fists): +1 = 15 Beastmen\'s Seals; +2 = 20 Kindred\'s Seals; +3 = 35 Devious Dice; Walk of Echoes weapon = 35 Liminal Residue.\n• Currently only Revenant Fists (to Dumuzis) can start from scratch; other coin weapons lack the level 80 step, so use the "-1" route for them.' }, { title = 'Where the items come from', note = '• Coins (Birth, Advancement, Glory, Decay, Ruin): monster drops across many zones.\n• Devious Dice: any Walk of Echoes Treasure Coffer; Liminal Residue: coffers of Walks 8–15.\n• Frayed Sack (D) / Frayed Sack (L) drop in Walk of Echoes; each opens into 10–20 Devious Dice or 10–20 Liminal Residue.\n• With half-cost upgrades enabled, required counts are halved, rounding up.' }, { title = 'The Walk\'s Treasure Coffer', note = '• After a cleared Walk, the coffer beside the Echo yields 2–5 items: 2 base for being present at the end, +1 per 6 evaluation points, max 5; each item rolls independently on that Walk\'s table.\n• Dice and Residue drop in stacks of 2–4.\n• Per-draw rates (Walk: Dice / Residue): 1: 8.7%; 2: 6.7%; 3: 9.0%; 4: 7.6%; 5: 8.2%; 6: 8.1%; 7: 6.6%; 8: 8.8% / 4.4%; 9: 7.1% / 3.5%; 10: 9.1% / 4.5%; 11: 8.0% / 4.0%; 12: 8.9% / 8.9%; 13: 9.7% / 9.7%; 14: 9.1% / 9.1%; 15: 8.2% / 8.2%.\n• Walk 2: Scroll of Shell V 2.0%.\n• Walk 3: Scroll of Stone V 2.7%; Carnelian, Clarite, Chunk of Durium Ore 1.8% each.\n• Walk 4: Scroll of Shell V and Scroll of Stone V 2.3% each; Clarite 1.5%.\n• Walk 5: Scroll of Shell V and Scroll of Stone V 2.5% each; Carnelian, Clarite, Chunk of Phrygian Ore, Chunk of Durium Ore 1.6% each.\n• Walk 7: Scroll of Shell V 2.0%; Carnelian, Clarite 1.3% each.\n• Walk 10: Dualism Collar 5.5%.' } } },
    { name = 'Guide: Waughroon Shrine battlefields', group = 'Server', desc = 'Waughroon Shrine (reached via Palborough Mines) battlefields with entry items, caps, enemies, mechanics and rewards. Source: https://vanadreams.org/wiki/#guide-c_battlefields_waughroon_shrine', steps = { { title = 'Overview', note = '• Entry: trade the orb or testimony at the arena entrance, or examine it while holding the key item.\n• No-Trust fights dismiss summoned Trusts on entry and block calling them; where allowed, each Trust fills a party slot.\n• Fight | Entry | Level cap | Party | Time | Trusts\n• Crustacean Conundrum | Cloudy Orb | 20 | 3 | 15 min | No\n• Birds of a Feather | Sky Orb | 30 | 3 | 15 min | No\n• Grove Guardians | Sky Orb | 30 | 6 | 30 min | No\n• The Worm\'s Turn | Star Orb | 40 | 6 | 30 min | No\n• Royal Jelly | Star Orb | 40 | 3 | 15 min | No\n• 3, 2, 1... | Comet Orb | 50 | 6 | 30 min | No\n• The Final Bout | Comet Orb | 50 | 3 | 3 min | No\n• Grimshell Shocktroopers | Moon Orb | 60 | 6 | 30 min | No\n• Up in Arms | Moon Orb | 60 | 3 | 15 min | No\n• Copycat | Clotho Orb | none | 6 | 30 min | No\n• Operation Desert Swarm | Lachesis Orb | none | 6 | 30 min | No\n• Prehistoric Pigeons | Atropos Orb | none | 6 | 30 min | No\n• The Hills are Alive | Themis Orb | none | 18 | 30 min | No\n• The Palborough Project | Phobos Orb | none | 3 | 15 min | No\n• Shell Shocked | Deimos Orb | none | 6 | 30 min | No\n• ★The Worm\'s Tail | Microcosmic Orb | none | 6 | 30 min | Yes\n• ★Grimshell Shocktroopers | Macrocosmic Orb | none | 6 | 30 min | Yes\n• A.M.A.N. Trove (Mars / Venus) | Mars Orb / Venus Orb | none | 6 | 30 min | Yes\n• Invitation from Naji (solo / and Co.) | Invitation from Naji | none | 6 | 30 min | Yes\n• The Rank 2 Final Mission | mission | 99 | 6 | 15 min | Yes\n• On My Way | Bastok mission | 99 | 6 | 30 min | Yes\n• A Thief in Norg!? | Banishing Charm (kept) | none | 6 | 30 min | No\n• Beyond Infinity | Soul Gem Clasp | 99 | 6 | 10 min | Yes\n• Shattering Stars (RDM, THF, BST) | job testimony | 99, no subjob | 1 | 10 min | No' }, { title = 'Crustacean Conundrum', note = '• Heavy Metal Crab (Lv22 RDM: Waterga, Bio, Blind; 30 HP) and Metal Crab (Lv19; 15 HP).\n• Every hit, WS hit or spell deals at most 1 damage; DoTs do nothing; their melee can drain 30 HP; moves: Bubble Shower, Bubble Curtain, Big Scissors, Scissor Guard.\n• Bring high hit-count jobs (dual wield, double attack, H2H, multi-hit WS; each landed WS hit counts once); kill Metal Crab (15 hits), then Heavy Metal Crab (30 hits); WHM heals through Waterga.\n• Rewards: 1,500 gil, Crab Shell, Mannequin Body every win, small chance of Mannequin Hands.' }, { title = 'Birds of a Feather', note = '• Macha (Lv32 RDM bird): Dispelga, Sleep; immune to Sleep. Neman (Lv30): charmable, adds Wing Cutter. Both: Helldive, Damnation Dive, Barrage moves.\n• Kill Macha first; a BST can charm Neman to attack her; keep someone free to wake sleepers.\n• Rewards: 3,000 gil, Bird Feathers, job belts and earrings, scrolls.' }, { title = 'Grove Guardians', note = '• Metsanneitsyt (Lv36 queen: Stonega, Stone II, Aspir, Drain; resists Silence) plus two Metsanhaltija (Lv32–33); none can be slept; moves Sprout Spin, Slumber Powder, Sprout Smack.\n• If the queen is over 10 yalms from any living guardian, she builds TP rapidly and spams moves.\n• Tank the queen where the guardians stand, kill both guardians, then the queen.\n• Rewards: 4,000 gil, job mantles and shields, scrolls, Mannequin Body.' }, { title = 'The Worm\'s Turn', note = '• Flayer Franz (Lv45) + 15 Flesh Eaters (Lv38–40), all linking worms; spells Stone II, Stonega, Rasp, Bind, Stoneskin; moves Full-Force Blow, Gastric Bomb, Sandspin, Tremors, MP Absorption, Sound Vacuum.\n• Franz: no sleep or silence; draws back distant players. Flesh Eaters are charmable.\n• All worms must die: tank Franz, sleep and kill Flesh Eaters a few at a time, Franz last; melee must chase ranged casters; AoE sleep and charm help.\n• Rewards: 6,000 gil; roughly 50% rolls each for Spirit Torque, Nemesis Earring, Earth Mantle, Strike Shield.' }, { title = 'Royal Jelly', note = '• Eight Princess Jellies (Lv35), one per element: absorb their own element, weak to its opposite; cast Bind plus that element\'s enfeeble and nuke; unsleepable.\n• Once engaged each creeps to the arena centre and is undamageable there; when all living ones arrive they fuse into Queen Jelly (Lv41, pooled HP, fast TP, all elements plus Bindga).\n• Kill princesses before they reach the centre; melee is safest; nukers check each one\'s element first.\n• Rewards: 5,000 gil, Marksman\'s Ring, Mana Ring, Archer\'s Ring, weapons incl. Dusky Staff, Sealed Mace, Shikar Bow, Grudge Sword.' }, { title = '3, 2, 1...', note = '• Time Bomb (Lv55, 9999 HP): stationary, no attacks or TP moves; immune to sleep, stun, bind, paralyze, petrify, gravity.\n• A 60-second countdown starts on engage; at zero it self-destructs, wiping the party (loss).\n• Six pre-buffed DDs, TP up if possible; open with top WS and two-hours together; skillchain + magic burst.\n• Rewards: 12,000 gil, Bomb Arm (~50%), Kageboshi or Odenta every win, elemental belt.' }, { title = 'The Final Bout', note = '• The Waughroon Kid (Lv53 MNK goobbue): strong melee, regen, hits may Weight; Blow, Beatdown, Uppercut, Blank Gaze (Blow and Blank Gaze always used twice in a row); Counterstance at 40% HP.\n• 3-minute limit: three heavy DDs; turn away after the first Blank Gaze; after Counterstance finish with WS rather than long melee.\n• Rewards: 8,000 gil, Boyahda Moss, two items from mantles, gorgets, hands and head pieces.' }, { title = 'Grimshell Shocktroopers', note = '• Six linked quadav (Lv62–64), strongly sleep resistant, two-hour below ~50% HP; moves Ore Toss, Head Butt, Shell Bash, Shell Guard, Howl.\n• Yo\'Bhu Hideousmask WAR (Mighty Strikes); Zo\'Dhu Legslicer WHM (heals, Silence, Paralyze, Benediction); Ka\'Nha Jabbertongue BLM (-ga II, Flare, Burst, Flood, Sleepga, Stun, Manafont); Bi\'Fho Jestergrin THF (Perfect Dodge); Ku\'Tya Hotblood PLD (heals, Flash, Invincible); Ea\'Tho Cruelheart DRK (Absorb spells, Stun, Blood Weapon).\n• Kill Zo\'Dhu, Ka\'Nha, Ku\'Tya, then the three melee; silence casters; a PLD or NIN tank holds the rest; only take one under half if you can kill it during its two-hour.\n• Rewards: 18,000 gil; Archalaus\'s Pole, Chicken Knife, Fey Wand, Vassago\'s Scythe; Assault Earring, Enhancing Mantle or Astral Shield.' }, { title = 'Up in Arms', note = '• Fe\'e (Lv62 sea monk): six tentacles, very fast attacks with frequent double attack; loses one at 88/77/66/55/44/33% HP, each loss slowing its attacks but making hits stronger.\n• With tentacles: Ink Jet. Under 33%: normal attacks become ink, TP move Maelstrom. Against a target 12+ yalms away it may use Hard Membrane or Regeneration.\n• Sleep, Bind and Gravity work: RDM/SCH kite with Gravity and tier II nukes, sleeping it to rest MP; with a tank, use Blind/Paralyze, expect the heaviest damage mid-fight, burn the last third fast.\n• Rewards: 15,000 gil, Black Pearl, Teleport Ring: Altep, Teleport Ring: Dem, Ajari Bead Necklace, Philomath Stole, Walkure Mask, very rare Kraken Club.' }, { title = 'Copycat', note = '• Osschaart (Lv79 ahriman): double attack, tier III -ga, elemental debuffs, Drain, Aspir, Bio II, Bind, Stun, Blaze Spikes; hard to silence; moves Blindeye, Eyes On Me, Hypnosis, Mind Break, Binding Wave, Airy Shield, Magic Barrier, Level 5 Petrify.\n• On engage he randomizes a charm order and charms the next player every 30 s (pulling distant ones in); he copies the last charmed player\'s job and uses its two-hour once at a random point between 65% and 20% HP (Benediction = full heal; Invincible/Perfect Dodge = stall; BST/DRG/PUP = bat/wyvern/automaton; SMN = avatar).\n• Favour jobs whose two-hours are harmless to copy, bring two tanks and two healers, and have lullaby or sleep for charmed allies; if a WHM or PLD was just charmed, wait one cycle before pushing him under 65%.\n• Rewards: 24,000 gil; one of Coffinmaker, Destroyers, Expunger, Retributor; one of Durandal, Hoplite\'s Harpe, Sorrowful Harp, Attila\'s Earring; Fuma Sune-Ate.' }, { title = 'Operation Desert Swarm', note = '• Six linked Platoon Scorpions (Lv73); only moves are Wild Rage and Earth Pounder.\n• When one uses a TP move, every other scorpion at 1000+ TP repeats it immediately.\n• After Wild Rage a scorpion stops auto-attacking 10–25 s; after Earth Pounder it can\'t move 10–25 s. Wild Rage gets stronger per dead scorpion.\n• Spread damage so they die close together; keep TP low (Absorb-TP, sleep, minimal melee contact); use the post-move windows; Bind, Gravity and sleep split the pack.\n• Rewards: 24,000 gil, High-Quality Scorpion Shell, Serket Ring, Venomous Claw, Anubis\'s Knife, plus one of Expunger, Heart Snatcher, Rampager, Senjuinrikio.' }, { title = 'Prehistoric Pigeons', note = '• Four Titanis (Lv76 BRD rocs), very sleep resistant, gain TP on their own; moves Feather Barrier, Stormwind, Blind Vortex, Giga Scream, Dread Dive.\n• Max: Minne, Minuet. Jax: Paeon, Carols. Xax: March, Elegy (on players). Dax: Foe Lullaby, Magic Finale (on players).\n• At 60% HP each uses Soul Voice, then stronger songs (Horde Lullaby, Victory March, Carnage Elegy, etc.); each death gives survivors more haste and damage.\n• Kill order: Dax, Xax, Max, Jax; drop the last two close together; Dispel/Finale their buffs; save two-hours for the final bird.\n• Rewards: 24,000 gil; one of Michishiba-no-Tsuyu, Dissector, Coffinmaker, Gravedigger; Titanis Earring.' }, { title = 'The Hills are Alive', note = '• Tartaruga Gigante (Lv85 adamantoise): heavy double-attack melee; Tortoise Song, Head Butt, Tortoise Stomp, Harden Shell, Earth Breath, Aqua Breath; always takes 30% less magic damage; immune to sleep, stun, slow, petrify.\n• Every 2,000 HP lost it toggles its shell; entering clears its debuffs. In shell: no moving, turning or melee, near-immune to physical/ranged, fast regen, casts Flood, Waterga IV, Silencega, Slowga.\n• It exits after 90 s, at full HP, or after another 2,000 damage, always with full TP.\n• Melee while it is out, nuke while it is in; track damage; ready shadows/cures for exit TP moves; reapply debuffs after each shell.\n• Rewards: 32,000 gil, Blue Pondweed, two weapons or Abjurations, Adaman Chain, Adamantoise Shell, Strider Boots, Angel Skin, Princely Sword.' }, { title = 'The Palborough Project', note = '• Mahuika (Lv80 bomb, unsleepable): Berserk, Vulcanian Impact, Heat Wave, Hellstorm; each Hellstorm/Vulcanian Impact spawns 1–2 Nga Manawa (Lv75, ~1,000 HP) that self-destruct 30–45 s after appearing.\n• Killing Mahuika wins even with adds still alive.\n• Focus Mahuika; kill an add only if it will blow up next to the healer, otherwise move away; fire resistance helps.\n• Rewards: Fracas Grenade or Fervor Ring (or a Fewell orb), small chance of a seal pattern, ingots, gems, medicines.' }, { title = 'Shell Shocked', note = '• Four unsleepable Lv82 quadav: Vu\'Dhe Impervious (PLD), Ga\'Khu Bloodglee (DRK), Zi\'Pha Foecrippler (RDM), Ro\'Mho Unrelenting (BLM); two-hours below ~50%; standard quadav moves.\n• All four must die: Ro\'Mho, then Zi\'Pha, while a tank holds the melee pair; Silence and Stun the BLM.\n• Rewards: two One Byne Bills, high-level magic scroll, medicine, seal pattern, plus Barbican Axe, Calmecac Leggings, a One Hundred Byne Bill or a Fewell orb.' }, { title = '★ fights', note = '• Microcosmic enemies are Lv107, Macrocosmic Lv109; Trusts allowed.' }, { title = '★The Worm\'s Tail', note = '• Flayer Franz + 15 Flesh Eaters at Lv107, same kit as The Worm\'s Turn; Franz has far more HP.\n• Tank Franz, clear Flesh Eaters with AoE, Franz last; tank, healer and support Trusts suit a small group.\n• Rewards: 20,000 gil; one of Aiwon Gauntlets, Earthcry Mantle, Jwalamukhi Ring, Dosis Tathlum; scrolls, Geomancy plates, Fewells; Beitetsu, Riftborn Boulder, Pluton.' }, { title = '★Grimshell Shocktroopers', note = '• Same six quadav at Lv109 with identical spells, heals and two-hours.\n• Same order: Zo\'Dhu, Ka\'Nha, Ku\'Tya, then melee; bring a tank, a healer (players or Trusts) and one or two strong DDs.\n• Rewards: 30,000 gil; one of Parashu, Tabahi Fleuret, Qasama Hexagun, Anaimatos Scythe, Mistilteinn; scrolls, Geomancy plates, Fewells; Rem\'s Tale Chapter 5, Reisenjima materials.' }, { title = 'A.M.A.N. Trove (Mars Orb / Venus Orb)', note = '• Arena holds ten wooden chests plus the Terminal Coffer; examine a chest within 4 yalms to open it.\n• Each opened chest adds a coffer slot; a louder sound means a better slot.\n• One chest is a mimic (Lv125 BLM/DRK, half physical damage, Death Trap); opening it or attacking any closed chest springs it, removing other chests and hiding the coffer until it dies.\n• Opening the Terminal Coffer rolls the loot and wins; kill the mimic with magic, or open the coffer early to keep current slots.\n• Venus Orb has better odds and always includes at least one equipment slot.\n• Rewards: materials, Geomancy plates, crystals; Lv119 gear (loud slots); trove-only accessories (very loud); tiny chance of 5,000,000 gil; 1,000 capacity points per winner; killing the Venus mimic grants the title Mimic Masher.' }, { title = 'Invitation from Naji', note = '• Entry consumes the Invitation from Naji key item; no cap, 6 players, 30 min, Trusts OK.\n• Naji (Lv99 WAR): Burning Blade, Red Lotus Blade, Vorpal Blade; Mighty Strikes below ~50%.\n• Easy for a Lv99 player with tank and healer Trusts.\n• Reward: one Dial Key #ANV.' }, { title = 'Invitation from Naji and Co.', note = '• Same key item, consumed on entry. Naji, Kupipi and Excenmille, all Lv125.\n• Naji: WAR weapon skills, Mighty Strikes. Kupipi (WHM): cures, -na spells, Protectra, Shellra, Slow, Paralyze, Flash, Starlight, Moonlight, Benediction. Excenmille (PLD): Cure, Flash, Double Thrust, Leg Sweep, Penta Thrust, Invincible.\n• Kill Kupipi first (silence her if possible), then Naji, then Excenmille; a full Trust group behind a strong tank works; hold burst until after Benediction.\n• Reward: two Dial Keys #ANV per enemy defeated.' }, { title = 'The Rank 2 Final Mission', note = '• For San d\'Oria and Windurst players on the Bastok leg; Lv99 cap, 6 players, 15 min, Trusts OK.\n• Dark Dragon (Lv25): Wind Breath, Heavy Stomp, Petro Eyes, Thornsong; immune to gravity, paralyze, silence; pulls back distant players. Seeker (Lv23 BLM ahriman) retreats to cast when hurt.\n• Kill Seeker, then the dragon; face away from Petro Eyes.\n• Reward: mission progress, title Dark Dragon Slayer.' }, { title = 'On My Way', note = '• Bastok mission; Lv99 cap, 6 players, 30 min, Trusts OK.\n• Four Lv68 quadav: Ku\'Jhu Graniteskin, Sa\'Nha Soulsaver (WHM), Da\'Shu Knightslayer (RDM), Go\'Bha Slaughterer (DRK); two-hours below ~50%.\n• Kill Sa\'Nha, then Da\'Shu, then the melee.\n• Reward: mission progress.' }, { title = 'A Thief in Norg!?', note = '• Banishing Charm is kept on entry; only the leader needs the quest step; no cap, 6 players, 30 min, no Trusts.\n• Three kindred immune to sleep, silence and terror; moves Soul Drain, Hecatomb Wave, Demonic Howl, Condemnation, Quadrastrike.\n• Gaki (Lv62 BLM, Manafont); Rasetsu (Lv63 DRK, Blood Weapon); Onki (Lv61 SMN) with Onibi (Lv55 fire elemental), Astral Flow calls an avatar.\n• Kill Gaki, then Onki, then Rasetsu; keep a tank on Rasetsu and the healer ready for Astral Flow.\n• Reward: quest progress.' }, { title = 'Beyond Infinity', note = '• Leader needs the Soul Gem Clasp key item; Lv99 cap, 6 players, 10 min, Trusts OK; no EXP loss on death.\n• Atori-Tutori (Lv102 MNK): Howling Fist, Asuran Fists, Final Heaven, Ascetic\'s Fury, Victory Smite; Hundred Fists below 35%.\n• Tank with shadows or a sturdy tank Trust plus a healer Trust; save your two-hour or biggest WS for below 35% to cut Hundred Fists short.\n• Reward: level-cap quest progress.' }, { title = 'Shattering Stars (Red Mage, Thief, Beastmaster)', note = '• Trade the job\'s testimony (Red Mage\'s, Thief\'s or Beastmaster\'s) as that job at Lv65+ on the quest; Lv99 cap, no subjob, solo, 10 min.\n• Maat (Lv70) can\'t be killed: win by getting him under 20% HP, or by stealing from him on the Thief version.\n• Each hit of 400+ strengthens his attacks; five minutes after engaging he gains TP very fast and repeats Asuran Fists.\n• RDM: Chainspell at 55–60%; nukes, enfeebles, Dispel, Enwater; resists Silence and Gravity.\n• THF: Perfect Dodge at 55–60%; a successful Steal wins.\n• BST: Familiar at 90–95%; random pet (rabbit, mandragora, tiger, beetle or damselfly) after 10 s, and again 30 s after each pet dies.\n• Finish within five minutes keeping hits under 400. RDM: Slow, Paralyze, Blind, enspell melee. THF: Steal first. BST: tie up or kill his pet and focus Maat.\n• Reward: the quest step that raises your level cap.' } } },
    { name = 'Guide: Wearing your support job\'s gear', group = 'Server', desc = 'Vanadreams lets your main job equip any gear your support job can use, with level, race and skill limits. Source: https://vanadreams.org/wiki/#guide-c_support_job_gear', steps = { { title = 'Overview', note = '• Main job may equip weapons and armour usable by its support job (e.g. BLM/WAR with a great axe; WHM/PLD in PLD armour with a PLD shield).' }, { title = 'How it works', note = '• Allowed: anything equippable by either the main or the support job.\n• Item level requirements check your main job level.\n• Race-restricted gear stays race-restricted.\n• Changing or losing the support job (Mog House job change, battlefield support-job restriction, Obliviscence) unequips support-only pieces.' }, { title = 'Skill from borrowed weapons', note = '• Support-job weapon types cap at 80% of the support job\'s skill cap at your main job level, unless your main job\'s own cap is higher.\n• Covers melee weapons, Archery, Marksmanship, Throwing, Shield, and support-only hand-to-hand (e.g. BLM/MNK).\n• Skill rises normally in combat up to that 80% cap.\n• Weapon skills unlock by skill level; the support job\'s main-job-only weapon skills remain locked.' }, { title = 'Putting the gear on', note = '• Requires your own vanagear sets (vanagear 0.1.7+, on by default in the launcher); the game\'s equipment menu and vanagear\'s built sets use main-job gear only.\n• Type /vg and open one of your sets or create one with New set; each slot list includes support-job items, and picks are saved to the set.\n• From chat: /vg set Axe Main Great Axe, then /vg wear Axe; stop with /vg wear off.\n• For a single action, name a set after a weapon skill, spell or ability (e.g. Shield Break) to equip it only for that action, or use /vg with <set> <command>, e.g. /vg with Axe /ws "Shield Break" <t>.\n• Equipped pieces show in the equipment window normally.' } } },
    { name = 'Guide: Western Adoulin Side Quests', group = 'Server', desc = 'Seekers of Adoulin side quests that begin in Western Adoulin: Geomancer (Sylvie), Svenja\'s manor, the Mummers\' Tarutaru Sauce, Amchuchu\'s vegetables, Pioneers\' Coalition tasks and the Rune Fencer Ergon weapon. Source: https://vanadreams.org/wiki/#guide-c_adoulin_side_quests_west', steps = { { title = 'Overview', note = '• Grid squares refer to Western Adoulin unless a zone is given.\n• Many follow-ups only unlock after the Vana\'diel day changes; if an NPC has nothing new, come back later.' }, { title = 'Elementary, My Dear Sylvie', note = '• Needs GEO main, level 66+, Dances with Luopans done; Sylvie stands at Adoulin Waterfront (I-5).\n• Speak to Sylvie, then Dabnorrin at Morimar Basalt Fields Frontier Bivouac #1 for key item Vessel of Summoning (he replaces it if you lose).\n• As GEO, use it at the Primordial Convergence K-6 (approach via J-6) to spawn Burgeoning Flames (Lv75); check again after the kill.\n• Rewards: 3,000 bayld, title Geomancipator, level cap raised to 75.' }, { title = 'For Whom the Bell Tolls', note = '• Needs GEO 90+ and a game-day wait.\n• Sylvie, then Nhili Uvolep (Eastern Adoulin I-7), then Vestavius (Morimar frontier station K-10).\n• Morimar J-6 Ergon Locus ???: get key item Silver Luopan, check again to fight Deranged Ameretat, check once more after.\n• Report to Sylvie. Rewards: Filiae Bell, Dowser\'s Wand.' }, { title = 'The Bloodline of Zacariah', note = '• After a game-day wait, speak to Sylvie and trade her 3 Chunks of Acuex Ore (Acuex in Cirdas Caverns, or AH).\n• Check the Overgrown Grave in Cirdas Caverns (M-8/9), then see Nhili Uvolep (Eastern Adoulin I-7).\n• Reward: Geomancy Mitaines.' }, { title = 'The Communion', note = '• After a game-day wait, speak to Sylvie; Nhili Uvolep hands over key item Lhaiso Neftereh\'s Bell.\n• Overgrown Grave (Cirdas M-8/9): check for scene, check to fight Ancestral Rage, check after.\n• Report to Sylvie. Rewards: Geomancy Pants, title Storied Geomancer.' }, { title = 'Treasures of the Earth (Azimuth Coat)', note = '• Needs GEO 99, The Communion done, any Bagua armor piece held in any bag.\n• Sylvie, then Morimar Ergon Locus ??? J-6 and the ??? at H-6, then back to Sylvie to choose a crystal.\n• Holla Crystal of Gales: La Theine Plateau locus, Otherworldly Rimester Lv109.\n• Dem Crystal of Dunes: Konschtat Highlands locus, Lv125.\n• Mea Crystal of Flames: Tahrongi Canyon locus, Lv135 (also gives title Lifecycler).\n• Win to get key item Pale Azure Cloth (whole party on the step gets it); crystal is consumed; Sylvie gives another if you lose.\n• Report to Sylvie, Wescolina (H-7), Helina in Selbina; wait a game day and speak to Helina again.\n• Rewards: Azimuth Coat, 15,000 EXP. One rematch crystal from Sylvie per conquest week afterwards.' }, { title = 'Azimuth tailoring (Helina)', note = '• Trade a material set to Helina for an order slip; collect the next Vana\'diel day; one order at a time.\n• Hood: Dragua\'s Scale, Siren\'s Hair, Khroma Ore, or 20 High-Purity Bayld.\n• Coat: Dragua\'s Scale, Arachne Thread, Star Sapphire, or 30.\n• Gloves: Dragua\'s Scale, Siren\'s Hair, Fiendish Skin, or 15.\n• Tights: Dragua\'s Scale, Siren\'s Hair, Arachne Thread, or 10.\n• Gaiters: Dragua\'s Scale, Fiendish Skin, Arachne Thread, or 25.' }, { title = 'Svenja\'s chain', note = '• All start at Door: Svenja\'s Manor (I-8); a game-day wait between each.\n• Flowers for Svenja (Adoulin fame 1): see Eppel-Treppel at Eastern Adoulin G-10; trade Sickles to Foret de Hennetiel Harvesting Points for key item Hennebloom Leaf; return. 1,000 bayld.\n• Do Not Go Into the Light: manor door, Door: Hospital (I-9, Logan), Borghest at Morimar frontier station; trade Chanteillie (J-10) Fire Crystal + Urunday Lumber + Damascus Ingot for key item Inventors\' Coalition Pickaxe; deliver to Door: Hospital. 1,000 bayld.\n• Hypocritical Oath: manor door, Door: Hospital, then Wegellion behind the Scouts\' Coalition (Eastern Adoulin); trade him Frost Turnip + Vial of Slime Oil; return to manor. 1,000 bayld.\n• Sick and Tired: manor door, Emjook-Renook (Yorcia Weald station), Fritha (Foret de Hennetiel station); harvest another Hennebloom Leaf (Nicked Dagger may also appear); show Fritha, return to manor. 1,000 bayld.\n• Not-So-Clean Bill: manor door, Borghest, Fritha; Foreboding Vineprints at Foret de Hennetiel J-10 (west of Bivouac #2): scene, fight Pungent Patricia (Lv99), check after; end at Door: Hospital. Rewards: Glorious Earring, 1,000 bayld, 1,000 EXP, title Good Dew-er.' }, { title = 'Mummers\' Coalition: No Laughing Matter', note = '• Peladi Shalmohr is at the Mummers\' Coalition (G-10); Mischief Marker signpost at J-11. Needs Adoulin fame 1.\n• Speak to Peladi, check the Marker, then trade it each course separately.\n• Appetizer: Fire Crystal, Popoto, Stick of Selbina Butter.\n• Main: Fire Crystal, Slice of Dhalmel Meat, Flask of Olive Oil, Pinch of Black Pepper.\n• Dessert: Fire Crystal, Stick of Selbina Butter, Faerie Apple, Pot of Maple Sugar, Stick of Cinnamon.\n• Tuffle-Buffle can spoil a course and the items are lost; carry extras.\n• Rewards: 900 EXP, title Apprentice Tarutaru Sauce Manager.' }, { title = 'All the Way to the Bank', note = '• Fame 3, game-day wait. Peladi gives key item Tarutaru Sauce Invoice.\n• Trade gil: Defliaa 19,440, Hujette 3,000, Flapano 5,600 (Western Adoulin); Bernegeois 4,560, Malgrom 6,832 (Eastern Adoulin).\n• Show the resulting Tarutaru Sauce Receipt to Peladi.\n• At the Marker choose Tuffle-Buffle\'s hats 5 times: no repeats and never the hat adjacent to the previous pick in the list.\n• If booed, buy the requested snack from a town shop and trade it to the Marker.\n• Rewards: 1,000 EXP, title Brygidesque Manager; unlocks Westerly Breeze\'s gruel trade.' }, { title = 'To Laugh Is to Love', note = '• Fame 3, game-day wait. Speak to Peladi, check the Marker.\n• Pick Qiqirn Hood, Great Cook, Lively Jig and Senroh Skewer (Malgrom, Eastern Adoulin E-8), then trade the skewer to the Marker; other combos fail and eat the food.\n• Rewards: 1,000 EXP, title The Lovelorn.' }, { title = 'A Barrel of Laughs', note = '• Game-day wait. Check the Marker, then Door: Depository beside it.\n• Rala Waterways M-6: check Entrance: Coliseum behind Yeggha Dolashi, again to fight Pupadi Dollmohr (~55,000 HP, 30-minute limit).\n• On timeout, talk to the Sauce Barrel at the pier end (by Jorin), trade the food it wants, retry.\n• Check Door: Svenja\'s Manor (I-8).\n• Sih Gates: at a Harvesting Point use /laugh (up to 5 times raises odds) then trade a Sickle for key item Guffawshroom.\n• Check Door: Hospital (I-9), the Marker, then talk to Peladi to pick an earring.\n• Rewards: 1,000 EXP, title Sauce Supreme, choice of Anastasi, Burana, Gelos or Hija Earring.\n• Swap: once per conquest week trade the earring to Peladi while holding 10,000 bayld.' }, { title = 'Amchuchu\'s vegetable quests', note = '• Start at Amchuchu\'s Laboratory, Inventors\' Coalition (J-10); game-day wait between quests.\n• Raptor Rapture (fame 1, required for Crisis): Pagnelle (G-10), Gontrain (H-12), Pagnelle; trade Sickles at Ceizak Battlegrounds Harvesting Points for 3 Rockberries (one per sickle); Pagnelle; talk to Relentless Storm or Jaroney-Baroney on the Rala Waterways E-11 bridge; Pagnelle. 1,000 bayld.\n• Revolution (fame 1): lab; Sih Gates K-8 ??? in the small round room gives Memo from Midras (beware Apex Leeches by sound, Apex Chapuli by sight, Pungent Fungus removes Sneak); Cid at Bastok Metalworks H-8 for Cid\'s Catalyst; back to the ??? for Chunk of Milky White Minerals; lab. Rewards: 12 Rarab Tails, 2,000 bayld, title Vegetable Revolutionary.\n• Evolution (fame 4, SoA mission 2-2-1+, nation rank 5+): lab; Midras at the ??? next to the Yorcia Weald I-8 Ergon Locus; lab. 12 Rarab Tails, 2,000 bayld, title Vegetable Evolutionary.\n• Crisis: lab; trade Chanteillie (J-10) Midrium Ingot, Urunday Lumber, Raaz Leather; next game day get Amchuchu\'s Missive from the lab; deliver to Cid; lab. 12 Rarab Tails, 2,000 bayld, title Inventor Extraordinaire.' }, { title = 'Vegetable Vegetable Frustration', note = '• Needs Bastok\'s Cid\'s Secret and The Usual done; carry Sabiki Rigs.\n• Lab, then Raibaht at Bastok Metalworks G-8.\n• Palborough Mines map 3 G-8 Peculiar Fissure: knock 3 times, then think. Return to Raibaht.\n• Contemplation Site at Western Adoulin docks I-5: find Midras, trade a Sabiki Rig for Packet of Midras\'s Explosives (repeat if the bomb escapes).\n• Fissure: check to place, check to ignite; Incensed Pineapple spawns, dispel its Berserk before Self-Destruct.\n• Check the fissure for Tarnished Ring and Rusty Locket; show Raibaht, give the locket to Midras, check the lab.\n• Rewards: 2,000 bayld, title Vegetable Hero, Midras\'s Helm +1.' }, { title = 'Pioneers\' Coalition quests', note = '• Scaredy-Cats (fame 1): Eamonn or Bilp at Pioneers\' Coalition (E-8); Earthen Mound in Ceizak Battlegrounds; Sih Gates E-6 Foreboding Presence: scene, fight Fomor Pioneer (~10,000 HP, high evasion, Cure IV/V), check after; return. 1,000 bayld + key item Reive Unity.\n• Western Waypoints, Ho! (fame 1): Alienor outside E-8; attune all nine waypoints: Platea Triumphus H-8, Pioneers\' Coalition E-8, Mummers\' Coalition G-10, Inventors\' Coalition J-9, Auction House F-10, Rent-a-Room H-11, Big Bridge L-9, Airship Docks H-4, Adoulin Waterfront I-5. Completes on accept if already done. 1,000 EXP, 500 bayld, 3,000 kinetic units.\n• Granddaddy Dearest (fame 3, Waypoints done, weekly per conquest): Alienor gives Tray of Adoulinian Delicacies; Anastase in Ru\'Lude Gardens G-9 gives Small Bag of Adoulinian Delicacies and names Jillia (Selbina), Zurko-Bazurko (Mhaura), Quwi Orihbhe (Rabao) or Wistful Bison (Norg); deliver, report to Anastase, then Alienor. 500 EXP, 300 bayld, 1,500 kinetic units.\n• F.A.I.L.ure Is Not an Option (fame 4, F.A.I.L. Badge from A Pioneer\'s Best (Imaginary) Friend): Clautaire (I-12); Mog Garden Mineral Vein gives key item Hunk of Bedrock; return. 1,000 EXP, 500 bayld.' }, { title = 'Rune Fencer: Quiescence (Epeolatry)', note = '• Needs Destiny\'s Device done; bring Pickaxes.\n• Gaddiux, Inventors\' Coalition J-10.\n• Yorcia Weald I-8, north of Bivouac #2 among the numbing blossoms, 21:00-3:00 Vana\'diel time: trade a Pickaxe to the ??? for Numbing Blossom Seed, another for Broken Rapier Hilt. Show Gaddiux.\n• Runje Desaali (Eastern Adoulin J-11): deposit 100 High-Purity Bayld (stacks OK) for Vial of Crimson Catalyst. Then Octavien (Eastern Adoulin I-8).\n• As RUN, Rala Waterways M-6 Entrance: Coliseum: beat Zurko-Bazurko in 15 minutes (dual wield, frequent parry, Savage Blade, Chant du Cygne; Swipe/Lunge recommended) for key item Quiescence.\n• Gaddiux gives Lexeme Blade.\n• Upgrade 1: deposit 200 Ghastly Stones, trade blade to Runic Overflow at Foret de Hennetiel K-10 (Bivouac #2): stage II.\n• Upgrade 2: 200 Verdigris Stones, 2,500 High-Purity Bayld, Yggdreant Root, Waktza Rostrum, Cehuetzi Claw; Runic Overflow at Marjami Ravine I-12 (Bivouac #2): stage III.\n• Upgrade 3: 200 Wailing Stones; Runic Overflow on the barrel at Inventors\' Coalition I-10: Epeolatry.\n• Only plain (not +1/+2) stones count. Each deposit grants a runic ring key item (deluge, luster, vision) consumed by the Overflow. Lost blade: 1,000,000 gil to Runje for one at your stage.' } } },
    { name = 'Guide: Wildskeeper Reives: Colkhab and Kumhau rewards', group = 'Server', desc = 'Server reward changes for the Colkhab (Ceizak Battlegrounds) and Kumhau (Kamihr Drifts) Wildskeeper Reives. Source: https://vanadreams.org/wiki/#guide-c_wildskeeper_reives', steps = { { title = 'Overview', note = '• Join the Reive and help kill the Naakual.\n• Any player who earned Bayld evaluation receives a Pinch of High-Purity Bayld each time Colkhab or Kumhau dies.\n• Kumhau\'s material drop is now random at 25% each: Pluton, Chunk of Beitetsu, Riftborn Boulder or Chunk of Aht Urhgan Brass.' } } },
    { name = 'Guide: Window switcher (playing more than one character)', group = 'Server', desc = 'The Vanadreams Launcher includes a switcher that raises a chosen, next or previous character window via key or controller and can restore saved window layouts. Source: https://vanadreams.org/wiki/#guide-c_window_switcher', steps = { { title = 'Turning it on', note = '• Launcher > Addons: tick Window switcher (tagged "launcher") and press Save, or tick On on its page.\n• Select it and press Switcher settings for keys, slots and layouts.\n• Launch each profile with Play; windows fill the slot list and show character names once in game.' }, { title = 'Keys', note = '• Defaults: Pause = next, Scroll Lock = previous; click a button and press a new key (Ctrl/Alt/Shift combos allowed), Esc clears.\n• Slots 1-6 can each get a direct key via Key: none on that row.\n• Keys act only while a game window is focused and are not passed to the game; tick Keys work from any window to use them elsewhere.\n• ▲ ▼ reorder slots (saved per character name); Show raises that window.' }, { title = 'Controller', note = '• Assign button combos to Pad next and Pad previous (e.g. Back + RB); choose ones unused by your in-game pad layout, since the game also reads the pad.' }, { title = 'Layouts', note = '• Position windows, enter a name, press Save windows as this layout.\n• Choose the layout and press Restore to reapply.\n• Tick Put each character in its place in the layout as it logs in for automatic placement.' }, { title = 'Good to know', note = '• With the switcher on and a game running, closing the launcher sends it to the tray (moon icon); right-click > Quit to stop. It exits on its own after all game windows close.\n• Windows started as administrator cannot be raised (row shows "administrator"); launch via Play with Run as administrator unticked.' } } },
    { name = 'Guide: Wings of the Goddess Side Quests', group = 'Server', desc = 'Assorted Wings of the Goddess side quests: past-nation errands, Scholar AF3, the pixies\' weapon augments, the Swarm, and Cait Sith\'s Walk of Echoes fights. [S] marks past zones reached via Cavernous Maws. Source: https://vanadreams.org/wiki/#guide-c_wotg_side_quests', steps = { { title = 'Overview', note = '• Some steps need a new Vana\'diel day or a zone change before the NPC updates.' }, { title = 'Healing Herbs', note = '• Check the left (north) Door: Rhinostery in Windurst Waters [S].\n• Check the same door in present Windurst Waters for key item The Healing Herb.\n• Hand it over at the [S] door.\n• Grauberg [S] H-13 ???: key item Fireblossom; bring it to the [S] door.\n• Return after the next day, then after one more day.\n• Reward: Vial of Tincture; return the returned tome at the present-day door.' }, { title = 'Beast from the East', note = '• Talk to Nichais, Southern San d\'Oria [S] L-7.\n• Check the Timeworn Altar at Grauberg [S] F-11.\n• Report to Nichais and trade him a Shell Bug (dropped by present-day Brass Quadav).\n• Check the altar again with 2 free inventory slots.\n• Rewards: title Wyrmsworn Protector, two random gems.' }, { title = 'A Jeweler\'s Lament', note = '• Trade Wahid (Bastok Markets [S] J-9) a Sunstone, Aquamarine and Jadeite; they are returned.\n• Zone, talk to Wahid again.\n• Walk into North Gustaberg [S] for a scene; check the ??? at J-4 twice for key item Unadorned Ring.\n• Give the ring to Wahid, zone, talk again.\n• Reward: Trainee Burin.' }, { title = 'The Young and the Threadless', note = '• Talk to Ponono (Windurst Waters [S] K-11) for key item Ponono\'s Charm; zone and talk again for Delicate Wool, Linen and Cotton Threads.\n• Dip wool at Knightwell (West Ronfaure), linen at Fay Spring (Grauberg [S]), cotton at Lake Tepokalipuka (East Sarutabaruta), any order.\n• Return to Ponono. Reward: Trainee Scissors.' }, { title = 'Son and Father', note = '• Needs San d\'Oria quest Father and Son.\n• Talk to Exoroche (Southern San d\'Oria [S] K-9), then Landeric fishing in Jugner Forest [S] G-5.\n• Return to Exoroche to receive the Bronze Sword (free slot needed); trade it to Exoroche, get it back.\n• Trade it to Landeric and answer, then talk to Exoroche.\n• Reward: Trainee\'s Spectacles.' }, { title = 'Her Memories: Verdure Footfalls', note = '• Windurst branch of mission Her Memories; must be enlisted with Windurst.\n• Enter Windurst Waters [S] from West Sarutabaruta [S] for a scene; talk to Miah Riyuh (H-9).\n• Check the Sealed Entrance at F-11, G-4 and J-8 in West Sarutabaruta [S], any order.\n• Report to Miah Riyuh. Reward: key item Large Memory Fragment.' }, { title = 'Seeing Blood-red (Scholar artifact 3)', note = '• Needs SCH main Lv50+, Downward Helix done plus one Vana\'diel day.\n• Talk to Erlene in The Eldieme Necropolis [S].\n• Pashhow Marshlands [S] E-11 Indescript Markings: key item Unaddressed Sealed Letter; Erlene converts it to key item Porting Magic Transcript.\n• Check the Indescript Markings in the Grauberg [S] cave to fight Ulbrecht solo in Ruhotz Silvermines (30 min, heavy caster, can use Tabula Rasa); transcript consumed on entry.\n• After the scene, report to Erlene. Retry: trade her a Sheet of Vellum.\n• Rewards: Scholar\'s Mortarboard, title Summa Cum Laude.' }, { title = 'Succor to the Sidhe (repeatable)', note = '• Trade Callisto (Grauberg [S] F-6) an unaugmented base weapon: WAR Erlking\'s Kheten, MNK Oberon\'s Knuckles, WHM Dweomer Maul, BLM Ogre Sickle, RDM Oberon\'s Rapier, THF Fane Baselard, PLD Erlking\'s Sword, DRK Dweomer Scythe, BST Erlking\'s Tabar, BRD Dweomer Knife, SAM Rindomaru, NIN Tsukumo, DRG Fay Lance, SMN Fay Crozier, BLU Erlking\'s Blade, COR Fane Hexagun, PUP Oberon\'s Sainti, DNC Ogre Jambiya, SCH Fay Staff, RNG Fay Gendawa.\n• Talk to a Watchful Pixie to trigger an ambush (Lv76-82, no drops; resets after 30 minutes):\n• East Ronfaure [S] J-7: Faytrapper Vashgash, 2 Faygorger Rams, 4 Faygorger Sheep.\n• Jugner Forest [S]: Treefeller Snogrog, Tainted Treants, Pixietraps, Sentry Saplings.\n• Vunkerl Inlet [S]: Almops, Edonus, 4 Glacial Wisps.\n• Batallia Downs [S] F-7: Gnashfang Rahskhas + 5 pets.\n• North Gustaberg [S] H-6: Stabnix Skewerfinger, 10 Pixie Impalers.\n• Grauberg [S] J-11: Ru\'Bha Stonewall, 4 Sentinel Wivres.\n• Pashhow Marshlands [S]: Go\'Rha Sludgewater, 10 Swamp Mucks.\n• Rolanberry Fields [S]: six Quadav warriors.\n• West Sarutabaruta [S] F-10: Poroggo Gourmand, 6 Poroggo\'s Toadies.\n• Meriphataud Mountains [S] I-6: Yii Haqi the Threnodist, Nuu Gazo the Dirgerimer, 2 Slate + 2 Ochre Scorpions.\n• Fort Karugo-Narugo [S]: Laa Vaqu the Sutler, 4 Pixiebanes.\n• Sauromugue Champaign [S]: Laa Heha the Falconer, 4 Cinderwings, 4 Gorebeaks.\n• Beaucedine Glacier [S] H-10: Shesha, Vasuki, Kaliya, Astika.\n• Xarcabard [S] J-8: Megalotaur, Torvotaur.\n• After the last kill, talk to the Jubilant Pixie (or the Watchful one) for 1-3 random augments: stats, HP, accuracy, attack, evasion, magic accuracy, magic attack, Fast Cast, Store TP; ranged acc/atk on Gendawa and Hexagun.\n• Reroll by trading the weapon to any Watchful or Jubilant Pixie; 5 attempts total. New weapon: trade to Callisto again.' }, { title = 'The Swarm (repeatable)', note = '• Use a Flask of Pest Repellent (seasonal events) to unlock it.\n• Talk to Fortilace, Rolanberry Fields [S] D-9; nearby party members of any size enter with you.\n• 1 minute prep (buffs removed on entry), then 5 minutes of endless spawns.\n• Points: Swarmspawn 100 (passive), Dinky 150, Fodder 200, Picayune 300; fast kills build a Swarm Chain up to x2; periodic party HP/TP boosts. AoE recommended.\n• Reward: title Swarminator regardless of score; quest clears, so another Pest Repellent restarts it.' }, { title = 'Champion of the Dawn', note = '• Needs mission A Token of Troth.\n• Enter the Walk of Echoes via a Veridical Conflux (Grauberg [S], Pashhow Marshlands [S] or Xarcabard [S]).\n• Collect three dawndrops: East Ronfaure [S] (the empty spot where Cait Sith waited), and the A Fork in the Road forks in Jugner Forest [S] and Beaucedine Glacier [S].\n• Check the Ornate Door three times (Breath of Dawn forms, challenge, enter); Breath of Dawn consumed on entry.\n• Fight Cait Sith Lv99: 15 minutes, up to 6, trusts OK, buffs and TP wiped.\n• After winning, check the door for one wish in order: Cait Sith pact, Nesanica Torque, Nesanica Belt, Nesanica Ring; owned picks roll to the next unowned; all owned = 10,000 gil.\n• Retry with any one dawndrop. Reward: title Light of Dawn plus the wish.' }, { title = 'The Dawn Also Rises (repeatable)', note = '• Once per Earth day (midnight JST reset).\n• Check the Ornate Door, collect one dawndrop from any of the three spots, check the door twice to enter, then check after winning for another wish.' }, { title = 'A Forbidden Reunion', note = '• Needs WotG missions finished (Lest We Forget), Champion of the Dawn and a trust permit.\n• Enter the Walk of Echoes via a Veridical Conflux (re-enter if you were already inside).\n• Check the Ornate Door for key item Butterfly-shaped Key, again for the scene, again to enter (key consumed).\n• Fight Gloomtalon (gallu) and Gloomscale (zilant): 30 minutes, trusts OK, buffs/TP wiped. Lilisette must survive; outsiders can heal/buff her and she fully recovers twice. Doom attacks: bring Holy Water.\n• Check the door after winning; on a loss the door gives another key.\n• Rewards: Atomos pact, title Heir of Eternity, Cipher: Lilisette if not owned.' } } },
    { name = 'Guide: XI View interface (cleaner menus and icons)', group = 'Server', desc = 'Optional fan-made widescreen UI pack (16:9/16:10 menu skins, fonts, menu and status icons) loaded through XIPivot without touching game files. Source: https://vanadreams.org/wiki/#guide-c_xi_view_interface', steps = { { title = 'Overview', note = '• Install: launcher Addons page, tick XI View interface, Install, Save; XIPivot must also be installed and ticked.\n• In game set Menu > Config > Misc > Icon Type 2 for the new status icons.\n• Disable by unticking and saving. Alongside XI-Vision maps, the pack listed higher on the Mod packs panel takes priority for shared files.\n• Based on KenshiDRK\'s XI View 2.0 (widescreen edition).' } } },
    { name = 'Guide: XI-Vision maps (redrawn zone maps)', group = 'Server', desc = 'Optional redrawn zone map pack loaded through XIPivot without touching game files. Source: https://vanadreams.org/wiki/#guide-c_xi_vision_maps', steps = { { title = 'Overview', note = '• Install: launcher Addons, tick XI-Vision maps, Install, Save; XIPivot must be installed and ticked.\n• Disable via the Addons page or the Mod packs panel, which also sets priority (higher pack wins on shared files).\n• Maps by Drauku from Caradog\'s XI-Vision; only map files are loaded, the old-client interface files are excluded since they can crash with a maximised chat window.' } } },
    { name = 'Guide: Zoning between regions', group = 'Server', desc = 'The server now splits the world across three map servers; no client or launcher changes are needed. Source: https://vanadreams.org/wiki/#guide-c_map_server_split', steps = { { title = 'Overview', note = '• Crossing to an area on another map server (e.g. Jeuno to Windurst, Whitegate to Mhaura) may take a second or two longer; let it finish instead of logging out.\n• On a black-screen zoning failure, close the game and log in again; you arrive at the destination zone.\n• Dynamis - Divergence: logging in after your run ended places you at the city\'s Dynamis exit; if unavailable, you are logged out once, then placed there on next login.' } } },
    { name = 'Guide: ★ Walk of Echoes [P] fights and ★The Orb\'s Radiance', group = 'Server', desc = 'Covers five ★ battlefields (four via Selbina\'s Veridical Conflux, one at Reisenjima Sanctorium) that run on the phantom gem system, with entry rules, per-boss mechanics and drops. Source: https://vanadreams.org/wiki/#guide-c_high_tier_summon_and_rov_fights', steps = { { title = 'Overview', note = '• Gems: Trisvain, Northern San d\'Oria; 10 merit points each; level 95+; set difficulty with him beforehand; every member needs one.\n• Rules: no level cap, max 6 players, 30-minute limit, Trusts permitted.\n• ★A Stygian Pact: Odin Prime; requires quest The Rider Cometh; Veridical Conflux, Selbina (H-7).\n• ★Champion of the Dawn: Cait Sith; requires quest Champion of the Dawn; Veridical Conflux, Selbina (H-7).\n• ★Divine Interference: Alexander; requires quest Waking the Colossus; Veridical Conflux, Selbina (H-7).\n• ★Maiden of the Dusk: Lady Lilith then Lilith Ascendant; requires WotG mission Maiden of the Dusk; Veridical Conflux, Selbina (H-7).\n• ★The Orb\'s Radiance: Cloud of Darkness; requires RoV mission The Orb\'s Radiance; Reisen Crystal, Reisenjima Sanctorium.' }, { title = 'Entering from Selbina', note = '• Party leader examines the Veridical Conflux at Selbina (H-7) and selects a fight.\n• Nearby members holding that gem go into Walk of Echoes [P]; anyone without it is left outside.\n• One party at a time; if occupied, retry later.\n• No exit inside: use the temporary Veridical Conflux Shard received on entry to leave early; otherwise you return at time-out or 6 minutes after a win (time to loot).' }, { title = '★A Stygian Pact (Odin Prime)', note = '• Geirrothr damage is divided among all targets hit: 6,000 Very Easy, +3,000 per difficulty step, 18,000 Very Difficult; extra targets (Trusts, pets) lower each share.\n• Zantetsuken Kai (Easy+): strong frontal attack.\n• Zantetsuken Go at 50% HP or lower: instant death for anyone with reduced defense (Defense Down, Berserk, Last Resort), and for anyone lacking Protect or a defense buff while Odin has Endark or an attack buff; dispel his buffs fast.\n• Very Easy: casts no magic. Difficult+: wind magic barely affects him.\n• Drops: Zantetsuken, Shin Zantetsuken, Geirrothr (rare), Hjarrandi Helm, Hjarrandi Breastplate, Gere Ring, Freke Ring.\n• Very Difficult title: Dread Purger.' }, { title = '★Champion of the Dawn (Cait Sith)', note = '• She cannot die until she uses Divine Seal late in the fight; afterward her attack speed and damage jump, so hold your best finisher for then.\n• Watch: Eerie Eye (turn away), Mewing Lullaby (sleep plus TP reset), Level ? Holy.\n• Drops: Cath Palug Hammer, Cath Palug Stone, Cath Palug Crown, Cath Palug Earring, Cath Palug Ring.\n• Very Difficult title: Sidhe Smasher.' }, { title = '★Divine Interference (Alexander)', note = '• No spellcasting.\n• Normal+: uses Divine Judgment each time he loses 10,000 HP (15,000 Difficult, 20,000 Very Difficult); burst damage triggers it more often.\n• Difficult+: Perfect Defense once at 50% HP; wait until it ends.\n• Drops: Sacro Breastplate, Sacro Gorget, Sacro Mantle, Sacro Cord, Sacro Bulwark.\n• Very Difficult title: Alexander Annihilator.' }, { title = '★Maiden of the Dusk (Lady Lilith)', note = '• Very Easy/Easy: killing Lady Lilith wins.\n• Normal+: guardians Larzos, Haudrale and Aquila join her; each one killed adds an extra equipment roll.\n• Larzos: melee and weapon skills; use magic.\n• Haudrale: red mage spells (Silence, Dispel, enfeebles); use ranged attacks.\n• Aquila: ranged black mage nukes; use melee.\n• After Lady Lilith dies, Lilith Ascendant appears with five Light Gyves; each surviving Gyve cuts her damage taken by 15%, so kill Gyves first, then her.\n• Drops: Malignance Sword, Daybreak, Malignance Pole, Malignance Earring, Malignance Box (yields one Malignance armor piece).\n• Very Difficult title: Lilith Liquidator.' }, { title = '★The Orb\'s Radiance (Cloud of Darkness)', note = '• Enter via the Reisen Crystal in Reisenjima Sanctorium (mission location); Iroha is absent and you cannot leave until the fight is over.\n• Darkness adds spawn in waves: the first special ability following Waning Vigor or Expunge summons a full wave (3 on Very Easy, more on higher settings); each later special ability adds one. Primordial Surge, Waning Vigor and Expunge summon none.\n• Drops: Null Masque, Null Loop, Null Shawl, Null Belt.\n• Very Difficult title: Eternal Master.' }, { title = 'Rewards', note = '• Each clear: Rem\'s Tale chapters 6-10 plus Reisenjima materials scaled by difficulty, as with other ★ fights.\n• ★A Stygian Pact, ★Champion of the Dawn, ★Maiden of the Dusk: one extra Rem\'s Tale (chapter 6-10, 10% each).\n• Walk of Echoes fights also drop Siren\'s Hair, Orichalcum Sheet, Durium Sheet, Twill Damask, Damascus Ingot, Behemoth Leather; ★Maiden of the Dusk adds Raxa and Platinum Silk Thread.' } } },
}

return S
